  "NPCMapLocation.DaultonsHouse": "DaultonsRoom",
  "Daulton.Display": "Daulton",
  "Maple.Display": "Maple",
 
  "Mail.Daulton.WoodGift": "Hey. I scored some decent lumber down at the docks this morning. Figured you might use it on the coop or the fence before it rots in the rain. Stay dry out there.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.SpicyEel": "Willy handed me a piping-hot plate of spicy eel this morning, already cooked and seasoned just right. Figured it’d warm you up after a long day in the fields.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.MaplesWool": "Maple’s been shedding like a maniac in the barn. Collected a fleece or two. Figure you could spin it into something. ^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.SuperCucumber": "Willy pulled in a massive cucumber at low tide, snagged a Super Cucumber for you. Keep it handy when you need that extra stamina out in the fields.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.SalmonMail": "Salmon run’s started. I caught these this morning.Thought you might like a fresh fish dinner. Hope it hits the spot after a day of chores. They’ll taste better on your plate than bobbing in my net.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.BookCrabbing": "Found this tattered copy of “The Art O’ Crabbing” behind Willy’s barrels. Thought you might get a laugh, or at least pick up a trick or two, before your next dock wander.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.EnergyTonic": "Work’s been brutal these days. Figured you could use a pick me up. Here’s an Energy Tonic. Pop it when your arms feel like lead.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.HeartEvent6": "Hey, @. Any chance you can swing by the pier after sunset? Say, around 8-ish? Been turning something over in my head and I could use a steady ear while the water’s calm.^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.HeartEvent10": "If Maple shows up with this note, don’t be alarmed. She’s on a mission. I’ve been working up the nerve to say something for weeks, and tonight’s the night. Meet me by the water in Cindersap after dark. I'll have everything ready. Just come, okay?^  -Daulton",
  "Mail.Daulton.MaplesTreatRecipe": "Hey @. Maple goes wild for these, and I thought you might like to make some for her yourself. It’s her absolute favorite. I call it Maple’s Special Treat. Trust me, show up with a few of these and she’ll be your best friend for life.^ —Daulton",


  //GREEN RAIN//
  
  "Daulton.GreenRain": "Huh, that's some weird green rain.$0#$b#Never saw anything like this back in Zuzu City. Reminds me of one of those B-grade horror movies.$1",
  "Daulton.GreenRainFinished": "That green rain was something else. Maple's been acting different since it stopped.$0#$b#Not sure what to make of it, honestly.$1",
  "Daulton.GreenRain2":  "Green rain again. This place keeps finding new ways to surprise me.$0#$b#At least it's not boring.$1",
 
  //INTRO LINES //
  "Daulton.IntroDialogue.1": "Hey there. You must be the new farmer everyone's been talking about.$0#$b#Name's Daulton. I work down at the docks with Willy.#$b#Moved here from Zuzu City a while back.$0#$b#Welcome to Pelican Town, farmer.$1#$e#$action AddConversationTopic met_Daulton 999999#$e#",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.2":"Working the docks isn't bad. Honest work, fresh air, and Willy's good company.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.3": "Maple got into my toolbox again yesterday. Found her chewing on a wrench.$1#$b#Smart bunny knows quality metal when she sees it.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.4": "I spend some time helping out the Adventurer's Guild too.$0#$b#All this dock work's got me in decent shape.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.5": "Sam and I jammed for hours last night. Bud's got real talent.$1#$b#Reminds me why I moved here from the city.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.6":  "Sandy sent me some cactus fruit from the desert. Woman's got good taste.$1#$b#Wish she lived closer so we could hang out more.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.7": "Caught Sebastian skulking around the docks earlier. Guy needs to find a hobby that doesn't involve brooding.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.8": "Gus makes a mean fish stew. Good thing, since my cooking would probably poison half the town.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.9": "Found some interesting scrap metal on the beach. Perfect for my next project.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.10": "The arcade at the Saloon reminds me of this underground place I used to go to in Zuzu.$1#$b#Different crowd here though. Way more friendly.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.11": "Maple's been digging holes in the yard again. Little bun's got engineering ambitions.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.12": "Watched this old horror flick last night. The practical effects were way better than all that digital garbage.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.13": "Been helping Willy repair some of the older equipment. There's something satisfying about bringing old things back to life.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.14": "Sam mentioned you're pretty good with a sword. Maybe we should hit the mines sometime.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.15":  "The fish here taste way better than anything you could get in Zuzu City.$1#$b#Probably helps that they're not swimming in polluted water.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.16":  "Willy's got stories that would make your hair curl. Decades of fishing wisdom packed into that old sailor.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.17":  "Sometimes I play drums just to see how many seagulls I can scare off the pier.$0#$b#Current record is twelve.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.18": "Built Maple a new feeding station yesterday. Little bun deserves the royal treatment.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.19":  "The sunset from the docks hits different than anywhere else. Makes all the hard work worth it.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.20": "The community center's got good acoustics. Wonder if they'd let me practice there sometime.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.21": "Maple's been stealing socks from my laundry again. Little kleptomaniac.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.22":  "Marlon's got some serious gear at the guild. Real professional stuff.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.23": "Sebastian walked past without his usual death glare today. Progress, I guess.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.24": "Maple ate through another charging cable. At this rate, I'll go broke buying replacements.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.25": "Emily's crystal collection is actually pretty cool.$1#$b#Don't tell her I said that.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.26": "Found some old ship parts washed up on shore. Willy says they're from a wreck decades ago.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.27":  "Been sketching designs for a better fish smoker. Willy's current setup is ancient.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.28": "Alex keeps asking about my workout routine.$0#$b#Dock work is better than any gym.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.29": "Vincent asked me to build him a robot.$0#$b#Kid's got his priorities straight.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.30": "Met Leah by the woods this morning.#$b#She’s turning that driftwood into an art show she says might be worth dropping by.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.31": "Heard there’s a rumour of sea serpents off the coast. Would be neat to catch a glimpse, though I’d rather keep my limbs intact.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.32": "I tried baking for once.#$b#Ended up burning half the kitchen. Gus still ate it, though. Hats off to him.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.33": "Caught a fish that glowed in the moonlight last night. Almost thought I was hallucinating.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.34": "Sandy’s cactus fruit tastes like candy. Wish she’d ship me more than just a handful.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.35": "Emily showed me a new crystal she found.#$b#Something about the way it catches the light had me staring for minutes.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.36": "Maple chewed through half my slippers.#$b#Little fluffball owes me a replacement pair.$5",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.37": "Maple tried to hop into my tool bucket this morning. Nearly gave me a heart attack when the whole thing tipped.$5",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.38": "Sam and I were messing around on the arcade machines again. Pretty sure the high score’s mine now, not that he’ll admit it.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.39": "Clint handed me a wrench and said, ‘No wonder people stare at you.’ I don't have grease on my face, do I?$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.40": "Ran into Abigail out by the mines. She had this look like she was hunting ghosts or something. I didn’t ask.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.41": "Harvey tried to give me a vitamin sample. I told him I get all the nutrients I need from Gus’s chili fries.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.42":  "Emily said my aura was ‘stormy but sincere.’ No idea what that means, but it sounds nice, so I’ll take it.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.43": "Had a weird dream about fishing with a giant rabbit. Woke up and found Maple curled up on my face. Explains a lot.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.44": "Sometimes I catch Clint just staring at the forge like it insulted his mother. That guy’s intensity is a lot.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.45": "Fixing up fishing nets ain’t glamorous, but there’s a rhythm to it. Like drumming, just... wetter.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.46": "There’s a gull down by the pier that’s got it out for me. I think I stepped on his seaweed stash by accident.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.47": "Marlon invited me to spar at the Guild. I agreed.#$b#Curious to see if my dock-honed reflexes hold up.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.48": "Leah’s forest paintings are amazing. I asked if she’d paint Maple next; she said only if she stays still.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.49": "Willy’s been tinkering with a sea cannon; swears it’ll catch more fish. I told him if it blows us off the pier, I’m blaming him.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.50": "Tightened mooring lines today while Maple sniffed at the saltwater air, then hopped off toward a pile of sea grass.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.51": "Robin asked if I needed extra wood.$0#$b#I collected a whole stack.#$b#Figured I’ll build Maple a hideout.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.52": "George grumbled about ‘kids these days,’ then Maple hopped onto his lap. Even he couldn’t resist that fluff.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.53": "Maple stole Leah’s sketchbook.#$b#Now every page has bite marks. I told her it’s abstract art.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.54": "I asked Robin for a custom drum stool. She built it so sturdy it feels like it could withstand an earthquake.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.55": "I tuned up my drum set today. Not for a gig or anything.#$b#Just feels nice when everything sounds right.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.56": "Sometimes I miss the noise of Zuzu City... but then I hear the wind in the trees here, and I don’t miss much after that.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.57": "Hey there. I ran into Abigail by the river.#$b#She asked how your crops are doing.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.58": "Hey. Ran into Sam in the Saloon.#$b#He’s been practicing a new riff you’d probably like.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.59": "Hey there. I repaired a hole in the net today.#$b#Willy says we’ll catch more fish now that it’s patched. Maple tried to chew the rope.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.60": "Hey, Farmer. I was just thinking about building a rack for my tools. Been tripping over my own gear lately.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.61": "Saw Marlon today. He handed me a sharpening stone and said: Just in case. I’m not sure what he thinks I’m preparing for.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.62": "How’s it going? I’ve been thinking about upgrading my bait box. Might ask Robin if she’s got spare parts lying around.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.63": "Hey. Maple's been in a mood today.#$b#Keeps thumping at the pantry door. Probably wants another carrot.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.64": "Hey, Farmer. Just got back from checking the pier. There’s something peaceful about watching the tide do its thing.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.65": "Willy and I patched up a leaky section of the pier. The sea spray made my arms ache, but it felt good to see it hold.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.66": "Worked on mending nets with Willy today.#$b#Maple hopped onto the dock and nibbled at some stray seaweed. Wonder if she thinks it’s a salad.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.67": "Emily asked if I’ve ever done yoga. I told her I stretch my arms pretty far when I reach for the bait bucket.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.68": "Checked crab pots this morning.#$b#Caught a few keepers. Maple was busy chewing on a piece of rope until I shooed her away.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.69": "Penny keeps staring at me when I’m moving barrels. I asked if something was on my shirt and she just turned red.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.70": "I sanded down one of my drumsticks too much. It kind of wobbles now.$0#$b#Might use it as a paint stirrer instead.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.71": "I saw Robin working on a new design out front. Looked complicated, but she made it seem easy.$0#$b#Kind of inspiring, actually.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.72":  "Maple knocked over a whole stack of kindling. Just sat there after, like she was proud of himself.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.73": "Hey, Farmer. You know that feeling when everything smells like fresh wood and saltwater? That’s a good day, right there.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.74": "Willy joked that I should enter a strongman contest.#$b#Said my dock work built me like a barn door. Might be from lifting Maple too many times.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.75": "Penny asked if I ever read on break. I said sometimes I read the back of bait packages. Didn’t go over well.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.76": "Maple’s been burrowing under the porch lately. I think she’s building a bunker or something. I respect it.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.77": "Sebastian muttered something about ‘shirtless lumber ads’ when I passed by. I think he’s mad I used his favorite bench?$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.78": "Emily keeps asking what color I’d paint my house. I keep saying ‘wood.’ She doesn’t like that answer.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.79": "Haley said I look ‘cinematic’ when I lean on the dock railing. Not sure what that means, but I guess it’s better than looking seasick.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.80": "Emily asked if I meditate. I told her I zone out while sanding wood sometimes. She said that counts.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.81": "Maple found a leaf shaped like a heart.$0#$b#I showed it to Marnie.#$b#She said I should press it in a book. Might do that.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.82":  "Emily handed me a new shirt.#$b#Said it shows off my... hard work. I told her I appreciate the thought.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.83": "Maple tried to hop into my toolbox again. I told her it’s not a burrow, but she seems unconvinced.$5",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.84": "Vincent gave me a drawing of me and Maple on a pirate ship. I’m not sure who’s steering, but we look very serious.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.85": "Sam joked that I’m ‘built like a barn.’ I nodded and told him I’m good with hay bales.#$b#Does that count?$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.86": "Good to see you, Farmer.$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.87": "Some folks don’t get how peaceful it is to fix something with your hands. Beats yelling at a screen, that’s for sure.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.88": "Maru asked if she could measure my arms for ‘research.’ I think she meant for science, but I didn’t ask questions.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.91": "Hey there, @. Nice day for a walk around town.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.92": "Well, if it isn't the famous farmer. How are things?$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.93": "The breeze coming off the water feels incredible today.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.94": "Sometimes I think about traveling, but then I remember how perfect it is here.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.95": "Been meaning to stop by your farm and see how you're doing. Heard it's looking great.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.96": "Willy's taught me a lot about fishing over the years. Good man.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.97": "Ran into Morris earlier. That man could make a sunrise feel like a tax form.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.98": "Sam nearly broke his amp again trying to ‘fix’ it.$0#$b#Told him hitting it doesn’t count as a tune-up.$1",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.99": "Another day in paradise.$0#$b#And I mean that less ironically than I used to.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.100": "Gus asked me to 'keep it down' upstairs. Apparently my drumming at 6 AM isn't universally appreciated.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.101": "I don't miss traffic jams, but I do miss having five pizza places within walking distance.$s",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.102": "Maple's convinced she runs the household. I'm just the guy who opens the pellet bag.$5",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.103": "My old bandmates would laugh if they saw me now. Probably wouldn't recognize me without the sleep deprivation.$h",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.89": "Hey. Sometimes survival looks weird. You good?$0",
  "Daulton.CharacterDialogue.90": "Well that’s one way to say hi. Want to throw a rock next?$5",

   //MISC LINES//

  "fishCaught_Catfish": "Willy mentioned you pulled in something impressive. He pretended not to care, but I saw the look on his face.$0",
  "fishCaught_Crimson": "The Crimsonfish? That one's a legend. Sharp-eyed and mean.#$b#Just like my old dock boss. Well done.",
  "fishCaught_Lava": "You wrangled a Lava Eel and lived to tell the tale? That thing belongs in a volcano, not a tackle box.$1",
  "fishCaught_Midnight": "Midnight Carp's a quiet catch. Moody little guy. You'd like the spot I found one.#$b#Real peaceful.$0",
  "fishCaught_Puffer": "Pufferfish are like me after a bad haircut.#$b#Round and mad. Props for not getting poked.$1",
  "fishCaught_Legend": "You caught the Legend? I thought that thing was just a story Willy told to scare off rookies.$1",
  "fishCaught_Oct": "Octopus are clever.#$b#Smarter than most folks I know, honestly. Part of me thinks you should’ve just let it go back home.$0",
  "mineArea_80": "You reached that deep in the mines? That takes guts. I’ve been down there, and it’s no place for daydreaming.$1",
  "purchasedAnimalRabbit": "Heard you got a rabbit. Good luck.#$b#Maple still bosses me around like I work for her.$0",
  "willyCrabs": "Willy’s still grumbling about those crabs, huh? I tried helping, but he nearly threw a net at me. I left him to it.$0",
  "wonEggHunt": "Congrats on the egg hunt. You’re fast.#$b#I found three and got stuck in a hedge for the rest of it.$0",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerWon.1.1": "That was your display? No kidding. I’d have voted for it, but I got distracted by the guy juggling corn.$0",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerWon.1.2": "Hey, congratulations! Your grange display was incredible. I knew you had it in you!$h",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerWon.1.3": "I'm not surprised you won. That display was something else. You've got a real eye for this stuff.$h",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerWon.1.4": "Guess all that farm sweat finally paid off, huh?$h",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost.1.1": "They wouldn’t know quality if it hit ‘em in the face. You were robbed.$s",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost.1.2": "Eh, can’t win 'em all. Next time, go heavier on the weird vegetables.$s",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost.1.3": "The competition was really stiff this year. Your display looked great though. You should be proud of what you put together.$0",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost.1.4": "Ah, better luck next year! I thought your display was solid. These contests can be pretty subjective anyway.$0",
  "wonGrange": "Great job at the fair. You earned every ribbon. That was all you.$h",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost_PurpleShorts.1.1": "Well, that’s one way to lose with style. Or get banned. Hard to say.$1",
  "Fair_Judged_PlayerLost_PurpleShorts.1.2": "I’m never going to unsee that display. Ever.$s",
  "wonIceFishing": "Hey, congrats on winning the ice fishing contest. That’s no joke.#$b#Line control on frozen water is a whole different skill.$1",
  "Spouse_MonstersInHouse.1.2":"Something just growled at me near the bookshelf. If I disappear, avenge me. And maybe clean up afterward.$0",
  "SpouseStardrop": "Didn’t know I could feel this way about anyone. Guess I figured it out the moment I saw you smile like this.$4",
  "object.old-compass.name": "Old Compass",
  "object.old-compass.description": "A rusted old compass with a foggy lens and a needle that drifts in circles.",

  "Daulton.Dating_Abigail.1.1": "So you're dating Abigail? Cool. She's always seemed pretty independent to me. Bet she keeps you on your toes.$0",
  "Daulton.Dating_Alex.1.1": "So you're with Alex now? He's a good guy once you get past all the sports talk.$1",
  "Daulton.Dating_Alex.1.2": "Alex, huh? If it works, it works. No one else benches during a thunderstorm.",
  "Daulton.Dating_Shane.1.1": "Shane? Huh. Hope he’s being decent to you.$u",
  "Daulton.Dating_Shane.1.2": "Heard you and Shane were getting close. He’s working on stuff, I get that. Just...take care of yourself too.$s",
  "Daulton.Dating_Shane.1.3": "I heard that you and Shane might have something. If he’s cleaning up his act for you, then I’ve got nothing to say.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Penny.1": "Word is you're with Penny now. She's got more patience than anyone I know. Those kids adore her.$0",
  "Daulton.Dating_Maru.1.1": "Maru’s smart. Probably builds you gadgets just for fun.$h",
  "Daulton.Dating_Maru.1.2": "I'm glad you and Maru found each other. Just don’t try to keep up with her brain. You’ll pull something.$s",
  "Daulton.Dating_Maru.1.3": "You made a good call with Maru. If she’s got your back, you’re in good hands. Literally.#$b#She’s probably made a robot for it.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Elliott.1.1": "Heard you and Elliott are dating. He’s a good guy...just be patient with the theatrics.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Elliott.1.2": "Elliott tells me he’s writing again. Says it’s because of you. That’s a good sign.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Sam.1.1": "Sam’s been talking about you nonstop. He acts cool, but you’ve got him twisted in the best way.$h",
  "Daulton.Dating_Sam.1.2": "So you and Sam, huh? He’s been different lately. Lighter. I think that’s you.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Sam.1.3": "He tells me everything, you know. But when it comes to you...he just smiles.$h",
  "Daulton.Dating_Leah.1.1": "You and Leah seem good together. It suits her.#$b#The way she lights up around you.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Leah.1.2": "I'm not the type to get involved in someone else’s love life...but I think Leah made a good call this time.$h",
  "Daulton.Dating_Leah.1.3": "You and Leah, huh? She deserves someone kind. I think she found that in you.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Emily.1.1": "So, you and Emily, huh? That explains the sudden increase in glitter and spontaneous dance energy.$h",
  "Daulton.Dating_Emily.1.2": "You and Emily, huh? I respect it. I wouldn’t survive it, but I respect it.$l",
  "Daulton.Dating_Sebastian.1": "You got through to Sebastian? Impressive. Just don’t vanish on him.#$b#He’s used to that.$s",
  "Daulton.Dating_Haley.1.1": "You’re with Haley? Alright. She’s mellowed out a bit lately. Might be your influence.",
  "Daulton.Dating_Haley.1.2":"Word is you're dating Haley. She's got high standards, so that's gotta be flattering, right?$0",
  "Daulton.Dating_Harvey.1.1": "So you're dating Harvey? He's got a good heart. Worries about everyone in town like they're family.$0",

  "object.maple-treat.name": "Maple's Special Treat",
  "object.maple-treat.description": "A petite carrot-cake hay biscuit, baked especially for Maple.",
  "recipe.maple-treat.name": "Maple's Special Treat",

  //REJECION LINES//
  "Daulton.Rejection.1": "Dancing? Nah, not really my thing.$0#$b#I'm more of a 'watch from the sidelines with a drink' kind of guy.$1",
  "Daulton.Rejection.2": "Dance? Wth you?$0#$b#Nah.$0",
  "Daulton.Divorce.1": "You made me believe I was safe. That’s on me, isn’t it?$2",
  "Daulton.Divorce.2":  "Tell me, did it ever feel real? Or was I just a quiet place to rest until you got bored?$2",
  "Daulton.Makeup.1":"Hey...I've been thinking about what happened.$2#$b#Maybe we both said things we didn't mean. Want to try again?$0",
  "Daulton.Hated.1": "We don't have anything to talk about, @.$0#$b#You made your choice. Now live with it.$2",
  "Daulton.Breakup.1":  "Yeah, I felt it too. Things haven't been the same between us lately.$2#$b#Better to be honest about it than pretend everything's fine.$2",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.1": "Keep it. I don't want any reminders of what we used to have.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.2": "I...no. I can't take gifts from you. Not after everything.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.3": "I appreciate the thought, but I need you to respect the boundaries we have now.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.4": "No, @. Gifts won't fix what happened between us.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.5": "Please. Don't make this harder than it already is.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.6": "Those days are over. Keep your gifts.$s",
  "RejectGift_Divorced.1.7": "I need you to stop trying to act like we're still close.$s",

  // FUN LEAVE AND RETURN LINES//
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.1": "Gonna go fishing down by the river.$0#$b#Catch you when I get back.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.2": "Sam wants to hang out and jam a bit.$0#$b#Won't be too late.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.3": "Taking Maple out for some fresh air.$0#$b#She's been cooped up all morning.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.4": "Willy asked me to stop by the docks.$0#$b#Probably wants to show me some new knot or something.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.5": "Heading to the Saloon to grab some food.$0#$b#Want anything while I'm out?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.6": "Taking Maple to visit the other animals.$0#$b#She likes making friends.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.7": "Checking out the arcade's new game.$0#$b#Gus mentioned they got something good.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.8": "Maple's getting restless.$0#$b#Time for her daily adventure.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.9": "Heading out to test this fishing lure I made.$0#$b#See if it actually works.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.10": "Going to grab a soda and people-watch.$0#$b#Simple pleasures, you know?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.11": "Sam's got some new music to show me.$0#$b#Probably terrible, but I'll listen anyway.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.12": "Maple needs some exercise.$0#$b#Thought we'd explore the forest a bit.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.13": "Sam's convinced he found the perfect metal album.$0#$b#I'll bring it home if it's actually decent, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.14": "Heading to the river with my tackle box.$0#$b#Fish should be biting around this time.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.15": "Gonna mess around with some boat parts down at Willy's.$0#$b#I'll be back before dinner, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.16": "Gonna practice drums somewhere the neighbors won't complain.$0#$b#See you tonight, beautiful.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.17": "Taking Maple to socialize with the other farm animals.$0#$b#She gets lonely being the only bunny around.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.18": "Testing out this fishing spot Sam told me about.$0#$b#If it's good, maybe we can go together sometime.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.19": "Going to tinker with that old motorcycle engine I found.$0#$b#Don't worry babe, I'll keep all my fingers attached.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.20": "Gonna grab us some decent takeout from Gus.$0#$b#What do you want me to bring home, sweetheart?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.21": "Heading out for a bit.#$b#Might fish, might jam, might just end up lying in the sun. I’ll be thinking about you either way.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funLeave.22": "Going to help Willy with some boat maintenance.$0#$b#I'll be back for dinner, sweetheart.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.1": "Hey babe, I'm back.$0#$b#Missed you while I was out.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.2": "Back from fishing.$0#$b#Didn't catch much, but it was peaceful.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.3": "Just got back from jamming with Sam.$1#$b#My ears are still ringing a bit.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.4": "Maple and I had a good walk.$0#$b#She's exhausted now.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.5": "Willy had me fixing nets most of the afternoon.$0#$b#Honest work, but my hands are shot.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.6": "Beat Abigail at the arcade finally.$1#$b#She's demanding a rematch tomorrow.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.7": "Back from the pier.$1#$b#Always feels good to come home to you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.8": "Maple made friends with the chickens.$0#$b#She's napping now after all that socializing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.9": "Maple wore herself out chasing butterflies.$0#$b#She's out cold on her favorite blanket now.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.10": "Got some good practice in, but kept losing focus.$0#$b#Hard to concentrate when all I want is to get back to you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.11": "Sandy's doing well, but she spent half the time asking about you.$1#$b#Says I light up every time I mention your name.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.12": "That horror game was decent, but I kept wishing you were there.$1#$b#Everything's better when you're around to share it.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.13": "That walk helped me think about how lucky I am.$4#$b#Not everyone gets to come home to their best friend and soulmate.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.14": "Watching the waves made me think about us.$4#$b#How we just fit together perfectly, you know?",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.15":  "Maple had fun, butshe kept looking around for you.$0#$b#Smart bunny knows you're the best part of this family.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.16": "Grabbed us dinner from Gus since I'm hopeless in the kitchen.$1#$b#You deserve better than my cooking disasters anyway, beautiful.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.17": "Sandy stopped by and we caught up for hours.$0#$b#She says I'm a different person since I married you...in the best way.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.18": "Helped Willy organize the tackle shop today.$0#$b#He keeps saying how marriage suits me...guess love shows, huh?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.19": "Took a long walk through the forest with Maple.$0#$b#Beautiful scenery, but it's got nothing on the view when I walk through our door.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.20": "Maple got into the garden and made a mess.$0#$b#Can't stay mad at her though...she gets that mischievous streak from living with us.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.21": "Watched the sunset from the pier tonight.$1#$b#Beautiful, but not nearly as breathtaking as seeing you again.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.22":  "Helped move some heavy equipment at the docks.$0#$b#Hard work, but knowing I'm coming home to you makes everything worth it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.funReturn.23": "Spent time organizing my workshop today.$0#$b#Amazing how having someone who cares makes you want to be more organized.$1",

 // SEASONAL //  
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.1.1": "First day of spring, huh?$1#$b#New season, new possibilities. Glad I get to share them all with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.1.2": "First day of spring means Willy's gonna have me hauling twice as much gear.$0#$b#Good thing I've got something beautiful to come home to.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.1.3": "First day of spring and I'm waking up next to my favorite person.$l#$b#Maple's been extra energetic this morning too. I think she's as excited about the season change as we are.$h#$b#What do you say we make this a good one?",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.1.1": "Spring nights like this make me feel grateful.$1#$b#For this place, this life, and especially for you.$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.1.2": "Been messing around with my drum setup tonight. Spring always gets my creative juices flowing.$1#$b#Don't worry, I'll keep it quiet...but maybe tomorrow we could hit the saloon?$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.1.3": "Maple's already claimed her spot on the couch if you want to join us.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.2.1": "Willy's got me helping with some boat maintenance today.$0#$b#Spring means more fishing boats heading out.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.2.2": "Morning, gorgeous.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.2.3": "Woke up early and caught Maple trying to 'help' organize my toolbox.$5#$b#Little bun had washers scattered everywhere.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.2.1": "Worked hard today, but coming home to you makes it all worth it.$1#$b#You're the best part of any season.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.2.2": "I love how spring makes everything feel fresh and new.$h#$b#Reminds me of when I first moved here from the city. Everything was an adventure...still is, with you around.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.2.3": "Maple's claimed the best spot on the couch again.$1#$b#Smart bunny. Spring nights are perfect for claiming cozy spots and good company. Mind if I claim the spot next to you?$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.3.1": "Maple's been extra energetic with the warmer weather.$1#$b#Spring fever affects bunnies too, apparently.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.3.2": "First warm day in a while. Perfect for some fishing down by the docks.$h#$b#Willy mentioned the fish are more active this time of year. Want to come along and watch a master at work?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.3.3": "Maple's been extra bouncy this morning. I think she's trying to tell us something about the season.$h#$b#Either that or she's plotting world domination again. With her, you never know.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.3.1": "Love these mild spring evenings.$0#$b#Perfect weather for sitting close with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.3.2": "Three things I'm grateful for today: spring sunshine, my workshop, and waking up next to you.$l#$b#Though Maple's demanding to be added to that list. Fair enough, buddy.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.3.3": "You know what I missed about city life? The late-night food options.$1#$b#But what I don't miss? Everything else. This quiet evening with you beats any city nightlife.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.4.1": "Spring rain means good fishing later.$0#$b#Want to come with me sometime this season?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.4.2": "Maple knocked over my coffee cup this morning. Little troublemaker.$1#$b#But looking at you right now ... I can't stay annoyed at anything. Spring's got me in too good a mood.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.4.3": "Sam challenged me to a 'who can eat more salmonberries' contest yesterday.$1#$b#I won, but at what cost? My stomach still thinks I've betrayed it. Victory tastes like regret.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.4.1": "Been thinking about starting a new project this spring.$0#$b#Maybe something useful for the farm.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.4.2": "Built a automatic bunny feeder for Maple. It works too well.$1#$b#She's figured out how to game the system and now gets triple rations. I've been outsmarted by my own pet again.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.4.3": "You know what's weird? I actually miss the sound of the harbor bells sometimes.$0#$b#Not enough to go back, but...it's funny what sticks with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.5.1": "Spring cleaning time, I guess.$0#$b#My workshop could definitely use some organization.$0",
   "Daulton.Marriage.spring.5.2":"Willy mentioned the fish are starting to run again.$0#$b#Perfect excuse to test out that lure I've been messing with. Want to come watch me probably lose it to a tree branch?$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.spring.5.3":"Morning, gorgeous. Found Maple trying to reorganize my tackle box again.$1#$b#Little bun's got opinions about my fishing setup, apparently.$h",
   "Daulton.Marriage.spring.5.4":"I was thinking of heading down to the docks later to help Willy with some equipment repairs. Want to come watch me work?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.5.1": "Spring makes everything feel fresh and new.$1#$b#Kind of like how I feel every day with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.5.2":  "You know what I love about this place? I can actually hear myself think.$0#$b#Back in Zuzu, the only quiet I got was when Maple fell asleep on my drums.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.5.3": "Sandy sent another letter asking when we're visiting the desert.$1#$b#She keeps threatening to mail me more glittery postcards until I show up.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.6.1": "Love how the seasons change, but some things stay perfect.$1#$b#Like us.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.6.2": "Maple knocked over my coffee this morning chasing a dust mote.$1#$b#I'd be annoyed, but watching her bounce around like a maniac was worth the cleanup.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.6.3": "Been working on this drum pattern that's been stuck in my head all day.$1#$b#Want to hear it? Fair warning: Maple's my only critic so far, and she just thumps along.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.6.1": "Perfect night for stargazing.$1#$b#Though I'd rather look at you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.6.2": "Maple's been extra cuddly tonight.$1#$b#Guess she knows spring's got us all feeling a little more affectionate.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.6.3": "Perfect night for a horror movie and terrible snacks from the Saloon.$h#$b#I grabbed some of Gus's 'mystery sandwiches.' They're either amazing or deadly.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.7.1": "Another beautiful spring day done.$1#$b#Every season's better when I get to share it with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.7.2": "Thinking about hitting the arcade later if you're up for it.$1#$b#That new fighting game's been calling my name all week.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.7.3": "Been tinkering with that old radio again.$0#$b#Good news: it makes sounds. Bad news: they're not music sounds. Progress?$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.7.1": "Spring nights like this are made for being close.$1#$b#Good thing I married my favorite person.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.7.2": "Sam stopped by with some new tracks he wants me to listen to.$0#$b#Kid's got enthusiasm, I'll give him that. Taste in music is... debatable.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.7.3": "Willy told me the wildest fishing story today.$0#$b#Either that man's lived ten lifetimes or he's got the best imagination in the valley.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.8.1": "Found some interesting metal scraps washed up by the docks.$0#$b#Spring storms bring all kinds of treasures to shore.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.8.2": "Been watching you work from the kitchen window.$4#$b#The way you handle those animals... there's something incredibly attractive about competence, you know?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.8.3": "Your chickens were having a full-blown argument this morning.$0#$b#I tried to mediate, but apparently my negotiation skills don't work on poultry.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.8.1": "Maple's been stealing my socks again.$0#$b#Spring energy's got her acting up...but she's still adorable.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.8.2": "Saw Elliott wandering around the beach at sunrise again.$1#$b#Guy's either deeply artistic or deeply troubled. Hard to tell the difference sometimes.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.8.3": "Harvey stopped by yesterday asking about 'workplace safety at the docks.'$0#$b#I think he's running out of people to worry about.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.9.1": "The fish are biting better now that the water's warming up.$1#$b#Makes me want to spend more lazy afternoons by the river with you.$1", 
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.9.2": "Caught Maple teaching your goats her 'innocent face' technique.$1#$b#They're fast learners. We might be in trouble.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.9.3": "Perfect morning for watching my gorgeous spouse make this whole valley look better.$4#$b#Seriously, how did I get this lucky?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.9.1": "Maple's been sleeping better with the warmer weather.$1#$b#Guess we're all more content when spring rolls around.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.9.2": "Caroline tried to give me gardening advice again.$0#$b#I nodded politely, but we both know I kill cacti. Some talents can't be taught.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.9.3": "Lewis asked if I'd help organize some community event.$0#$b#I suggested a 'mind your own business' workshop. He didn't laugh.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.10.1": "Sandy sent a letter saying she might visit this spring.$0#$b#Can't wait for her to see how happy you make me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.10.2": "Been thinking about that smile you gave me over breakfast.$4#$b#It's gonna keep me distracted at the docks all day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.10.3": "Woke up to you humming in the kitchen.$l#$b#Best alarm clock in the world, hands down.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.10.1": "Spring evenings like this remind me why I left the city.$1#$b#Well, that and meeting the love of my life here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.10.2": "Penny was reading to the kids by the river yesterday.$1#$b#That woman's got patience I can't even imagine. Takes a special person.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.10.3": "Your animals are spoiled rotten, you know that?$h#$b#I saw that cow giving me attitude this morning. She knows she's living the good life.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.10.4": "Marnie complimented your animal care again yesterday.$1#$b#Said she's never seen livestock look healthier. Makes me proud, watching you excel at everything.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.11.1": "Perfect weather for working on that boat repair with Willy.$0#$b#Spring's got me motivated to actually finish projects.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.11.2": "Your goats have formed some kind of alliance with Maple.$h#$b#I caught them planning something behind the barn. Should I be worried?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.11.3": "Evelyn invited us over for cookies again.$1#$b#That woman's heart is as sweet as her baking. We're lucky to have neighbors like her.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.11.4": "Moring, beauitful. I found this while tinkering last night.$h#$b#Figured you could use it more than I can. Always handy to have around.[787]",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.11.1": "Sam played me this new song, but it reminded me of you.$1#$b#Everything good in the world somehow leads back to you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.11.2": "Been thinking about you all day while hauling nets.$4#$b#Willy caught me grinning like an idiot at a particularly stubborn crab trap.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.11.3": "Your cows were serenading me while I fixed the fence.$0#$b#Either they like my work, or they were complaining about the noise. Hard to tell with cows.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.12.1": "Egg Festival tomorrow.$0#$b#Think Maple would be good at finding eggs, or would she just eat them?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.12.2": "Your chickens have officially adopted Maple as their mascot.$h#$b#She struts around the coop like she owns the place. They seem to approve.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.12.3": "Your sheep have started following Maple around the pasture.$h#$b#She's either their leader now or they think she's a very small, weird sheep.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.12.4": "Took me three tries to smelt this properly. Worth every attempt.$h#$b#Iridium bars are rare. Just like you.[337]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.12.1": "Festival tomorrow should be fun.$1#$b#Especially since I get to spend it with my favorite person.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.12.2": "Perfect night for holding you close and forgetting the rest of the world exists.$l#$b#Come here, beautiful. I need to recharge after a day without you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.12.3": "Linus waved at me from his tent today.$1#$b#Good guy. Lives life on his own terms. Can't help but respect that.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.13.1":  "Festival today should be fun.$1#$b#Especially since I get to spend it with my favorite person.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.13.2": "Egg Festival today.$0#$b#Never thought I'd get excited about competitive egg hunting, but here we are.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.13.3": "Egg Festival's today. You ready to show this town how it's done?$1#$b#I'll be cheering you on from the sidelines. Go get 'em, beautiful.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.13.4": "Your chickens have been acting suspicious all morning.$h#$b#I think they know something's up with all this egg talk.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.13.1": "That Egg Festival was pretty entertaining.$1#$b#Though watching you enjoy yourself was the best part.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.13.2": "Perfect evening for showing my incredible spouse how much they mean to me.$4#$b#Hope you're ready for some serious attention, gorgeous.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.13.3": "Festival wore me out more than a full day at the docks.$1#$b#But seeing you enjoy yourself made every minute worth it, babe.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.14.1": "Maple's been extra playful with the warmer weather.$1#$b#Spring energy affects us all, I guess.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.14.2": "Coffee's already brewing.$0#$b#Figured you'd need it after I heard you mumbling about crop rotations in your sleep.[395]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.14.3": "Maple's been sitting by your pillow for ten minutes.$0#$b#Think she's trying to telepathically convince you to give her breakfast.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.14.1": "Spring evenings are perfect for sitting on the porch.$1#$b#Even better when you're here to share them with.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.14.2": "Been working on something special for you in my workshop.$1#$b#Can't tell you what yet, but...let's just say I'm better with tools than words.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.14.3": "Willie asked if marriage had 'softened me up.'$1#$b#I told him love made me stronger, not softer. He just grunted and walked away.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.15.1": "Planned out some good fishing spots for us to try.$1#$b#Everything's more fun when we do it together.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.15.2": "Morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Sun's hitting your face just right. Makes me want to skip work and just watch you exist.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.15.3": "You steal the covers, talk in your sleep, and somehow still look perfect in the morning.$1#$b#How is that fair?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.15.1": "Learning so much from Willy these days.$1#$b#Feels good to have mentors and someone amazing to come home to.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.15.2": "Shane actually smiled at me today.$1#$b#Small miracle. Guy's been through hell, but he's fighting his way back. Good for him.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.15.3": "You know what the best part of my day is?$1#$b#Right now. Coming home to you, tired and happy and exactly where I belong.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.16.1": "Can't wait for Sandy to visit and see how happy we are.$1#$b#Though I think it's pretty obvious how much you mean to me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.16.2": "Found Maple in your shoe again.$0#$b#Little bun's got attachment issues. Can't blame her though.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.16.3": "Sun's barely up and the chickens are already squawking. But seeing you makes it feel worth it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.16.4": "Woke up early and watched the fog roll in over the hills. Peaceful morning.#$b#Brought you a Leek. Thought you might do something with it better than I could.[20]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.16.1": "Found Maple asleep in your gardening basket earlier.$1#$b#She's got the right idea...everything's better when it smells like you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.16.2": "Maple's already claimed her spot on the bed.$0#$b#Gonna have to negotiate for space with a bunny again.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.16.3": "Been thinking about you all day while sorting nets.$4#$b#Willy caught me grinning like an idiot. Told him I married way above my league.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.17.1": "Love how organized and focused you are in the mornings.$1#$b#Your drive and ambition are incredibly attractive.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.17.2": "Caught you stretching like a cat again.$1#$b#One of these days I'm gonna miss work just watching you wake up properly.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.17.3": "Maple brought you a sock as a morning offering.$0#$b#Pretty sure it's mine, but she means well.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.17.1": "Sam dragged me to look at some new amplifiers in town.$0#$b#Kid's got expensive taste, but terrible timing with money.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.17.2": "Come here.$4#$b#Long day, and I need to remember what happiness feels like. You're pretty good at reminding me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.17.3": "Been working with my hands all day, but the only thing I want to touch is you.$4#$b#Come here, sweetheart. Let me show you what I mean.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.18.1": "The way you tackle every morning with determination.$1#$b#You're the strongest person I know, and somehow you're mine.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.18.2": "Morning, sunshine.$1#$b#And before you say anything about your hair, you look perfect.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.18.3": "You mumbled something about 'evil turnips' around 3 AM.$0#$b#Want to talk about it, or should I just avoid the crops today?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.18.1": "Finally got that drum piece figured out.$1#$b#Want to hear it? It's dedicated to you, obviously.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.18.2": "Spent the whole day looking forward to this moment.$4#$b#You, me, Maple judging us from her corner. Perfect evening.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.18.3": "Been thinking about that smile you gave me this morning.$4#$b#Carried me through eight hours of untangling nets and Willy's lectures.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.19.1": "Been thinking about this morning when you smiled at me over coffee.$1#$b#That smile could power the whole town.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.19.2":"Your side of the bed's always warm.$1#$b#Like having a personal heater that occasionally steals blankets and looks incredible.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.19.3":"Willy's gonna ask why I'm late again.$0#$b#Gonna tell him my spouse is too beautiful to leave. He'll understand.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.19.1": "Spring nights like this remind me why I left the city.$1#$b#Peace, quiet, and the most amazing person in the world beside me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.19.2": "You know what I love about coming home?$1#$b#The way your whole face lights up when you see me. Makes every day worth it.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.19.3": "Maple fell asleep in my toolbox again.$0#$b#Found her curled up next to the wrench you gave me. Good taste, little bunny.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.20.1": "Good morning, love.$1#$b#Spring mornings with you are better than any dream I could have.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.20.2": "Love how you hum while doing dishes.$1#$b#Better than any music I could make. Though don't tell my drums I said that.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.20.3": "Woke up to Maple pawing at my face.#$b#Figure she knew I’d overslept.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.20.1": "Avoided Sebastian's brooding session at the lake today.$0#$b#Why waste time on negativity when I come home to pure sunshine?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.20.2": "Home. Finally.$1#$b#Day's not real until I walk through that door and see your face, sweetheart.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.20.3": "You've got sawdust in your hair from the coop repairs.$0#$b#Looks good on you. Everything looks good on you. It's ridiculous.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.20.4": "Maple and I took the long way home through the forest. Fireflies were out.#$b#Felt like magic.#$b#Found a Morel near the old stump. Thought you might want it.[257]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.21.1": "Morning, beautiful. Sun’s just peeking over the hills... I almost didn’t want to wake you. $4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.21.2": "Maple's been plotting something all morning.$0#$b#She's got that look. Last time she looked like that, she reorganized my sock drawer.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.21.3": "Morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Sun's not even fully up and you're already making my day better just by existing.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.21.1": "Flower Dance is coming up soon.$0#$b#Think we should practice our moves, or just wing it?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.21.2": "Love how you light up when I walk in.$1#$b#Makes every minute away from you feel worth it when I get that welcome home.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.21.3": "Caught myself humming while fixing nets today.$1#$b#Willy asked if I was feeling alright. Told him I was feeling married. He grunted approvingly.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.21.4": "You should’ve seen Maple chase a butterfly this morning. Pure chaos.#$b#Found this Wild Horseradish while trying to catch her. Figured you might like it.[16]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.22.1": "Started my day watching you get ready for farm work.$1#$b#Even in work clothes, you take my breath away.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.22.2": "Morning, sunshine.$1#$b#Coffee's ready, Maple's fed, and I've got about ten minutes to stare at you before work.[395]$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.22.3": "Maple brought you a carrot as a wake-up gift.$0#$b#It's slightly chewed, but the thought counts. She's learning romance from me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.22.1": "Your compassion for everyone in town amazes me.$1#$b#I fall for you more every day, you know that?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.22.2": "Maple knocked over my coffee cup trying to get to you earlier.$0#$b#Can't blame her. I'd probably do the same if I was small and furry.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.22.3": "Been thinking about your smile while untangling fishing line for three hours.$4#$b#Made the time pass faster. Also made Willy question my sanity, but worth it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.22.4": "Hey, love. The trees are humming today.#$b#I picked you a Daffodil on my way back from town. Bright little thing. Reminded me of you.[18]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.23.1": "Good morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Waking up next to you never gets old.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.23.2": "The sunrise hit the water at an odd angle this morning.#$b#Reminded me of the first time I saw you on the pier.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.23.3": "Morning, sweetheart. I see you're wearing my old flannel again.$1#$b#Looks better on you than it ever did on me. Keep it. I've got others.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.23.1": "You make this whole town brighter just by being in it.$1#$b#And somehow I'm the one who gets to come home to you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.23.2": "Come here.$4#$b#Long day, and I need to remember what the good parts of life feel like. You're pretty much all of them.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.23.3": "Perfect timing. I was just about to come find you.$1#$b#Needed to see that face that makes everything else make sense.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.23.4": "Maple found this out in the field and refused to drop it until I promised I’d give it to you.#$b#So here.#$b#One slightly slobbered-on Sweet Pea. Bunny-approved.[595]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.24.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#The way the morning light hits you...you're absolutely stunning.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.24.2": "Willy asked if I've gone soft since getting married.$0#$b#Told him yeah, and it's the best thing that ever happened to me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.24.3": "Lewis asked me to move the festival decorations again.$0#$b#Third time this month. Apparently I'm the town's unofficial heavy lifting service now.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.24.1": "Perfect spring evening to just sit here and admire you.$1#$b#Still can't believe someone as incredible as you chose me.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.24.2": "Krobus waved at me from the sewers again.$0#$b#Starting to think he's just lonely down there. Can't blame him.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.24.3": "Gunther mentioned you donated something interesting recently.$0#$b#Wouldn't tell me what. Now I'm curious what ancient junk you've been hoarding.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.25.1": "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#The way you stretch when you wake up is the cutest thing I've ever seen.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.25.2": "Evelyn flagged me down to open a pickle jar yesterday.$0#$b#Sweet old lady, but I'm starting to think she saves all the stubborn ones for me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.25.3": "Robin wants me to help her carry lumber later today.$0#$b#Said Demetrius 'tried his best' but couldn't manage the weight. Poor guy.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.25.1": "Love watching you plan out the farm strategies.$1#$b#Your mind is as beautiful as everything else about you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.25.2": "Linus offered me some wild mushroom tea today.$0#$b#Politely declined. Guy's tough, but I'm not ready for that level of adventure.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.25.3": "Caroline offered me homegrown tea samples again.$0#$b#Accepted one to be polite. Still tastes like lawn clippings, but don't tell her.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.25.4": "Maple dragged me halfway across the farm chasing a bee.#$b#Figured I’d bring you the Honey she was after. Seemed fair.[340]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.26.1": "Still thinking about how beautiful you looked in the morning light.$1#$b#I'm the luckiest guy in the valley, no question.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.26.2": "Clint asked if I could move his new anvil into position later today.$0#$b#Thing weighs more than a small car, but sure. Add it to the list.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.26.3": "Gus needs help rearranging the Saloon furniture again later today.$0#$b#Man redesigns that place monthly. Good thing I don't mind the workout.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.26.1":  "Willy mentioned how impressed he is with your farming skills.$0#$b#Told him I married the most capable person in Pelican Town.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.26.2": "Marnie asked me to stack fifty hay bales today.$0#$b#Shane tried to help for about ten minutes, then mysteriously needed a break. Shocking.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.26.3": "Pierre needed his delivery truck unloaded.$0#$b#Apparently the usual delivery guy took one look and said 'nope.' Can't blame him.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.27.1": "Good morning, beautiful.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.27.2": "Tried to tune my drums quietly this morning.$0#$b#Maple woke up anyway and started thumping along. Worst backup drummer ever.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.27.3": "Maple's been sitting on your pillow for twenty minutes.$0#$b#Think she's trying to absorb your farming wisdom through osmosis.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.27.4": "Hey. I had a dream you were surrounded by wildflowers.#$b#Woke up and picked you a Tulip. Might not mean much, but it’s from me.[591]$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.27.1": "Ready for whatever the next season brings.$1#$b#As long as you're with me, I'm good with anything.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.27.2":"Maple got her head stuck in a flower pot again.$0#$b#Third time this month. You'd think she'd learn, but no. Stubborn little bunny.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.27.3": "Last spring night, huh? Kinda want to bottle up the smell of the flowers and keep it for a rainy day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.27.4": "You hear those frogs down by the water? Funny little guys.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.27.5": "Maple’s been hopping through the tall grass like she owns it. Gonna miss that green glow the nights have had.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.28.1": "End of spring already.$0#$b#Time flies when you're living your best life with someone amazing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.28.2": "You mumbled something about 'defiant turnips' in your sleep.$0#$b#Want to tell me what vegetables did to offend you this time?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.28.3": "Found you wearing my work shirt as pajamas again.$0#$b#Keep it. Looks better as sleepwear than it ever did as workwear.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.28.1": "Another spring season done.$1#$b#Can't wait to see what summer brings for us.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.28.2": "Last night of spring.$0#$b#Tomorrow everything gets twice as hot and Maple gets twice as lazy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spring.night.28.3": "Your strawberries came out perfect this year.$1#$b#Already planning summer crops, aren't you? I can see those wheels turning.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.1.1": "First day of summer.$1#$b#Hot weather means more time by the water...want to join me later?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.1.2": "Your tomatoes are gonna love this heat.$0#$b#Unlike me. I'll be hiding in the workshop by noon.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.1.3": "You look good in summer light.$4#$b#I mean, you look good in any light. But there's something about morning sun that suits you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.1.1": "Even when you're covered in dirt from farming, you're gorgeous.$1#$b#How did I get so lucky to call you mine?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.1.2": "Summer means three months of you in tank tops.$4#$b#Not complaining. Just saying the season has its perks.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.1.3": "Finally cooling off.$0#$b#Best part of summer evenings is getting to hold you without melting.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.2.1": "Summer heat's making Maple extra lazy today.$0#$b#Can't blame her, it's pretty intense out there.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.2.2": "You're already planning which crops need extra water today.$0#$b#I love watching your brain work. Even at six AM, you're three steps ahead of everything.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.2.3": "Summer sunrise hits different when you've got someone worth waking up for.$4#$b#Used to hate mornings. Now they're the best part of my day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.2.4": "Good morning. You could hear the crickets all night, huh?#$b#Brought you a Sunflower.#$b#Felt right for a morning like this.[421]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.2.1": "Cooled off nicely this evening.$1#$b#Perfect temperature for sitting close with you on the porch.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.2.2": "Love how you look after a day in the summer heat.$4#$b#Tired, satisfied, beautiful. Best combination in the world.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.2.3": "Maple's been hiding under the porch all day.$0#$b#Can't blame her. Smart enough to know when to avoid the sun.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.2.4": "Evening, babe. I stayed out a little later than usual, just listening to the tide roll in.#$b#Found this Coral while I was at it. Thought you'd like the color.[393]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.3.1": "Willy's got me working early mornings to beat the heat.$0#$b#Worth it though, means more evening time with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.3.2": "You laugh in your sleep sometimes.$1#$b#Woke up to it this morning. Whatever you were dreaming about, I hope it was good.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.3.3": "You stretch like a cat when you wake up.$1#$b#Cutest thing I've ever seen. Makes my whole day better.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.3.1": "Love these warm summer nights.$1#$b#Everything feels more relaxed, especially with you here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.3.2": "Heat's got everyone moving slower today.$0#$b#Except you. You just keep being incredible no matter what the weather does.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.3.3": "Long summer days mean more time to appreciate how incredible you are.$4#$b#Silver lining to sweating through my shirt for twelve hours.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.3.4": "Evening, babe. I passed the grove on the way back and caught the scent of citrus on the breeze.#$b#Picked you an Orange before the birds could get to it. Bright little thing, isn't it?[634]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.4.1": "Summer fishing is completely different than spring.$0#$b#Willy's teaching me all the seasonal tricks.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.4.2": "Woke up grateful again.$1#$b#Happens every morning now. You did that to me.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.4.3": "You're so beautiful it almost hurts to look at you.$4#$b#Almost. Not enough to stop.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.4.1": "Finally cool enough to tinker in the workshop.$0#$b#Been working on something special for you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.4.2": "Maple spent the day following shade around the yard.$0#$b#Found her under the tomato plants looking personally offended by the sun.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.4.3": "You smell like sunshine and that soap you use.$4#$b#Best combination in the world. Better than any ocean breeze.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.5.1": "Good morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Even this summer heat can't compete with how hot you look.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.5.2": "Your hair catches the morning light perfectly.$4#$b#Everything about you is perfect. How is that possible?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.5.3": "Sunlight hit the water just right and reminded me of the first time I saw you by the pier. Almost made me forget I was already late.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.5.1": "You left early this morning before I could properly say goodbye.$2#$b#Come here so I can fix that oversight.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.5.2": "Been working since sunrise, but seeing your face makes it all worth it.$4#$b#Every single sweaty, exhausting minute of it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.5.3": "You work so hard every day.$1#$b#Makes me want to work harder too. Be worthy of what we have.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.6.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#This summer heat's got nothing on how you make my heart race.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.6.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Sleep well? You were mumbling about irrigation systems around midnight.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.6.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Already hot out there. What's the plan for keeping the crops happy today?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.6.4":"Found this in the mines yesterday during my day off.$h#$b#Figured my spouse deserves diamonds...even if I'm not great at the romantic gestures.[72]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.6.1": "Evening breeze finally kicked in.$1#$b#Perfect weather for holding you close and forgetting about the heat.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.6.2": "Come here and let me hold you.$4#$b#Long day, and this is what I've been looking forward to.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.6.3": "Love how content you look after a good day's work.$1#$b#Beautiful and accomplished. How did I get this lucky?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.7.1": "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#You've got that post-sleep glow that makes me want to keep you in bed all day.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.7.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Maple's been sitting by your side of the bed for twenty minutes. Think she's got requests.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.7.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Big day ahead? You've got that determined look already.$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.summer.7.4": "Maple was sprawled on the floor like a puddle. Summer’s hitting hard today.#$b#Here.#$b#Have an Ice Cream before it melts.[233]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.7.1": "Caught some decent fish today using Willy's summer techniques.$1#$b#Maybe I'll actually cook something decent for once.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.7.2": "You make me want to be better.$4#$b#Better husband, better man. You deserve the best of everything.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.7.3": "Every day I love you more.$4#$b#Didn't think that was possible, but here we are.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.7.4": "Hey. I was walking back from the docks and saw this shimmer in the sand.#$b#It’s a Sea Urchin. Not much, but...it felt like a little treasure.[397]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.8.1": "Morning, babe.$0#$b#Maple's already found the coolest spot in the house.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.8.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Willy's expecting me early, but I'm not leaving without my daily dose of you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.8.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#You left your work gloves on the kitchen counter. Planning something messy today?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.8.1": "Been avoiding the workshop all day because of the heat.$0#$b#Maybe I'll work on some fishing lures instead.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.8.2": "Willy's back went out, so I handled the heavy nets alone today.$0#$b#Old man felt guilty about it. Told him that's what having a younger guy around is for.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.8.3": "Emily asked me to move her crystal collection upstairs.$0#$b#Those things are heavier than they look. Also more fragile. Stressful combination.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.8.4":"Maple tried to hide this from me. Good thing she's terrible at being sneaky.$h#$b#Emeralds are lucky, apparently. I already feel pretty lucky, though.[60]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.9.1": "You walked past my workshop this morning and I lost track of what I was doing.$1#$b#Still not sure if I was fixing that radio or breaking it.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.9.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Maple's already claimed the coolest spot in the house. Smart bunny.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.9.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Your sunflowers are almost ready, aren't they? Been watching them grow taller every day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.9.4": "Morning, beautiful. You were curled up so tight last night, I almost didn’t want to move.#$b#I packed you a snack for later.#$b#Some Spicy Eel. Might give you a little kick today.[228]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.9.1":  "Been thinking about you all day while working the docks.$0#$b#Willy called me out for daydreaming again.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.9.2": "You make me feel like the luckiest man alive.$4#$b#Because I am. Every single day with you proves it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.9.3": "This is what happiness looks like.$1#$b#You and me, end of another day, nowhere else I'd rather be.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.9.4": "Stayed behind a few minutes after the tide pulled out. Found this clinging to the rocks.#$b#Here.#$b#A Rainbow Shell. It reminded me of you, somehow.[394]$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.10.1": "Good morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#The way you stretch when you wake up should be illegal.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.10.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#What's first on the agenda today? You've got that 'ready to conquer the world' look.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.10.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Your peppers are coming in nice. Thinking about making hot sauce this year?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.1": "Summer heat's got nothing on how you make me feel.$0#$b#Come here and let me show you what I mean.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.2": "Love how you smile when you see me come home.$4#$b#Makes every hour away from you worth it just for that moment.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.3": "Spent half the night on the porch watching fireflies. Next time, I’ll make you sit with me. It’s prettier with you there.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.4": "Maple flopped belly-up on the floor as soon as the sun dipped. Can’t blame her.#$b#I nearly joined her.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.5": "Smells like warm grass and river wind out there. Nights like this make me glad I stuck around.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.10.6": "You’ve got that sun-glow look tonight. It’s a little unfair, honestly.#$b#How you still take my breath this late in the day.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.11.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Found some wild berries down by the river. Perfect for beating this heat.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.11.2":"Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Sleep okay? You kept stealing the covers but I didn't mind. Too hot anyway.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.11.3": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Your chickens were having a full conference when I walked by. Think they're planning something?$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.summer.11.4": "Collected this from one of those glowing creatures in the mines.$h#$b#Solar essence. Warm to the touch, like sunshine in a bottle.[768]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.11.1": "Noticed Elliott staring at you during the festival.$2#$b#Guy needs to find his own muse and stop admiring mine.$6",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.11.2": "You're tired but you're smiling.$1#$b#Love that about you. Love everything about you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.11.3": "Summer days are long but they're never long enough with you.$4#$b#Could spend eternity and it wouldn't be enough time.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.12.1": "Morning, beauitful. The sun’s already working overtime.#$b#Feels like it never really cooled off last night.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.12.2": "Good morning, beautiful.$4#$b#Been working on a new drum pattern. Want to hear it tonight? Fair warning, Maple's my only critic so far.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.12.3": "Your rabbits have been plotting with Maple again.$0#$b#Found them in a circle yesterday like some kind of bunny council meeting.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.12.1": "Sam asked why I've been grinning like an idiot lately.$0#$b#Told him it's because I married way above my league.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.12.2": "Good day with the animals?$0#$b#Linus waved at me from his tent today. Guy's doing well. Looks healthier every time I see him.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.12.3": "Tell me about your day, beautiful.$1#$b#Jas asked if Maple could come play with her. Might have to arrange a bunny playdate.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.13.1": "Morning, gorgeous.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.13.2": "I woke up to Maple pounding on my chest.#$b#Think she’s reminding me to make breakfast. Want to join me in the kitchen?",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.13.3": "Willy’s dragging me to the docks at dawn. If you’re up, I’d love some company.#$b#Early mornings aren’t so bad with you here.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.13.1": "Willy says marriage has made me soft.$0#$b#If being crazy about my darling is soft, then I'm guilty as charged.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.13.2": "How was your day, sweetheart?$1#$b#Mine was interesting. Helped Clint move a new anvil. Thing weighed more than my truck.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.13.3": "Good day on the farm?$1#$b#Willy taught me some new knots today. Apparently I've been doing it wrong for months.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.14.1": "Good morning, babe.$1#$b#Summer sun's got nothing on how radiant you look right now.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.14.2":  "I’m thinkin’ of starting the day with eggs and toast. You want some, or just coffee and a kiss?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.14.3": "The dew’s still clinging to the grass.#$b#Feel like stealing you away for a sunrise stroll before the day heats up.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.14.1": "Love how you laugh at my terrible jokes.$0#$b#Makes me want to spend all night making you smile.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.14.2": "How were the crops today?$0#$b#Pierre asked me if you're selling extra preserves. Guy's got dollar signs in his eyes.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.14.3": "How did everything go today?$0#$b#Caught Elliott talking to himself by the pier again. Guy's either practicing speeches or losing it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.15.1": "That tank top should come with a warning label.$4#$b#Nearly walked into a dock post watching you this morning.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.15.2": "Dreamed I was drowning in fishing nets.$0#$b#Work's following me home. That's probably not good.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.15.3": "Maple woke me up gnawin’ on the corner of the rug again. I think she misses winter.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.15.4": "This stuff gives me the creeps, but you mentioned needing some.$h#$b#Void essence, straight from the source. The things I do for love.[769]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.15.1": "Marnie mentioned how well you care for your livestock.$0#$b#Makes me proud to hear people recognize how amazing you are.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.15.2": "How was the farm today?$0#$b#Marnie mentioned your animals look healthier than anyone else's. Made me proud.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.15.3": "Good day out there?$1#$b#Alex asked me for workout advice again. Told him dock work beats any gym. He looked skeptical.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.15.4": "The tide was strong tonight, but I stuck with it a while longer.#$b#Managed to land a solid Tuna. Thought you might want it for tomorrow's lunch.#$b#Or trade it if you're feeling fancy.[130]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.16.1": "You smell like summer rain and sunshine.$1#$b#Makes me want to pull you back to bed.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.16.2": "Morning, sweetheart. You're the best part of every morning. Just figured you oughta know that.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.16.3": "Robin's hammer broke yesterday. She asked to borrow mine.$0#$b#It's been three days. I'm starting to think it's gone forever.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.16.1": "That sundress you wore today nearly killed me.$4#$b#Spent the whole day thinking about taking it off you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.16.2": "How did everything go?$0#$b#Gus wants to buy more of your produce. Says you've got the best quality in the valley.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.16.3": "Tell me about your day, love.$1#$b#Abigail beat my high score at the arcade, unfortunately.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.17.1": "Good morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Willy asked why I keep grinning like an idiot at work. Had to tell him about my incredible partner.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.17.2": "Good morning, sweetheart. The dew’s still clinging to the petals.#$b#Thought you might enjoy seeing the world sparkle before the heat sets in.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.17.3": "The sun’s climbing fast.#$b#Wanted to steal a moment with you before the world got too bright.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.17.1": "Been working on a new drum piece inspired by last night.$0#$b#Think you could help me with the rhythm again?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.17.2": "How was your day, love?$1#$b#Wizard asked me to deliver something to Harvey. Didn't ask what it was. Probably better that way.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.17.3": "Tried to start the boat engine with a butter knife today.$0#$b#It worked. Don't tell Willy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.18.1": "Good morning, babe.$1#$b#Heading to the docks early today. Willy's got a big shipment coming in.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.18.2": "Maple's learned to open the treat drawer.$0#$b#She's evolving. This is concerning.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.18.3": "I dragged the hammock out to the orchard.#$b#Figured it’s the best place to watch you with the sunrise.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.18.4": "Been practicing my cooking skills. This is my masterpiece so far.$h#$b#Complete breakfast, made with love and only minor kitchen disasters.[201]$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.18.1": "You left for the mines before I could kiss you goodbye.$2#$b#Unacceptable. Come fix that right now.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.18.2": "Evening’s cooling down at last. Want to grab a blanket and sit on the porch with me for a bit?",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.18.3": "Fireflies are already out.#$b#Think this is the perfect night for a slow walk through the fields.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.19.1":  "Good morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Maple found the coldest spot in the house and refuses to move.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.19.2": "Caught a breeze off the water when I was checking the docks. Figured you’d appreciate the heads-up before the day fries us.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.19.3": "Morning, babe! Maple's already been up for an hour causing trouble. Found her trying to dig under Willy's tackle box.$1",
   "Daulton.Marriage.summer.19.4": "Hey. I was gonna surprise you with pancakes but ended up fighting the frying pan.#$b#So I found this instead. Not breakfast, but it’s still sweet.#$b#Here’s a Peach.[634]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.19.1": "Sandy wrote saying the desert heat makes this look like nothing.$0#$b#Still prefer our valley summers with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.19.2": "You came home covered in dirt and somehow still took my breath away.$4#$b#That's gotta be love, right?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.19.3": "Been thinking about the first time you smiled at me.$1#$b#Still hits the same way. Always will.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.20.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Even this summer heat can't ruin my mood when I wake up next to you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.20.2": "Beautiful morning by the water. Dad always said the best part of dock work was watching the sunrise over the waves.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.20.3": "Maple decided to 'help' me sort the nets this morning. Three guesses how that went.$h#$b#Let's just say we'll be untangling for a while.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.20.1": "You're handling this heat way better than me.$1#$b#What's your secret?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.20.2": "Thinking about taking Maple for her evening walk around town. Fair warning, she's been eyeing Pierre's seed display all week.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.20.3":  "Stars look beautiful over the water tonight. Sometimes I sit out here and imagine Dad seeing the same view from his freighter.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.21.1":  "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Coffee tastes better when you're the first thing I see.[395]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.21.2": "You're up early! I was just about to start organizing the tackle supplies. Wanna give me a hand? I promise Maple will mostly behave.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.21.3": "Maple’s already gnawing on something. I swear, @, if she chews through another net, Willy’s gonna skin me alive.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.21.1": "Alex was showing off at the beach again, trying to impress you. Idiot.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.21.2": "Peaceful night by the pier. Perfect for thinking about...well, everything really. Life has a way of working out, doesn't it?$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.21.3": "Maple's already asleep in her favorite corner. Little bunny works hard at being adorable all day. Can't blame him for being tired.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.22.1": "Morning, beautiful.$0#$b#Good luck with the crops today. Saw some crows eyeing your field yesterday.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.22.2": "By the way, the Adventurer’s Guild sent a letter.#$b#They want me to check out the mines again. Maple tried to hide it under the rug.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.22.3": "I caught myself humming a sea shanty before breakfast. Never thought I’d end up singing songs I used to mock back in Zuzu City.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.22.1": "Finally cool enough to practice drums without melting.$0#$b#Want to hear what I've been working on?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.22.2": "The docks look peaceful under the moon. Sometimes I wonder if I’d be braver out on the water when it’s this calm.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.22.3": "I spent the evening fixing my compass. It still points northwest, but at least the needle spins now instead of sticking.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.23.1": "Good morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Saw Harvey checking you out at Pierre's yesterday. Can't blame the guy.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.23.2": "Maple’s on a mission to chew every wooden surface in this house. I’d install metal walls if I could. She’s relentless.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.23.3": "Maple decided my shoelaces made an excellent breakfast. I spent half the morning retying them while she watched smugly.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.23.4": "Morning. I figured I’d try to bake muffins. Now we own a brick.#$b#So I’m gifting you something I didn’t cook. A nice Blueberry. Safe and sound.[258]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.23.1": "Maple got into the chicken coop again today.$0#$b#Found her napping with the hens like she belongs there.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.23.2": "The stars are out tonight. You ever notice how they look like glitter on dark water? Makes me wish I could paint that scene.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.23.3":  "I tried writing a drum riff for a new song earlier, but the rhythm kept sounding like a hopping bunny. Maybe that’s a sign.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.24.1": "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Going fishing with Sam later. He wants to learn some of Willy's techniques.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.24.2": "The sun crested the horizon just as I stepped outside. There’s something hopeful about mornings like these, even if Maple is already plotting mischief.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.24.3": "Woke up to you humming that old sea shanty. Now Maple’s hopping around trying to join in.#$b#She’s got rhythm, kind of.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.24.4": "Morning. The sun’s brutal already, huh?#$b#I packed you a Melon in case you're working outside.[254]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.24.1": "Helped move some hay bales for Marnie today.$0#$b#She mentioned how healthy our animals look compared to others.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.24.2": "Maple’s curled up in my tool pile. She insists on guarding my wrenches, though I’m not convinced he knows what they do.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.24.3": "Rest easy, babe. I’ll be right here if you need anything.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.25.1": "Morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Your chickens were making a racket this morning. I think they're excited to see you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.25.2":"Morning, love. Seeing you here makes the whole day feel brighter.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.25.3":"Woke up thinking about you.#$b#Felt right to start with a smile.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.25.1": "Sandy was impressed with how you've set up the farm.$1#$b#Said it's obvious you know what you're doing out here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.25.2": "Tried fixing that loose floorboard today, but I swear I made it louder. Sorry you had to tiptoe around.$s",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.25.3": "The workshop felt empty without your laughter. Couldn’t wait to come home and see you.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.26.1": "My birthday's coming up soon.$0#$b#Don't go crazy planning anything...just having you is the best gift I could ask for.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.26.2": "My back’s still sore from last night’s net repair, but seeing you at the window makes every ache worth it.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.26.3": "Maple nearly knocked over your teacup.#$b#Think she’s plotting to drown her worries in chamomile.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.26.1": "Long day, huh? You settle in.#$b#I’ll lock up and make sure Maple’s not chewing on the rug again.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.26.2": "I tried tinkering with that compass again.#$b#Ended up making it spin in circles. At least it kept Maple entertained.$s",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.26.3": "Heard Maple thumping across the floor; I checked twice before realizing she was scouting for midnight snacks in your shoe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.27.1": "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#End of summer already, but you just keep getting more stunning.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.27.2": "The Guild wants me to check out some tide pools later for...research purposes.$0#$b#Beats going underwater, that's for sure.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.27.3": "Someone left their fishing rod by the pier overnight. Maple's convinced it's a new toy for her to destroy.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.27.1": "Maple's been digging holes in the cool dirt all day...smart bunny.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.27.2":  "Come here, you.$8#$b#End-of-summer nights like this were made for staying close.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.27.3": "Found Maple napping in a coil of rope earlier. She looked so content I didn't have the heart to move her.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.28.1": "Morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Last day of summer heat, then we can actually function again.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.28.2": "Got a letter from my old bandmates in Zuzu yesterday. They're still playing the coffee shop circuit.$0#$b#Sometimes I miss the music, but I don't miss the noise.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.28.3": "Morning, beautiful. Maple's already claimed your side of the bed again. I tried to move her, but she gave me that look.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.28.1": "These jellies only come once a year.$0#$b#Good thing I get to experience it with the most incredible farmer in the valley.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.28.2": "Home at last. How was your day, love?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.summer.night.28.3": "Long day at the docks, but coming home to you makes it all worth it.$l#$b#Even if Maple's hogging the couch again.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.1.1": "Morning, beautiful.$1#$b#First day of fall. Your pumpkins are looking incredible this year.$1", 
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.1.2": "You're even more beautiful in the morning light. Don't argue with me. I'm your husband, I'm allowed to be sappy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.1.3": "You know what's better than waking up alone? Waking up with you and our fuzzy alarm clock.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.1.1": "Love how the cooler weather brings out the color in your cheeks.$1#$b#Fall suits you perfectly.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.1.2": "Thinking about Dad tonight. I think he would've loved you.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.1.3": "Ready for bed? Maple's already claimed her spot between our pillows. We might have to negotiate.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.2.1":  "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Good luck with harvest prep today.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.2.2": "Your sleepy voice is my favorite sound in the world.$l#$b#Well, that and when you laugh at my terrible jokes.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.2.3": "Morning, love. I still can't believe I get to wake up next to you every day.$l#$b#Best part of moving to this town was finding you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.2.1": "Learned some new techniques from Willy today.$0#$b#Your animals seemed extra curious about what I caught.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.2.2": "Home sweet home. How did we get so lucky, @? This little life of ours feels perfect.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.2.3": "Morning, my love. I was thinking...maybe tonight we could sit by the pier together? Just the three of us.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.3.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Fall colors are starting to show...reminds me why I love this valley.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.3.2": "The sunset looks different now that I have someone to share it with.$l#$b#Everything looks different, actually. Better.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.3.3": "Early shift at the docks, but I'll be thinking about you all day.$l#$b#Maybe we can watch the sunset together when I get home?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.3.1": "Been working on that drum piece again.$0#$b#Fall nights are perfect for making music.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.3.2": "Perfect evening for a walk on the beach. Want to watch the stars come out together?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.3.3": "You know what I love most about being married? Having someone who actually cares about my day.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.4.1": "Morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Saw Harvey eyeing your produce at Pierre's yesterday. Guy's got good taste.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.4.2":"I could get used to waking up next to you every day.$l#$b#Though I'm still not used to Maple judging our morning routine from his corner.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.4.3": "Your hair smells like sea salt and sunshine. Is that weird to say? Maple agrees with me, for what it's worth.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.4.1": "Found Maple trying to 'help' with the apple harvest.$0#$b#She's got the right idea, just terrible execution.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.4.2": "Every night I fall asleep grateful for this life we're building together.$l#$b#You make everything better.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.4.3": "Ready for bed? I could use some quality time with my spouse.$1#$b#Just the two of us.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.5.1": "Good morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Heading to help Willy with some boat winterizing today.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.5.2": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.5.3": "Morning, gorgeous. I was thinking about taking a boat trip this weekend. Want to come with me?$0#$b#Having you there makes me feel brave.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.5.4": "The mist was clinging to the grass when I stepped out.#$b#I brought you a Plum. Looks like autumn bottled it up just for us.[406]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.5.1": "End of another perfect day with my favorite person in the world.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.5.2":  "Want to sit on the porch tonight? I love our evening talks.$1#$b#Plus you look beautiful in the moonlight.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.5.3": "Want to plan a little getaway soon? Just the two of us, somewhere romantic.$1#$b#I saw this cozy inn advertised in the newspaper.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.6.1": "Maple's been collecting fallen leaves in her little corner.$0#$b#Even she's getting into the fall spirit.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.6.2": "You know what I realized? I used to hate mornings in Zuzu. Now I can't wait to start each day with you.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.6.3": "Good morning, beautiful. I'm working late shift today, but that means we can have lunch together at the pier.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.6.1": "Fixed that old radio finally.$1#$b#Now I can get decent metal stations while working in the shop.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.6.2": "Perfect night for stargazing. Want to grab some blankets and head to our spot by the pier?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.6.3": "You make coming home the best part of every day. I used to dread evenings in Zuzu. Now I can't wait for them.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.7.1": "Morning, sweetheart. Perfect weather for fishing. Want to join me by the river later?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.7.2": "I dreamed we were dancing last night. We should do that more often...you make me feel less clumsy.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.7.3": "Morning, gorgeous. The Guild wants me to document some new species near the tide pools. Want to come explore with me?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.7.1": "Festival season's starting up again.$1#$b#Looking forward to showing you off at all the town events.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.7.2": "I love how you steal my sweaters. You look better in them anyway.$4#$b#Though I might need them back eventually.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.7.3": "I never thought I'd be the type for domestic life, but with you? I could do this forever.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.8.1":  "Good morning, beautiful. Going to work on that boat repair with Willy. Fall's the best time for maintenance.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.8.2": "Woke up thinking about our first kiss. Still gives me butterflies, you know that?$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.8.3": "Good morning, sweetheart. I love how you look when you're still half-asleep and grumpy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.8.1": "Alex was showing off his football skills again, trying to impress you. Pathetic.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.8.2": "Long day, but seeing your face makes it all disappear.$4#$b#How did I get so lucky?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.8.3": "Evening, love. I finally finished that song I've been working on. It's about you, obviously.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.9.1": "Good morning, gorgeous. Clint mentioned he needs help with some metalwork. Might be fun to get my hands dirty.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.9.2": "The sunrise reminded me of our wedding day. Same golden light, same feeling that everything was perfect.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.9.3": "I caught myself humming while sorting nets yesterday. Willy said I've been doing that a lot since we got married.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.9.1": "Sebastian's been even more brooding than usual lately.$0#$b#Fall weather probably makes him feel extra dramatic.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.9.2": "Want to take a bath together tonight? I picked up some of those bath salts you like.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.9.3": "I love coming home to you. Our little house feels more like home than anywhere I've ever lived.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.10.1": "Morning, beautiful. Your pigs found some amazing truffles yesterday. They've got expensive taste.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.10.2": "The morning air has that crisp autumn bite. Perfect weather for snuggling up with my favorite person.$l",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.10.3": "Morning, sweetheart. I was thinking we could go apple picking this weekend. Make it a proper autumn date.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.10.1": "Good morning, sweetheart. Stardew Valley Fair's coming up, can't wait to see what you enter this year.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.10.2":"You looked beautiful working in the garden today. I kept getting distracted watching you from the dock.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.10.3": "I picked up some new sheet music in town. Want to hear me butcher it on the drums later?$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.11.1": "Found Maple trying to bury acorns like a squirrel.$0#$b#Smart bunny's preparing for winter already.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.11.2": "I still can't believe you married me, you know that?$4#$b#Sometimes I wake up thinking it was all a really good dream.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.11.3": "Morning! Just finished feeding Maple her breakfast. She's already eyeing my shoelaces like they're dessert.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.11.1": "Worked with Clint today on some interesting projects. Reminded me why I love building things with my hands.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.11.2": "Hey, I'm home. Sorry I'm late. Got distracted talking to Elliott about...well, you, mostly. He's got some fancy words for being in love.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.11.3": "Long day at the docks, but seeing you makes it worth it.4#$b#Even if I do smell like seaweed right now.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.12.1":  "Good morning, sweetheart. Going to test out some fall fishing lures I've been working on.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.12.2": "Early shift at the docks today. Willy's expecting a big haul, so I better get moving.#$b#Right after I find where Maple hid my work boots.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.12.3": "You're up early! I was just practicing some drum rudiments. Sorry if I woke you.#$b#Maple thumps back when I play.$h",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.12.1": "Love watching you plan for the fair. Your passion for everything you do is incredible.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.12.2":"Vincent asked if I could lift him up to reach the apple tree. Kid's got the right idea. Why climb when you can recruit someone with longer arms?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.12.3": "Kent asked for help moving furniture for Jodi. Guy's plenty strong, but his back's not what it used to be. Happy to pitch in.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.13.1": "Morning, gorgeous. Heading to the Saloon later to beat Abigail's high score.#$b#She's been bragging all week.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.13.2": "Beautiful sunrise over the water today. Dad always said the morning light made the ocean look like molten gold.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.13.3": "Ugh, overslept again. Maple chewed through my alarm clock cord. Third one this month. Maybe I should just train her to wake me up instead.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.13.1": "Love how you've decorated the house for fall. Makes everything feel cozy and warm.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.13.2": "Long day at the docks. My arms feel like jelly, but at least all the nets are sorted for tomorrow.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.13.3": "Just got back from Guild training. You should've seen Maple's face when I came home covered in slime.$1#$b#Actually, you should've seen MY face when I realized it was IN my hair.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.14.1": "Morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Going to help Marnie move some hay bales before the next storm hits.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.14.2": "Morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Going to help move some equipment at the docks before the weather turns.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.14.3": "Maple's doing her morning zoomies around the house. Already knocked over two lamps.$0#e#This is why we can't have nice things.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.14.1": "Evening walk with the troublemaker. She found three flowers to nibble and one shoe to steal.#$b#I'm calling that a win.$1", 
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.14.2": "Stars are really bright tonight. Sometimes I sit out here and wonder if Dad's watching from up there.$0#$b#Hope he's not too disappointed about the whole boat thing.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.14.3": "Time for Maple's bedtime banana chip. Yes, just one. Okay, maybe two.$1#$b#Fine, three, but that's it!$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.15.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Maple's been stealing apples from the orchard again.#$b#Caught her red-pawed this morning.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.15.2": "I made coffee. Didn't say it was good, just caffeinated. Proceed with caution.[395]$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.15.3": "You're still here. Good. I always worry I dream this part. Not sure what I did to get this lucky, but I’m not letting go.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.15.1": "Marnie was impressed with how healthy our animals look. Told her it's all thanks to my amazing partner's care.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.15.2": "Another day, another near-death experience with Maple and someone's garden.#e#Pierre's already drawing up a lifetime ban, I can feel it.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.15.3": "Your boots are caked in mud again. Let me guess.#$b#Swamp ghosts? No? Just tilled too hard? Fair enough.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.16.1": "Good morning, sweetheart.$1#$b#Stardew Valley Fair today. Ready to show off your incredible produce?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.16.2": "Some mornings I wish the world would slow down a little. Then you walk in, and it does.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.16.3": "Good morning, beautiful. I found one of your gloves under the couch. Don’t ask how it got there. Maple refuses to answer.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.16.1": "Your fair display was amazing today.$1#$b#Lewis couldn't stop complimenting your farming skills.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.16.2": "If you’re wondering why the living room smells like burnt apples...I tried baking. It won’t happen again. Probably.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.16.3": "Blackberry season means Maple's face is perpetually purple.$1#e#Found her in Leah's foraging spot. She was... not amused.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.17.1": "Spirit's Eve is coming.$0#$b#Perfect excuse to see you in a costume...or help you out of one later.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.17.2": "Grape harvest means Maple's been purple for three days straight. She got into the vineyard again. I'm basically raising a wine-scented rabbit at this point.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.17.3": "Morning. Maple tried to follow me into the shower again. She’s got no respect for personal boundaries.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.17.1": "Fall nights are perfect for horror games. Want to get scared together later?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.17.2": "You're back. Good. I was about to go full dramatic and stare wistfully out the window till you walked in.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.17.3": "Pumpkin spice everything at Gus's. Even the bait smells festive.#e#Willy's convinced it'll attract more fish. I'm convinced he's lost it.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.18.1": "Morning, beautiful.$1#$b#Pierre was asking if you'd consider selling more preserves. Apparently they're flying off his shelves.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.18.2": "Don’t rush. World’s not going anywhere. We’ve got time. Even if the cows don’t think so.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.18.3": "I’ve been staring at the same fence post for ten minutes thinking about breakfast. You ever get so hungry you philosophize about toast?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.18.1": "Morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Your animals seem happier now that the brutal heat's over.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.18.2":"Maple tried to redecorate the entryway. By that I mean she shoved hay under every rug.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.18.3": "Fall fog makes the boats look like ghost ships. Dad used to navigate through worse.#e#Meanwhile I get lost walking from my house to the docks.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.19.1": "Good morning, gorgeous.$1#$b#Your pigs found some amazing truffles yesterday. They're getting spoiled with all that good soil.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.19.2": "If I start calling the animals by name, does that make me a farmer yet? Or do I need to lose a boot in the mud first?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.19.3": "Woke up to birdsong and your breathing. Honestly, I don’t think I’ve ever been more at peace.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.19.1": "Perfect night for a horror movie marathon.$1#$b#Nothing beats getting scared and having you to hold onto.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.19.2": "Spirit's Eve decorations are going up. Someone put a skeleton captain on Willy's boat.$0#$b#Nearly had a heart attack at 5 AM. Thanks, whoever did that.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.19.3": "You missed Maple’s dramatic reenactment of 'I deserve a second dinner.' She flopped twice. Full performance.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.20.1":  "Your cows seemed extra content today. Fall grass must taste better than summer.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.20.2": "Maple knocked over the broom, then acted offended that the broom had fallen. She’s dramatic in the mornings. Wonder where he gets it.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.20.3": "I thought about surprising you with breakfast in bed. Then I remembered my last pancake disaster. Still owe you a clean skillet for that.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.20.1": "Love how the farmhouse smells like your cooking and fall leaves.$1#$b#Makes everything feel like home.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.20.2": "Maple dug up someone's buried treasure on the beach. Actual treasure. Gold coins and everything.$0#$b#Of course MY rabbit finds pirate gold. Of course she tries to eat it.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.20.3":"Come here, you. Tell me about your day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.21.1": "Morning, sweetheart. Sebastian was actually civil yesterday. Fall weather must be mellowing him out.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.21.2": "Morning, beautiful. Been up since dawn thinking about you. Made breakfast. Burned breakfast. Made toast instead. Romance at its finest.[216]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.21.3": "Hey gorgeous. The sunrise was incredible today, all gold and copper. Still wasn't as stunning as waking up next to you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.21.1": "Caught Harvey staring at you in town today. Guy needs to find his own amazing spouse and stop admiring mine.$6",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.21.2": "Rough day at the docks, but seeing you makes it all worth it. Come here. Let me show you how much I missed you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.21.3": "You smell like autumn leaves and sunshine. How do you always smell so good?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.21.4": "I saw Maple sitting perfectly still in the yard, like she was communing with the void. I didn’t interrupt. Felt rude.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.22.1": "Good morning, beautiful. Clint's been asking if you're selling any more metal ore. Told him to get in line.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.22.2":"Good morning. You know what I love most? That sleepy smile you do. Right there. That one. Gets me every time.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.22.3": "Morning, babe. The sun came up soft today. Gold over everything.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.22.1": "Found Maple stealing carrots from your harvest pile. Little bun's got good timing with the best produce.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.22.2": "Some nights I still can't believe this is real. You're real. Promise me we'll have a thousand more nights like this.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.22.3": "Exhausted doesn't even cover it. But then you look at me like that.$2#e#Suddenly I've got all the energy in the world. Come here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.22.4":"Shane's chickens invaded the docks today. Complete chaos. I'm finding feathers in places feathers shouldn't be. How's your day been?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.23.1": "Good morning, beautiful. Maple's been helping herself to the apple drops...little thief.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.23.2": "You headed out already? Let me know if you want company.#$b#We could walk the long way past the river. Might see that heron again.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.23.3": "I’ve been thinking about building a bench out by the old oak.$0#$b# Somewhere quiet for us to sit when the chores are done. What do you think?",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.23.1": "Love these longer nights we get to spend together. Fall's definitely growing on me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.23.2": "I started a list of things to fix around the house...then promptly lost the list. Guess we’re improvising.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.23.3": "Finally. Do you know how many times I thought about kissing you today?$1#$b#Lost count around noon. C'mere and let me show you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.24.1": "Love how excited you get about the festivals. Your enthusiasm for everything is infectious.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.24.2": "You know what's unfair? You looking this good before coffee. Meanwhile I look like I fought a sea monster.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.24.3": "Hey gorgeous.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.24.1": "Your crops are becoming famous around town. Makes me proud to see people recognize your talent.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.24.2":"You've got that look. The one that makes me forget my own name. Actually, what is my name? See? Gone. You're dangerous.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.24.3": "Spent all day moving heavy crates but my arms are never too tired to hold you.#e#That was pretty good, right? Been working on that one since lunch.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.25.1": "Good morning, gorgeous. Your goats have been extra playful since the weather cooled down.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.25.2": "We could run off to the forest today. Skip the chores. Lie in the shade and let the world turn without us for a while.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.25.3": "Maple managed to open the feed bin this morning. She’s currently running laps around the coop. Too fast to catch, too smug to stop.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.25.1": "Clint stopped by asking about your metal ore quality. Told him you've got the best eye for materials in the valley.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.25.2": "Today someone asked how I got so lucky. Couldn't answer. Still can't. But I'm not questioning it. Just grateful.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.25.3": "Maple chewed through one of my old shoelaces. I tied it back together with fishing line. If I trip, avenge me.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.26.1":"Morning, beautiful. Spirit's Eve tomorrow. This town really goes all out.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.26.2":"You talk in your sleep, did you know that? Something about pumpkins.#e#Even your dreams are adorable. How is that fair?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.26.3": "Tried to slip out quietly for work but couldn't resist one more kiss.#e#Or five. Definitely five. Willy's gonna kill me for being late.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.26.1": "Been setting up some seasonal decorations around the workshop. Nothing too scary though.#$b#Don't want to traumatize Maple.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.26.2":"There's my favorite person. Tell me something good about your day. Actually, just kiss me first. Words can wait.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.26.3": "Ugh, Pierre's asking about my 'workout routine.' Told him it's called 'being too scared to use the boat crane.' He didn't laugh.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.27.1":  "Good morning, sweetheart. End of fall alreadY. Time flies when you're this happy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.27.2":"Morning. Harvey said I'm 'built like a dock worker.' Was that a compliment? Either way, these muscles are all from hauling your farm shipments. You're welcome.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.27.3": "Hey beautiful. How's the farm this morning?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.27.1": "Another season down with you by my side. Looking forward to cozy winter nights together.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.27.2": "Alex keeps challenging me to arm wrestle. Kid doesn't know when to quit.#$b#Beat him three times yesterday.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.27.3": "How was the mine today? You look exhausted.$0#$b#Come here. These dock-worker arms are good for a few things.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.28.1": "Good morning, beautiful. Last day of fall. Going to miss watching you work in all those autumn colors.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.28.2": "Your goats were screaming at dawn again. They're louder than my drums.$0#e#How is that even possible? What are you feeding them?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.28.3": "One last breath of crisp air before the frost moves in. You want to spend it in the woods with me?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.28.4": "Maple tried to bury a snack stash in the pumpkin patch this morning. She knows winter’s coming.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.28.1": "Winter starts tomorrow, but I'm not worried.$1#$b#Any season's perfect when I get to spend it with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.28.2": "So how many pumpkins did you harvest? Willy's taking bets. I put 20g on 'too many.' That's a number, right?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.fall.night.28.3": "Last night of fall, huh? Tomorrow it'll all be frost and quiet. Kinda makes me want to hold on to you a little tighter tonight.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.1.1": "Morning, sweetheart. First day of winter. Time to break out the heavier blankets.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.1.2": "Maple’s refusing to step outside. I opened the door and she turned around like I’d personally offended her.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.1.3": "Snow’s coming down soft out there. Makes everything feel a little quieter. Kinda nice, right?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.1.1": "Fixed that old heater in the workshop today. Now I can actually work on projects without my fingers going numb.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.1.2":"Up for some Journey of the Prairie King later? I finally figured out the patterns.#$b#By 'figured out' I mean Sam told me. But still.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.1.3": "Did you catch anything good today? Willy's jealous of your fishing skills.#$b#Me? I'm just impressed you voluntarily go near water.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.2.1": "Good morning, beautiful. Maple's already claimed the warmest spot by the fireplace.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.2.2": "There’s a patch of sunlight by the window that’s just right for sitting in. I saved it for you. Maple tried to claim it but I won.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.2.3": "The snow outside’s untouched. Not even bird tracks.$0#$b#It’s like the whole valley decided to sleep in. We could too, you know.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.2.4": "Morning, sweetheart. Maple keeps hopping to the heater and back like it’s a game.#$b#Here.#$b#Have a Crocus. A little color for the grey days.[418]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.2.1": "Sam's been complaining about cold fingers affecting his guitar playing. At least my drums don't care about the temperature.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.2.2": "How many ice crystals can a rabbit eat before getting brain freeze? Maple's testing the limits. Your barn animals this dumb too?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.2.3": "Your cows look like cotton balls in the snow. It's adorable. Almost as adorable as you in that winter hat. Almost.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.3.1": "Morning, gorgeous. Willy's teaching me ice fishing techniques. Completely different game.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.3.2": "Snow’s stacked on the windows like frosting. I half expected to see a giant bite taken out of the house.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.3.3": "Morning, love. Snow came in heavy overnight. I’ll head out to clear the path.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.3.1": "Willy shared some hot cocoa after ice fishing today. Nothing beats coming home to you for warmth though.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.3.2": "Emily said I have 'surprisingly nice eyes' today. Surprisingly? What's that supposed to mean? Actually, don't answer that.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.3.3": "Evelyn called me 'that handsome young man with the rabbit' today. George called me 'that loud drummer.' I'll take both.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.3.4": "You want the good blanket today or are we sharing? I can be persuaded with pastries.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.4.1": "Good morning, sweetheart. Your animals are staying nice and warm in their upgraded shelters.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.4.2": "Hey. Don’t rush out yet.#$b#Feels like one of those days where the cold bites straight through. Thought maybe we could warm up together first.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.4.3": "Mornin’, beautiful. Wind’s already howling out by the docks. I’ll get my rounds done quick so I can meet you back here before we both freeze.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.4.1": "Ice fishing was interesting today. Definitely prefer summer fishing, but it's something new.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.4.2": "Jas asked if I'm strong enough to pull Santa's sleigh. Kids are weird. But also, probably?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.4.3": "Your horse looked at me like I was crazy for working outside today. Smart animal.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.4.4": "How many times did you slip on ice today? I'm at four. Clint saw the last one. Pretty sure my reputation's shot.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.5.1": "Morning, beautiful. Going to help Marnie with winter feed deliveries. Your animals are lucky to have such good care.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.5.2": "It’s so cold I saw Maple hesitate before leaving the blanket pile. If we’re smart, we’ll follow her lead and finish our work fast.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.5.3": "Hey. Snow’s still coming down. Let’s knock out what we have to, then disappear under every blanket in this house. Sound fair?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.5.1": "Love these long winter evenings with you. Perfect for just relaxing and talking about everything.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.5.2": "Played Journey of the Prairie King with Abby. She demolished me.#e#My ego needs comfort food. What's for dinner? $0", 
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.5.3": "Jodi asked if I could help move her couch. 'You're so strong!'Lady, I move hundred-pound crates. A couch is nothing. Want me to move anything?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.5.4": "Evening, beauitful. I don’t always know the right words, but I know what you mean to me.#$b#I found this Pearl tonight, and I just...wanted you to have something as rare as you are.[797]$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.6.1": "Morning, sweetheart. Festival of Ice is coming up, eady to show off your winter skills?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.6.2": "Morning, you. There’s ice on the inside of the barn door. If I don’t come back in ten minutes, I’ve frozen in place. Send Maple.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.6.3": "Good morning. The snow’s piled past the fence posts again. I’ll handle it.#$b#You just stay warm a little longer, yeah?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.6.1": "Saw Haley slip on ice outside Pierre's this morning. Girl needs to invest in better boots.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.6.2": "Home, finally. Willy had me reorganizing in the freezing outside all day.$0#$b#How was your day? Please say warmer than mine.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.6.3": "Made hot chocolate. The good stuff from Gus's recipe.$0#$b#Want to cuddle and complain about winter together? I'll go first.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.7.1": "Good morning, gorgeous. Elliott was complaining about winter writer's block yesterday...drama queen.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.7.2": "You’re up early. Smart. Mornings like this don’t wait.#$b#Though I wouldn’t have minded a few more minutes under the blanket with you.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.7.3": "Morning, love. I already mucked out the stable. In sub-zero weather. If that's not true love, I don't know what is. Your horse seemed grateful.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.7.1": "Pierre's been bragging about his 'winter business strategy' again. Guy sells the same stuff year-round and calls it a strategy.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.7.2": "Pierre's convinced you married me for free labor. Joke's on him. I charge in kisses. Very expensive. How's the greenhouse?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.7.3":   "How do your animals survive this? Mine's currently burrowed in my laundry.#$b#Found him by following the trail of chewed socks.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.8.1": "Woke up to Maple stealing the warm spot you left in bed.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.8.2": "Morning, love. Maple left a trail of hay across the floor like some kind of frosty breadcrumb map. I'll deal with it later.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.8.3": "Morning. Gus wants me to taste-test his new winter menu. Told him I only trust your cooking now. He looked offended.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.8.1": "Watched Pam try to drive in the snow today. That woman's either fearless or completely reckless.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.8.2": "Evelyn gave me cookies for 'being such a helpful young man.'#$b#I moved one bag of flour. One. Your farming's made me too efficient.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.8.3": "Spent lunch arguing with Shane about rabbit care. He knows chickens, not bunnies.$0#$b#Maple's a sophisticated creature.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.9.1": "Good morning, gorgeous. Your animals are handling winter like champs.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.9.2": "Maple tried to follow me outside, took one step, and turned right back around. Can’t blame her. I kind of wanted to stay curled up too.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.9.3": "Good morning, babe. If I get through my list before noon, I’m stealing you away. We can pretend we’re snowed in even if we’re not.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.9.1": "Linus somehow looks more comfortable in winter than most people do in summer.$0#$b#Guy's tougher than half the town combined.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.9.2": "Jas drew us in her family picture at school. We're stick figures.#e#But we're holding hands, so that's cute. Even drew Maple eating something.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.9.3": "Guild meeting tonight. Marlon's still pushing those underwater caves.#e#Maybe I'll just fight slimes forever. Land slimes. How's your mining going?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.10.1": "Good morning, gorgeous. Maple's been stealing extra blankets...smart bunny knows how to stay cozy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.10.2": "Morning, beautiful. I’ve got a shift down at the docks today. Shouldn’t take long.#$b#Then I’m all yours again.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.10.3": "Hey, you. Morning. I’m heading out to the forest later.#$b#Willy says a fallen tree might’ve blocked the creek. Thought I’d check it out.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.10.1": "Abigail was eating icicles at the bus stop this morning like candy.$s",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.10.2": "Good morning, gorgeous. Sam wants to jam a bit today.#$b#Might dust off the old drums if my fingers don’t freeze off first.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.10.3": "Morning, beautiful. If I finish at the docks early, meet me at the bend by the frozen stream? Could use some time alone with you.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.10.4": "You look good in the cold light, you know that? Morning, love. If I make it through sorting nets with all ten fingers, let’s do something just us later.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.11.1": "Your breath looked like little clouds this morning when you were talking. Even winter can't make you less beautiful to watch.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.11.2": "Maple chewed through my drumsticks again. The ones from Zuzu. Little bunny's got expensive taste. How's the farm this morning?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.11.3": "Morning, beautiful. Don’t go melting all the snow out there without me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.11.1": "Alex is trying to sell ice cream in winter weather. Kid's got ambition, I'll give him that. Zero business sense, but ambition.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.11.2": "Home! Maple's been waiting by the door since sunset. She does this little dance when she sees you. Same, girl. Same.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.11.3": "Made us hot chocolate. The marshmallows are bunny-shaped. Found them at Pierre's. Too cute not to buy, right?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.12.1": "Alex was out jogging in a snowstorm this morning. Kid's either incredibly dedicated or completely insane.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.12.2": "You awake, sunshine? The wind’s rough this morning. Don’t let it steal you before I get a proper good morning.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.12.3": "Forest’s got that soft light this time of year. Thought I’d walk out there after work. You in?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.12.night": "Sebastian's been lurking around the docks, guy's like a goth snowman.$5",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.13.1": "Evelyn invited us over for winter cookies again. That woman's heart is as warm as her kitchen.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.13.2": "Morning, gorgeous. Sam says we should try something new with the drumline today. I told him I’d be there once I kissed you goodbye.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.13.3":"Snow’s deeper than my boots today. Heading to the docks anyway. You’re my reward at the end.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.13.4": "Morning, love. Maple's doing her morning binkies in the kitchen. She's so happy you're here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.13.1":  "Gus is experimenting with 'winter fusion cuisine' again. Last time he tried that, I stuck to pretzels for a week.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.13.2": "Maple waited by your barn coat all day. Wouldn't move. She knows your schedule better than me. Smart little bunny.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.13.3": "Found Maple and your barn cat cuddling in the hay storage. My tough guy rabbit's gone soft. You have that effect on everyone.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.14.1": "Been working on that ice fishing technique Willy taught me. Turns out patience is harder when your hands are freezing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.14.2":"Maple’s refusing to leave the quilt pile. If you stay in bed much longer, I’m joining her.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.14.3": "Morning, babe. You’re too pretty for this weather. Snow should be jealous.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.14.1":  "Helped Willy repair ice damage on the docks today. Winter's rough on everything, but honest work feels good.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.14.2": "Maple keeps bringing you her favorite toy. The chewed-up drumstick.#e#That's her most prized possession. She loves you so much. Me too.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.14.3": "Sam says I’m offbeat when I think about you. Joke’s on him.#$b#I always think about you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.15.1": "Elliott was 'communing with the winter sunrise' by the beach today.$2#$b#Everything's a dramatic performance with that guy.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.15.2": "Morning. You ever think about just staying in bed all day? Asking for both of us.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.15.3": "Morning, love. I’ll be out stacking nets and missing you until further notice.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.15.1": "Abigail was crunching on what looked like frozen quartz at the Saloon...$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.15.2": "Can't feel my fingers from the cold. Worth it though.#$b#Made enough to take you somewhere nice.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.15.3": "Want to sneak away later? Snow’s deep near the river bend. Feels like a good place to get lost with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.16.1": "Marnie's been gossiping about Lewis's 'winter preparations' again.$0#$b#Those two need to just figure their situation out already.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.16.2": "Morning, sweetheart. I’ve got crate-lifting hands and kiss-stealing intentions.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.16.3": "Want me to bring you something back from town? If not, I’ll settle for a kiss to-go.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.16.4": "Dreamed we were dancing at the docks. No water, just music and moonlight. Might be my only good ocean-related dream ever. Thanks for that.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.16.1": "Haley refused to leave her house because snow might get on her boots. Meanwhile you're out here working in any weather like a champ.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.16.2": "My back's killing me from loading crates, but seeing you fixes everything.#$b#Come here. Missed you all day.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.16.3": "The ocean was rough today. Kept thinking about Dad out there. Then I remembered I've got you waiting at home. Made it easier.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.17.1": "Demetrius gave me a lecture yesterday about winter soil composition. Guy can make even dirt sound incredibly boring.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.17.2":"Morning, beautiful. Already shoveled the path to the coop. These dock muscles are good for something. Plus I like taking care of you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.17.3": "I wrapped Maple in a sweater this morning and she just flopped over like a throw pillow.$0#$b#Can’t say I blame her.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.17.1": "Alex is still trying to work out in this weather.#$b#Saw him slip three times.$0#$b#Dedication or stupidity, hard to tell the difference sometimes.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.17.2": "I used to think winter was just grey and miserable. Pelican Town’s changed my mind a little.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.17.3": "Winter's got that cozy vibe, doesn't it?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.18.1": "Found ice crystals on the workshop windows this morning.$0#$b#Nature's art is pretty impressive when you take time to notice.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.18.2": "The wind’s brutal. Don’t go out unless you have to. Or take me with you. I’m better than a scarf.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.18.3": "Morning, beautiful. Already loaded three boats. Arms are screaming.#e#Worth it though. Means I can carry you around later.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.18.1": "Clint's been hitting on Penny again, poor girl. Someone needs to tell him persistence isn't the same as charm.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.18.2": "Sorted tackle for eight hours. Mind's completely numb.#e#Good thing you're here to make me feel human again.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.18.3": "Full moon tonight. Dad used to say it pulled the tide and people's hearts.#$b#Cheesy old man. But looking at you...maybe he was right.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.19.1": "Found Maple trying to build a nest out of your winter scarves.$0#$b#Can't blame her for wanting the softest materials.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.19.2": "Morning, beautiful. You warm enough? I could throw a log on the fire.#$b#Or just pull you close.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.19.3": "Hey. Snow’s falling quiet today. Kind that makes me wish I could pause the whole valley and keep you like this a little longer.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.19.1": "Willy's been sharing winter fishing stories from his younger days.$1#$b#That man's lived ten lifetimes worth of adventure.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.19.2": "Played drums at the saloon. Pam threw a coin. An actual coin. My first tip. We're celebrating tonight. I'll buy the good wine.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.19.3": "Some nights I think Dad would've liked you. Brave, patient, kind. Everything he hoped I'd be. Somehow you see it in me anyway.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.20.1": "Jodi's been stress-baking again. Whole town smells like cookies. At least someone's winter anxiety has delicious side effects.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.20.2":"Got a few crates to unload today, but I’m bringing you back a fish or something shiny. Depends what jumps into the net.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.20.3":"Good morning. I left you the softest muffin and the warmest flannel. Feel free to think of me while you're cozy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.20.1": "Sebastian tried to lecture me about the 'beauty of winter's decay' today.$2#$b#I just walked away before he could get going.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.20.2": "The air smells like cinnamon and firewood lately.$0#$b#You’d think that would be enough, but I still prefer the scent of your sweater.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.20.3": "We should go to town together later. Pick out something sweet for the gift exchange. Or just walk slow and pretend to be festive.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.21.1": "Sam was complaining his guitar strings snapped from the cold.$0#$b#Maybe winter's trying to give the rest of us a break.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.21.2":"Hey. Want to pretend the snowstorm’s too strong and we’re stuck here all day? We can blame nature later.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.21.3": "Morning, love. You feel like staying in today? We can let the chores pile up just this once.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.21.1": "Lewis tried to give me a lecture about 'winter community responsibility' today.$2#$b#Guy acts like he's running a military operation instead of a small town.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.21.2": "I’ve seen the way you look at the lights in town. If I could string them across our bedroom ceiling, I would.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.21.3": "You should’ve seen Sam trying to tie a bow last night. Looked like he was wrestling a scarf. I almost cried laughing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.22.1":  "You were humming while making breakfast this morning.$1#$b#Best sound to wake up to, better than any alarm.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.22.2":"Morning. The snow looks extra soft today. Might be the light.#$b#Or it might just be how good you look in it.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.22.3":"Morning, beautiful. The Feast is coming up soon. I’ve been quietly panicking about your gift. In a charming way, of course.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.22.1": "Love how you curl up against me when it's cold.$4#$b#Best part of winter is having an excuse to stay close.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.22.2":"I’m thinking of adding a bow to Maple’s collar for the feast. She’s not thrilled. But she looks cute when she sulks.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.22.3":  "You tired, love? I kept thinking about the Feast all day. Mostly about dancing with you under the lights.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.23.1": "You look beautiful even bundled up in winter gear. How do you manage to make everything look good?$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.23.2": "You humming again this morning? I swear it’s becoming my favorite part of winter.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.23.3": "Morning. I walked by the tree in town yesterday.#$b#Nearly slipped on some snow thinking about what to write in your card.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.23.1": "Love how you steal my warmth when you're cold. Feel free to use me as your personal heater anytime.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.23.2":  "I saw Linus building a fire earlier. Said something about the longest night of the year. I thought about how lucky I am not to face it alone.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.23.3": "Feast’s almost here, beautiful. I keep checking my pockets like I forgot something. Pretty sure it’s just jitters.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.24.1": "You left soft kisses on my neck before getting up.$4#$b#Been thinking about that all morning, gorgeous.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.24.2": "You ready for tomorrow? I wrapped your gift twice just to keep Maple from unwrapping it early.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.24.3": "Feast prep’s in full swing.$0#$b#I can’t wait to see you open your gift. Hope it makes you smile.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.24.1": "Winter Star Eve tonight. All I want is to hold you close and watch the snow fall.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.24.2": "I’ve got everything ready for tomorrow. Still feels like I’m forgetting something...Did I tell you how much I love you today?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.24.3": "You’ve been glowing all day. If tomorrow’s anything like today, it’ll be perfect.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.25.1": "Happy Feast of the Winter Star, beautiful. You're the only gift I need, but I got you something anyway.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.25.2": "Happy Feast of the Winter Star. I don’t need anything but this morning with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.25.3": "There you are. Happy Winter Star, love.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.25.1": "Perfect end to a perfect Winter Star. Love making memories like this with you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.25.2": "That was one of the best Winter Stars I’ve ever had. Sharing it with you? Made it perfect.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.25.3": "Still got sparkles from the feast stuck to my jacket. Worth it to see you smile like that.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.26.1": "Still thinking about how stunning you looked at the festival yesterday.$4#$b#Had to stop myself from staring too obviously.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.26.2": "Morning, sunshine. If I could relive yesterday, I would.#$b#In a heartbeat.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.26.3": "Morning, beautiful. Still got a bit of holiday glow left in me. Might be the coffee...or you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.26.4": "Woke up early to the sound of snow shifting off the roof. Peaceful...until Maple started chewing on the woodpile again.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.26.1": "Winter nights like this were made for being close.$1#$b#Come here and let me warm you up properly.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.26.2": "Quiet night, huh? Feels like the calm after a song’s final note. I kinda like it.#$b#With you beside me.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.26.3": "I was humming that festival tune all day. Pretty sure even Maple's sick of it. But I’m still in that Winter Star mood.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.27.1":  "Winter mornings are perfect because I wake up next to you.$1#$b#Best view in the entire valley, hands down.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.27.2": "Back to the usual grind, huh? Docks won’t sort themselves. But first.#$b#One more minute with you.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.27.3": "Hey, gorgeous. Want to split the last of the festival cookies before I head out? I saved you the one with the sugar stars.[220]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.27.1": "Been thinking about you all day while working at the docks. Come here so I can show you how much I missed you.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.27.2": "Maple found a glitter ornament under the couch. I think she wants another Winter Star already.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.27.3": "Even the stars looked cold tonight. I’m glad I’ve got you to thaw out beside.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.28.1": "Caught myself staring at you over breakfast again. Still can't believe someone this incredible chose me.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.28.2": "Morning, beautiful. Last day of winter.#$b#Can you believe it? Kind of don’t want to let it go.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.28.3": "The sky’s a little brighter today, like winter’s giving us a gentle sendoff.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.28.4": "Maple brought in a pinecone like it was treasure.$0#$b#I guess we’re all holding on to winter in our own way.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.28.5": "Hard to believe this is the last snowy day for a while.$0#$b#I keep picturing you out in the fields again.#$b#With flowers in your hair $4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.28.1": "Another season with you in the books.$1#$b#Still can't believe I got this lucky.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.28.2": "No more firewood runs for a while. Might miss them, just a little. Mostly 'cause you'd always meet me at the door.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.28.3": "I saw the way you looked at those new seeds. I can’t wait to see what you grow this spring. $1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.28.4": "Maple’s been pawing at the door like she knows it’s almost her time again. I think she misses the green as much as we do.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.winter.night.28.5": "You remember last spring.#$b#When the wildflowers came in, and you picked that bunch just for the table? I’ve been looking forward to that again... probably more than I should admit.$1",

  // BIRTHDAY // 
  "Daulton.Marriage.birthday.Player": "Happy birthday, gorgeous.$1#$b#Made you something special in the workshop.#$b#Hope you love it.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.birthday.Daulton": "Thanks for making my birthday incredible, beautiful.$1",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Negative.1.1": "Oh. Uh, thanks. Wasn’t really expecting...that.$0",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Negative.1.2":"Not quite what I had in mind, but hey. Appreciate the gesture anyway.$0",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Positive.1.1": "Hey...this is really thoughtful. You didn’t have to, but I’m glad you did.$1",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Positive.1.2": "Okay, this is officially better than that year I bought myself socks and pretended it was fine.$1",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift": "Hey, thanks. Wasn’t expecting anything today, so this was a nice surprise.$1",


  // JEALOUS LINES // 
  "SpouseGiftJealous.1": "So. You gave {1} to {0}? Just being friendly, huh?",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.2": "Hey, not saying I’m upset. Just surprised you saved the {1} for {0}, that’s all.",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.4": "Must be nice, getting {1} from someone like you. Bet {0} enjoyed that.$s",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.3": "Was there a reason you picked {1}? Or just felt like making {0} smile today?$0",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.6": "Sure. Give {0} a {1}. I'll just be over here feeding Maple and pretending not to care.$s",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.7": "You’re allowed to be kind to folks. I just wish it didn’t twist my gut every time you are.#$b#Especially with {0}.$2",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.8": "Guess {0} needed that {1} more than I needed peace of mind today.$s",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.9": "If I start giving out {1}s to random folks, you cool with that? No? Just checking.$5",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.10": "Next time you’re handing out {1}s, maybe toss one my way? Just so I don’t start thinking too hard.$s",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.11": "Not gonna lie, seeing you hand {1} to {0} made me wanna go chop wood 'til I forget why I’m annoyed.$5",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.12": "Do you always smile like that when you give people gifts, or was {0} just special today?$s",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.13": "You sure know how to keep a guy on his toes. One day it's me, the next it's {0} getting a {1}.$5",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.14": "If I start handing out {1}s to Sandy, we calling it even or starting a fire?$0",
  "SpouseGiftJealous.15": "Next time you’re out being sweet to {0}, maybe save a little of that for me too, yeah?",
  "Spouse_MonstersInHouse.1.1": "Okay, I didn’t bring a monster home, so either we’ve got company or this place is haunted again.$5",

  //FESTIVALS//
  "Daulton.eggfestival.0": "Maple keeps twitching her nose toward the hidden eggs.$0",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.1": "You think there’s a strategy to egg hunting, or is it just sprint and hope?",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.2": "Kids seem to have the right strategy for this. Lower to the ground, more energy.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.3": "Maple found a candy wrapper and now thinks she's winning. I didn’t have the heart to tell her.",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.4": "Maple would dominate this competition if she was allowed.$0#$b#Bunny's got natural egg-hunting instincts.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.5": "Maple tried to sneak into the snack table earlier. She almost got away with it, too.",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.6": "This beats sitting in my workshop all day.$0#$b#Though watching you work is entertainment enough.$4",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.7": "Abigail's treating this like a military operation. Girl takes everything seriously.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.8": "Sam asked if I'd drum for next year's festival music. Told him only if you're dancing to it.$4",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.9": "Willy claims he used similar tactics hunting treasure on remote islands.$0#$b#Old man's got stories for everything.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.10": "A kid asked if I was a 'festival pirate' because of my work clothes.$0#$b#I didn't correct him. Seemed disappointed enough already.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.11": "Maple escaped this morning and found three eggs before the hunt started.$0#$b#I didn't report it. Bunny earned those fair and square.$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.12": "No pressure, but there’s a whole group of kids over there ready to absolutely destroy your score.",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.13": "A kid called me 'Egg Master Daulton.'$0#$b#Should I put that on business cards?$1",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.14": "Haley complained that dirt would ruin her manicure. I offered her my work gloves. She looked horrified.$0",
  "Daulton.eggfestival.15": "Penny asked if I'd help organize next year's hunt. I already have seventeen improvement ideas. She looked concerned.$1",

  "Daulton.flowerdance.accept.1.1": "Yeah, absolutely! This'll be fun. I've been looking forward to the flower dance all week.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.accept.1.2": "Of course I’ll dance with you. You just made this whole day ten times better.$l",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.accept.1.3": "Alright, partner. Let’s give the crowd something to look at.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.accept.1.4": "That's exactly what I was hoping to hear! I've got some rhythm saved up just for this occasion.$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.1": "You really think I’d say no? Let’s go make the other couples jealous.$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.2": "You know I’d say yes. I’m just glad you still want to ask.$4",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.3": "Dance with my amazing spouse? Now that's the best offer I've had all day. Let's go, gorgeous.$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.4": "You know I can't say no to you, especially when it comes to dancing. Come here, beautiful.$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.5": "Dancing with you is my favorite part of any festival. Ready to show everyone how it's done, babe?$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.6":  "My spouse wants to dance with me? Well, twist my arm why don't you. I love you, you know that?$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.7": "You're the only dance partner I'll ever need. Come on, let's give them something to talk about.$1",
  "FlowerDance.Accept.Spouse.1.8": "You really think I’d let anyone else dance with you?$b#Come on.$1",

  "Daulton.flowerdance.0":  "I spent half the morning dodging Pierre and his matchmaking. I swear he’s worse than my aunt.",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.1":  "I love how dancing makes the whole valley feel connected. Music brings people together in ways nothing else can.$4",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.2": "The flower arrangements are actually pretty impressive. Someone put real thought into the aesthetic here.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.3": "Been practicing dance steps in the workshop all week. Maple keeps judging my footwork. Tough crowd.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.4": "Haley complained that her partner stepped on her dress. I suggested steel-toed dancing shoes. She wasn't amused.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.5": "Elliott keeps talking about 'the dance of life and love.'Dude, it's just a waltz. Relax.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.6": "Willy taught me some old sailor dance moves.$0#$b#Apparently they don't translate well to formal occasions.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.7": "Alex asked if dancing builds muscle.$0#$b#I told him everything's a workout if you do it right.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.8": "Haley's complaining about grass stains on her dress. It's an outdoor festival. What did you expect?$2",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.9": "Dancing reminds me why I fell in love with music originally.$1#$b#It's all about feeling the beat in your bones.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.10": "The flower dance brings out everyone's softer side.$1#$b#Even Alex looks graceful when he's not trying to flex.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.11": "The flower crown thing is growing on me. Sandy would laugh if she saw me wearing one, but I don't care.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.12": "The flower arrangements smell incredible today. Perfect backdrop for showing off some decent moves.$1",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.13": "I suggested adding a drum solo section to the traditional music.$0#$b#Lewis said that's 'not how traditions work.' Killjoy.$2",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.14": "I've been practicing spins in the workshop. Maple keeps getting dizzy just watching me.$0",
  "Daulton.flowerdance.15": "Emily mentioned she'd love to see a 'metal fusion' dance version. Finally, someone who appreciates creative evolution.$1",

  "Daulton.luau.0": "I brought some spices Willy picked up from his trading days.$0#$b#Fair warning.#$b#Sailors have adventurous taste preferences.$1",
  "Daulton.luau.1": "I may or may not have seen Sam pour Joja Cola in the soup. We're doomed.",
  "Daulton.luau.2": "Your contribution's going to save this soup again.$1#$b#You've got magic in those hands, I swear.$4",
  "Daulton.luau.3": "The Governor's coming to eat mystery soup made by random townspeople. Either he's brave or completely insane.$1",
  "Daulton.luau.4": "Elliott added something he called 'essence of poetic inspiration.'I'm pretty sure it was just oregano, but he seemed pleased.$0",
  "Daulton.luau.5": "Sam suggested adding energy drink to the soup for 'extra kick.'I talked him out of it. You're welcome, Governor.$0",
  "Daulton.luau.6": "Willy told me sailor's soup recipes from his traveling days.$0#$b#Apparently 'hardtack and seaweed' isn't festival appropriate.$1",
  "Daulton.luau.7": "Alex asked if protein powder counts as a traditional ingredient.$0#$b#I told him that's not how food works.$0#$b#He looked confused.$2",
  "Daulton.luau.8": "Sebastian's contribution looks suspiciously like mushrooms from the mines. Kid's either brave or trying to poison everyone. Hard to tell.$0",
  "Daulton.luau.9": "Willy shared some old sea recipes for group cooking. Apparently pirates had better food safety standards than this festival.$1",
  "Daulton.luau.10": "I brought some fish from yesterday's catch.$0#$b#Figured actual food ingredients might help out whatever else goes in there.$0",
  "Daulton.luau.11": "Willy contributed some 'secret sea herbs' to the soup.$0#$b#I'm choosing not to ask what those actually are.$2",
  "Daulton.luau.12": "Beach festivals beat working in the summer heat.$0#$b#Ocean breeze makes everything more tolerable.$4",
  "Daulton.luau.13": "I suggested adding some kelp I found at the docks. Gus looked horrified. Apparently seaweed isn't 'traditional.'$2",
  "Daulton.luau.14": "Alex offered to 'flex the flavor' into the soup. I have no idea what that means, and I don't want to find out.$2",
  "Daulton.luau.15": "Haley refuses to taste the soup until someone else tries it first.$2#$b#Smart strategy, actually. I might adopt that approach.$1",

  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.0": "Willy tried to explain the jellyfish migration patterns to me. Old man knows more marine biology than most actual scientists.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.1": "I could watch them drift all night. Kinda hypnotic, huh?",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.2": "Maple keeps trying to hop toward the glowing water.$0",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.3": "The glow reminds me of those old horror movie effects. Except these don't want to eat anyone. Probably.$0",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.4": "I asked Willy if they're good eating. He just laughed and walked away. I'll take that as a no.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.5": "The water's so calm tonight it's like glass.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.6": "Alex asked if swimming with them would be good exercise. I explained why that's a terrible idea. Twice.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.7": "The water's so still tonight you can see every detail. Makes me appreciate living somewhere with actual natural beauty.$4",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.8": "Vincent keeps asking if the jellies are friendly. Kid's got the right idea.#$b#Everything's better when it might be your friend.$4",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.9": "The water's so calm tonight you can hear them moving. Turns out jellyfish make the weirdest little splashing sounds.$0",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.10":  "The water's so clear tonight you can see them coming from far out. Like watching a slow-motion underwater light parade.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.11":  "Evelyn brought blankets for everyone to sit on the sand. That woman thinks of everything. Town treasure.$1",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.12": "The way they pulse together is almost hypnotic.$0",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.13": "They're like living lanterns drifting through a liquid sky.$0#$b#Sometimes nature creates art that puts humans to shame.$4",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.14": "Sandy would love this.#$b#She's obsessed with natural phenomena. Desert doesn't have glowing sea creatures. Our valley wins.$4",
  "Daulton.moonlightjellies.15": "I've never seen anything this beautiful in my life.$0#$b#Makes me understand why people write poetry about the ocean.$0",

  "Daulton.stardewfair.0":  "I keep losing star tokens and I’m still having fun. That's how they get you.",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.1": "Another year, another chance for you to show off. Not that you need to.#$b#You're impressive every day.$4",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.2": "Your display's going to crush the competition again. I'd bet money on it, but that wouldn't be fair to everyone else.$4",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.3": "I suggested adding a drumming competition for next year's fair.$0#$b#Lewis said that's 'too noisy.' Man has no vision for entertainment.$2",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.4": "The strength tester looks rigged in Alex's favor.$0#$b#Guy's been practicing on that thing all summer.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.5": "I brought Maple but she keeps trying to eat the display vegetables. Bunny's got expensive taste in produce.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.6": "The fishing competition's a joke when Willy's not participating. Old man would demolish everyone and he knows it.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.7": "I won three tokens at the spinning wheel and bought cotton candy.$0#$b# First time I've had fair food since I was a kid.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.8": "The grange display competition gets more intense every year.$0#$b# People take their vegetables very seriously around here.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.9": "Haley's complaining that fair dirt is ruining her shoes.$0#$b# Maybe don't wear heels to an outdoor farm festival?$0",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.10": "The prize wheel's rigged.#$b#I can tell from the weight distribution.$0#$b#Still fun to spin, but don't expect fair odds.$1",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.11": "Abigail's eating the decorative gourds again.$0#$b#Girl's got the strangest appetite in the valley.$2",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.12": "The fair food's not bad when you're used to Saloon cuisine. Low bar, but they cleared it.$0",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.13": "Elliott keeps describing vegetables with poetic metaphors. They're turnips, Elliott. Just call them turnips.$0",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.14": "Emily's booth has more colors than a hardware store paint section. Girl doesn't believe in subtlety, but it works somehow.$4",
  "Daulton.stardewfair.15": "Maple would win any 'cutest pet' competition hands down. Too bad they don't have categories for perfect bunnies.$0",

  "Daulton.spiritseve.0":  "Maple's been fascinated by the carved pumpkins. Keeps trying to figure out if they're edible or decorative.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.1": "Saw something move in the maze and almost left a Daulton-shaped hole in the wall.", 
  "Daulton.spiritseve.2": "Maple wore a little pumpkin hat earlier. She hates me now.",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.3": "Hid behind a tree and spooked Caroline earlier. Woman nearly launched her candy basket into orbit.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.4": "The caramel apples are way better than anything I could make.$1#$b#Festival food beats my cooking disasters every time.$4",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.5": "The pumpkin bread's incredible.$0#$b#Been eating way too much of it.$1#$b#Good thing this only happens once a year.$4",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.6": "Jas asked if my bunny turns into a werewolf on Halloween.$0#$b#Told her Maple's scary enough in daylight.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.7": "The kids keep daring each other to talk to me.$0#$b#My reputation as the 'scary dock guy' is finally paying off.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.8": "The candy quality here beats anything from Zuzu City stores.$1#$b#Homemade treats versus factory sugar? No contest.$4",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.9": "This is my favorite festival by far.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.10": "Set up a jump scare near the cemetery entrance. Got Lewis good. Man nearly dropped his clipboard.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.11": "The caramel popcorn's dangerously addictive.$1#$b#Already gone through three bags and it's not even midnight.$4",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.12": "The hot chocolate's perfect for a chilly October night.$1",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.13": "The chocolate skulls are way better than Pierre's regular candy selection.$1#$b#Halloween brings out the good stuff.$4",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.14": "Saw Harvey in the maze earlier. He jumped at a fake bat and almost apologized to it.",
  "Daulton.spiritseve.15": "Got Alex to shriek by dropping fake spiders on him.$0#$b#Tough guy facade crumbles fast around plastic arachnids.$1",

  "Daulton.festivalofice.0": "Ice fishing's harder than regular fishing but twice as cold.$0#$b#Good thing Willy taught me the tricks for winter catches.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.1": "One of these years I’ll win. Probably. Maybe. Do you think Maple could enter?",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.2": "Willy's been giving everyone fishing advice they didn't ask for.$0#$b#Old man's in his element with a captive audience.$5",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.3": "Someone should tell Elliott that fish don't care about poetry.$2#$b#Dude's been reciting verses to his fishing hole for an hour.$5",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.4": "Funny how everyone acts surprised when the lake freezes.$0#$b#It’s been doing that every winter since I got here.$5",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.5": "The fish are sluggish in cold water but still biting.$0#$b#Just takes more patience than summer fishing.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.6": "Back in Zuzu, we didn’t have ice fishing. Just busted radiators and frozen pipes.$0#$b#This is weirdly peaceful in comparison.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.7": "Willy's got his game face on today. That beard of his twitches when he’s focused. It’s weirdly intimidating.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.8": "I've been meaning to rig a mini heater into my tackle box.$0#$b#But then I remember I’m not actually that ambitious.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.9": "The cold doesn’t bother me much.$0#$b#Zuzu winters taught me to stop feeling my fingers around mid-January.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.10": "Willy keeps nudging me about technique, like I’m trying out for the pros.$0#$b#I just nod. Let the old man have his moment.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.11": "The ice creaked earlier and Jazz screamed so loud I dropped my snack.$0#$b#There go my salted peanuts. Tragic.$2",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.12": "Marnie offered me some hot cider. Burned my tongue and still thanked her for it.$0#$b#Small town manners, I guess.$5",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.13": "The first time I tried ice fishing, I dropped the rod straight down the hole.$0#$b#Willy still won’t let me forget it.$5",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.14": "You know, this isn't the worst way to spend a morning.$0#$b#Frozen toes aside, it's kinda peaceful out here.$1",
  "Daulton.festivalofice.15": "This cold? It'll wake you up better than any cup of coffee.$0#$b#Might freeze your eyelids off, but you’ll be alert.$1",

  "Daulton.winterstar.0": "I tried tying a little red bow on Maple for the festival. She chewed it off in ten seconds flat. Little rascal still looks festive, though.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.1":  "You know it's a real holiday when someone brings out a plate the size of a wagon wheel.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.2": "I’ve been hovering near the roasted chestnuts all afternoon.$0#$b#If I vanish, check the snack table first.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.3": "I wrapped mine up in a Saloon napkin. It’s the thought that counts, right?$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.4": "I tried to make cookies for this. Turns out I’m better with a wrench than a whisk.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.5": "Didn’t know what to get my person, so I went with what I’d want.$0#$b#Hopefully they like practical stuff.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.6": "If you ever need a last-minute gift, just tape a candy cane to anything and call it festive.$0#$b#Worked for me.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.7": "Maple’s curled up near the fire with half a carrot hanging out of her mouth.$0#$b#Living the dream, honestly.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.8": "If someone got me something handmade, I’d probably keep it forever.$0#$b#Doesn’t happen much once you’re grown.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.9": "I don’t say this kind of thing often. $0#$b#I’m glad I ended up in this town. Especially today.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.10": "Whatever Gus put in that stew? I’d fight someone for the last bowl.$0",
  "Daulton.winterstar.11": "There’s a casserole over there that’s got at least five types of cheese.$0#$b#Dangerous. In a good way.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.12": "Not gonna lie.#$b#Most of my Winter Star spirit comes from free food and not having to cook.$0#$b#Feels like a win-win.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.13": "I brought store-bought crackers and tried to make ‘em look homemade.$0#$b#Covered ‘em in rosemary. No one’s questioned it yet.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.14": "If I go missing after tonight, assume I blacked out from overeating and check behind the dessert table.$1",
  "Daulton.winterstar.15": "There’s a pie over there that changed something in me.$0#$b#Like...emotionally.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.1": "You ever feel like the sand’s hiding something?$0#$b#Could be bones, could be treasure. Could just be a beetle.$h",

  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.1": "Hey, before things get too noisy.#$b#This is for you.$b#I know it’s not wrapped all fancy, but I picked it out myself.$4",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.2": "I've been hiding this from you for days now. Ready for your Winter Star surprise, gorgeous?$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.3": "Alright, close your eyes.#$b#Don’t ask, just do it.$b#Okay, now open. Happy Winter Star.$1",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.4": "You know how much I love giving you things that make you smile? Well, here's your Winter Star gift, beautiful.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.5": "Hey babe, I got you something special for Winter Star. I really hope you like it...I put a lot of thought into this one.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.6": "So, I may have spent way too much time picking out your Winter Star gift. Here goes nothing, sweetheart.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.7": "Winter Star gift time! I've been excited about this for weeks. I really think you're gonna love it, honey.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.8":  "Okay, so... I might have asked half the town for advice on this gift. Here's hoping they steered me right, babe.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.Before.Spouse.1.9": "I was so nervous about this gift that Maple kept giving me looks. But I think you'll really like it, sweetheart.$h",

  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.1": "Did you like it? I was so nervous you wouldn't...Winter Star's not the same without seeing that smile on your face. You're the best gift I could ever ask for, you know that?$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.2": "Hope you liked it. I spent way too long second-guessing, but...I think I got it right this time.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.3": "Glad I could give you something today. You’ve done more for me this year than you probably know.$4",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.4": "Hope it brought you even half the joy you’ve brought me lately.$4",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.5": "If I could’ve wrapped up the whole year and handed it to you, I would’ve.$1",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.6": "Thanks for pretending the wrapping job wasn’t a total mess. I owe you one.$b#Or two.$1",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.7": "Your reaction was worth all the stress I put myself through picking that out. You're amazing, you know that?$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.8":"Every Winter Star with you is better than the last. You make everything brighter, sweetheart.$h",
  "WinterStar.GiveGift.After.Spouse.1.9":"That look on your face is why I spend so much time thinking about your gifts. You're incredible, babe.$h",

  "WinterStarReceiveGift72": "A diamond? Seriously?$b#Didn’t think I was on that nice list this year. Thanks.",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift168": "Trash. Huh. You know, I’ve gotten worse.$s",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift221": "Pink cake? You really think I’m the kind of guy who eats cute desserts? ...You’re right.$h",  
  "WinterStarReceiveGift395": "Coffee? You do know me. This’ll get me through the cold mornings, no question.$h",  
  "WinterStarReceiveGift444": "Duck feather, huh? Fancy. I’ll find a good spot for it.$h",  
  "WinterStarReceiveGift305": "Void egg. That’s...thoughtful? In a haunted sort of way.$0",  
  "WinterStarReceiveGift848": "Cinder shard? That’s just cool. Thanks for the arcane rock.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift166": "You got me a treasure chest? Okay, now I feel underdressed for this.$1",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift194": "Fried egg. Can’t go wrong with a classic. Feels like a real breakfast gift.$1", 
  "WinterStarReceiveGift202": "Fried calamari? Didn’t expect seafood, but alright.#$b#This smells amazing.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift233": "Ice cream in winter? Bold choice. You know I’m not complaining.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift208": "Glazed yams. Yeah, I’ve tried these before. Didn’t go great.$s",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift346": "Beer? Uh. not really my thing. But thanks, I guess.$s", 
  "WinterStarReceiveGift196": "A salad. That’s what you picked? Alright then.$s",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift260": "Hot peppers! Now we're talking! You know I love spicy food. These'll be perfect for warming up during winter.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift74": "Whoa, a prismatic shard? This thing's incredible! The way it catches the light...Emily would go crazy for this.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift535": "A geode! I love cracking these open to see what's inside. Like a little mystery package. Thanks!$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift337": "Iridium? This is some high-quality stuff! Clint's gonna be jealous when he sees this.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift732": "Crab cakes? Okay, that’s fancy. Don’t expect me to share.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift787": "Battery pack? Now that’s a smart gift. I’ll actually use this.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift98": "Dwarf scroll III? You just giving me homework now?$s",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift122": "Dwarf gadget. What am I supposed to do with this? ...Actually, don’t tell me. I’ll figure it out.$0",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift336": "Gold bar. Well that’s generous. Either you like me or you don’t understand money.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift150": "Red snapper? That’s a clean catch. Bet it’d fry up nice.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift630": "An orange sapling. Bold gift. I’ll try not to kill it.$l",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift246": "Wheat flour? You know I’m not much of a baker, right?$s",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift432": "Truffle oil. Smells like money...and mushrooms.$1",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift107": "Dinosaur egg? What am I even supposed to do with this? Actually, don’t tell me.$1",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift268": "Starfruit. Fancy stuff. You really brought out the good gifts this year.$h",
  "WinterStarReceiveGift595": "Fairy rose. That’s a little unexpected. But it smells good, I’ll give you that.$l",

  "WinterStar_ReceiveGift.1.1": "Thanks. You didn’t have to get me anything, but I’m glad you did.$h",
  "WinterStar_ReceiveGift.1.2": "Hey, that’s actually pretty great. You’ve got good taste.$h",
  "WinterStar_ReceiveGift.1.3": "Appreciate it. I’ll hang onto this.$h",
  "WinterStar_ReceiveGift.1.4": "Nice. Not sure how you knew I needed this, but thanks.$h",
  "WinterStar_ReceiveGift.1.5": "That’s a solid gift. Guess I owe you one now.$h",


  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.2": "Between the heat shimmer and the wind, everything looks and sounds like it's vibrating. Desert reverb, Sandy called it. Kinda love that.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.3": "I grew up near saltwater and storms. This dry silence? Feels alien...but weirdly peaceful.$0",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.4": "Apparently there's a guy here who plays the didgeridoo in a cave. I’m tracking that sound down before sunset.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.5": "You ever feel like the sand’s hiding something? Could be bones, could be treasure. Could just be a beetle.$h",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.6": "You ever just...look at the sky out here and feel like you’re going to fall upward? Might be the heat talking. Or maybe that cactus soda I drank.$0",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.7": "You’d tell me if I had cactus stuck to me, right? Like...before I walk around like a porcupine?",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.8": "If one more person tries to hand me 'blessed moon dust,' I’m walking into the dunes and letting the vultures sort it out.",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton.1.9": "Everywhere I step there's either a sandal vendor or someone claiming they found inner peace in a taco. This place is wild.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.1": "Stay close, beauitful. I’ll snag us two iced cactus juices before the crowd drains the cooler.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.2": "You, the open sky, and a long horizon...Hard to believe I ever thought city lights were better than this.$l",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.3": "I’ll trade you one sweaty hat and a half-melted snack for a kiss under the desert sun. Fair trade, right?$h",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.4": "Remind me to never wear black jeans to a desert festival again. Unless you plan on carrying me home like a dramatic lounge singer.$l",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.5": "Funny. A year ago I wouldn’t have pictured myself here...But now? I can’t picture being anywhere you aren’t.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.6": "Willy got pulled into some kind of dance circle earlier. I’ll never unsee it.",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.7": "I was gonna complain about the heat, but then I saw a guy napping in a hammock with a lizard on his chest. Changed my whole perspective.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.8": "I almost bought us matching sun hats. I stopped myself.#$b#Barely. You’re welcome.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.9": "Every time I think I’ve figured this place out, I turn a corner and see something that looks like it crawled out of a dream. Kind of love that.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.10": "I have sand in places I didn’t even know existed. You're lucky I like you, or I'd already be back on the bus.$0",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.11": "You’re glowing. Not just from the heat, either. It’s good to see you like this.$1",
  "DesertFestival_Daulton_marriage.1.12": "Don’t worry about me. I'm good. You just keep enjoying yourself.#$b#I’ll be here, soaking up the view.$1",


  // TOWN LINES //
  "Daulton.Town.1": "I saw Jas chase a chicken this morning. The chicken won. Barely.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.2": "Just grabbing some supplies before heading back to the docks. Town's pretty quiet today.",
  "Daulton.Town.3": "Every time I pass by Pierre’s, I wonder if he secretly naps behind the counter. Feels like a safe bet.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.4":  "Love walking through the square. Reminds me why I left Zuzu City behind.$0",
  "Daulton.Town.5": "Thinking about hitting the Saloon later. Could use some arcade time.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.6": "Wonder what Gus has cooking today. My stomach's starting to rumble.$0",
  "Daulton.Town.7": "Sebastian walked by earlier and muttered something about existence being a loop.$0#$b#I offered him a snack.$0#$b#He walked faster.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.8": "Sam wants to start a band again. He pitched the name 'Molten Thunder.'I told him to sleep on it. Like, for a week.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.9": "Marnie tried to give me a jar of pickled something.$0#$b#I accepted it.$0#$b#Still trying to identify what it was.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.10": "Haley asked me what conditioner I use.$0#$b#I said 'dock wind and denial.’ Didn’t go over great.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.11": "I swear Emily’s outfit today could blind a squid.$0#$b#She pulls it off, though. Somehow.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.12": "Sandy sent me a letter with glitter in it. I’ll be finding sparkle on my gear for weeks.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.13": "Abigail challenged me to a gaming rematch.$0#$b#I pretended to hesitate.$0#$b#I did not hesitate.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.14": "Sometimes I just walk the long way home. Not in a rush. Feels good to stretch out the day.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.15": "Ran into Harvey today. He asked how I was sleeping.$0#$b#Didn’t have the heart to tell him I’ve been dreaming about angry fish.$2",
  "Daulton.Town.16": "Caroline’s always trying to hand me tea. I’m not polite enough to pretend I like it, but I’m not rude enough to say no.$5",
  "Daulton.Town.17": "Penny asked if I’ve read the library's historical records yet.$0#$b#I told her I once skimmed a cereal box.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.18": "Elliott complimented my posture earlier. I didn’t know what to do with that. Tried to stand weirder on purpose.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.19": "Ran into George. He grunted once. Pretty sure that counts as a greeting.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.20": "Harvey always looks like he’s trying not to worry out loud. Hope someone reminds him to breathe now and then.$0",
  "Daulton.Town.21": "Sometimes I just sit on the dock with a sandwich and pretend I’m busy. It fools about half the town.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.22": "Sometimes I wonder if I’m too rough around the edges for this place. Then you hear Pam laugh and realize: nah, I fit in just fine.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.23": "Sometimes I miss the city skyline. But then I remember this place has actual stars. Seems like a fair trade.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.24": "If you see me standing around not doing anything...that’s intentional. I'm very committed to it.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.25": "Penny’s got a good heart. Reminds me of people I should’ve been kinder to, back when I didn’t know better.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.26": "Maple woke me up by headbutting my pillow. Can’t even be mad. Little bunny's got priorities.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.27": "Maple has this thing where she flops over dramatically whenever I vacuum. I think she’s mocking me.$5",
  "Daulton.Town.28": "Leah said she wants to paint Maple one day. I told her good luck.#$b#She moves like a dust storm in a fur coat.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.29": "Sebastian said he ‘respects’ Maple’s ability to do absolutely nothing and still be adored.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.30": "If you ever need a therapy session, I recommend holding a bunny for five minutes. Maple’s booked, though.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.31": "Sometimes I just sit on the porch with Maple and listen to the wind.$0#$b#Not a bad way to spend a morning.$1",
  "Daulton.Town.32": "Should probably pick up some carrots for Maple while I'm out.",
  "Daulton.Town.33": "Maple refuses to eat store-brand pellets now. I’ve created a tiny, judgmental aristocrat.$5",
  "Daulton.Town.34": "Emily gave Maple a sparkly bow. She wore it for a whole five minutes before trying to eat it.$5",
  "Daulton.Town.35": "You haven’t known true betrayal until your own bunny chews through your headphone cord. Twice.$5",
  "Daulton.Town.36": "Not to be dramatic, but I’d fight a bear for that rabbit. Just putting that out there.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.1": "Hey there, gorgeous. Just running some errands around town. Want to walk with me for a bit?$0",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.2": "I passed by the Saloon and thought about grabbing a snack...Then I remembered what you packed me. Way better.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.3": "Someone asked if I miss city life. I told them I’d rather have one quiet morning with you than a hundred loud nights out.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.4": "Perfect timing, @. I was just thinking about you.$0#$b#Town's nice, but it's better when you're here.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.5": "Look who I ran into. My favorite person in the whole valley. How's your day going, babe?$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.6": "There's my beautiful spouse. You always manage to brighten up the whole town square.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.7": "Hey, love. I was about to grab some supplies. Need anything while I'm making the rounds?$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.8": "Running into you in town never gets old. Still can't believe I get to go home to you every day.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.9": "Hey beautiful.$l#$b#Town's busy today, but I always have time for you. How about we catch up at home later?$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.10": "There's that smile I love. Makes the whole day worth it, @.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.11":  "Look what the tide brought in. My gorgeous spouse, making everyone else jealous.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.12": "Perfect timing, @. I was just thinking we should do something together tonight.$1#$b#Maybe some arcade games at the Saloon?$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.13": "Sandy sent a letter teasing me for going domestic. Joke’s on her.#$b#I’ve never been happier.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.14": "Look who's gracing the town with their presence. I'm a lucky guy, getting to call you mine.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.15": "There's that face I love waking up to. What brings you to town today, gorgeous?$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.16": "Well this is a nice surprise. I was just thinking about how much I missed you.$1",
  "Daulton.TownSpouse.17": "Hey beautiful. Just the sight I needed to see. How about we head home and relax together?$1",

  //FOREST LINES//
  "Daulton.Forest.1": "Found a stick shaped like a lightning bolt. I gave it to Maple. She was unimpressed.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.2": "Forest reminds me why I left the city. You can actually hear yourself think out here.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.3": "Nice to get away from the docks for a bit. Forest's got a different kind of peace to it.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.4": "Thinking about checking out the Adventurer's Guild later. This place gets me in the mood for adventure.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.5": "Good place to clear your head. Fresh air and no noise except the wind.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.6": "Taking a break from tinkering. Sometimes the best ideas come when you're not forcing them.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.7": "Sometimes I come out here just to think. Helps me sort through the static in my head.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.8": "I think I saw a fox earlier. Or it was just a very judgmental cat. Either way, it vanished.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.9": "Saw a squirrel with something shiny in its mouth. Gonna lose sleep wondering what it stole.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.10":  "Taking a mental break from the docks. Forest helps reset the brain.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.11": "I keep finding interesting sticks out here. Might build Maple a throne if I get enough of them.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.12": "If I sit still long enough, birds start treating me like furniture. Kind of flattering, honestly.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.13": "Saw a wild rabbit dart across the path. Maple immediately looked offended.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.14": "Wonder if any of these fallen logs would work for my workshop. Always need good lumber.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.15": "I caught Maple carrying a leaf like it owed her money. She’s very serious about her foraging.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.16": "Maple tried to make friends with a toad. The toad was deeply unimpressed.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.17":  "Forest feels safer knowing Magnus is keeping an eye on things from that tower. Good to have a wizard around.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.18": "Wonder if Magnus ever gets lonely out here. Forest is peaceful, but it's pretty isolated.$0",
  "Daulton.Forest.19": "Might grab some branches for Maple. She loves chewing on fresh wood.$1",
  "Daulton.Forest.20": "Should ask Magnus about forest monsters sometime. Guy probably knows which ones are actually dangerous.$0",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.1": "Hey gorgeous. Perfect day for a forest walk with my favorite person.$1#$b#This place feels even more peaceful when you're here with me.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.2":  "There's my beautiful spouse. Forest's nice, but the view just got a whole lot better.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.3": "Forest's got nothing on you, babe. But it's a pretty romantic backdrop for spending time with my spouse.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.4": "Maple keeps trying to eat everything green.$0#$b#If I vanish into the woods one day, just follow the chewed leaves.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.5": "Saw a rabbit bolt across the path. Maple looked personally insulted. You should've seen her face.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.6": "Hey love. Perfect spot for a romantic stroll, don't you think? Just us and all this natural beauty.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.7": "We should bring tea next time. Or cocoa.$0#$b#You, me, and a little thermos between the ferns. Sounds perfect.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.8": "I was thinking about building us a little bench out here.  Somewhere we could come when we need to escape from everything else.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.9": "This place is perfect for stargazing. We should come back tonight.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.10": "Hey, babe. You out wandering too? I won’t slow you down. Just good to see your face.",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.11":  "Hey. I’m just taking a minute. I’ll be home before dark. Unless Maple leads me in circles again.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.12": "Every now and then, I still can’t believe I live in a place where this view.#$b#And you.#$b#Exist in the same space.$1",
  "Daulton.ForestSpouse.13": "Maple keeps following squirrels that are twice her size. It’s like living with a tiny, reckless knight.$1",
  
  // BEACH LINES//
  "Daulton.Beach.1": "Willy's teaching me some old fishing tricks. Guy knows more about the ocean than anyone.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.2": "Nothing like the smell of salt water and fresh fish. Takes some getting used to, but I love it now.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.3": "Beats sitting in some stuffy Zuzu City office.$1",
  "Daulton.Beach.4": "Willy's got stories for days. Half of them might even be true.$1",
  "Daulton.Beach.5": "Ocean's always changing. Keeps the job interesting, never know what you'll find.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.6": "Willy says the tide’s got moods. Today it feels...twitchy. Good for fishing, bad for dock repairs.",
  "Daulton.Beach.7": "Dock work keeps you in shape. All that lifting and hauling adds up.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.8": "Dock life suits me. Simple, straightforward, connected to something bigger than yourself.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.9":"Working with my hands feels right. Better than pushing papers around an office.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.10": "You ever smell saltwater and immediately crave fries? No? Just me?",
  "Daulton.Beach.11": "I patched a net this morning that looked like it got into a bar fight with a swordfish. Fun stuff.",
  "Daulton.Beach.12": "Willy's got me fixing up some of the dock equipment. Good thing I like working with my hands.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.13": "Salt air and honest work. This is the life I was looking for when I left Zuzu.$1",
  "Daulton.Beach.14": "Waves are calm today. Makes me nervous. The ocean’s rarely polite without a reason.",
  "Daulton.Beach.15": "Dock work's honest labor. You can see what you've accomplished at the end of the day.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.16": "Working with Willy's been great. Guy's got decades of experience to share.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.17": "Been fixing some of the older equipment. Good practice for my tinkering skills.$0",
  "Daulton.Beach.18": "Willy says I'm getting the hang of dock work. Feels good to earn his respect.$1",
  "Daulton.Beach.19": "If you see Maple, tell her driftwood is not food. She doesn’t listen to me anymore.",
  "Daulton.Beach.20": "Willy's been in a weird mood today. I think the crabs stole his lunch again.",
  "Daulton.Beach.21": "Caught a strange fish this morning. Had teeth. Too many teeth.$0#$b#I put it back.",
  "Daulton.Beach.22": "A jellyfish washed up earlier. Maple tried to challenge it to a duel. Don’t worry, she’s fine.",
  "Daulton.Beach.23": "Got up before dawn today. The sunrise over the water almost made it worth it.",
  "Daulton.Beach.24": "Maple tried to follow me to work today. Had to bribe her back home with a carrot.",
  "Daulton.Beach.25": "You’d think working with fish would kill your appetite. Hasn’t happened yet.",
  "Daulton.Beach.26":"There’s a crab under the pier with a mean look in its eye. We’ve got...history.",
  "Daulton.Beach.27": "You ever just sit and watch the tide roll in until you forget why you’re there? Happens more than I admit.",
  "Daulton.Beach.28": "I’m not great at sitting still, but something about the shore makes it easier.",
  "Daulton.Beach.29": "Some days the water looks like glass. Others, it looks ready to eat your boots. Today’s...in between.$0",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.1": "Well hello there, gorgeous. Perfect timing. Just finished up some dock work. Mind keeping me company while I wrap up?$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.2": "Look what the tide brought in. My favorite person in the whole valley. Come to check on your hardworking husband?$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.3": "There's that smile I love. You know how to make even a long day at the docks feel like paradise, @.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.4": "My spouse, looking beautiful as always. Want to steal me away for a romantic walk along the shore?$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.5": "Perfect timing, love. Just taking a break from helping Willy.$0#$b#How about we find a quiet spot on the beach and catch up?$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.6": "Hey gorgeous. Come to see your man in action? I love that you always know where to find me.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.7": "Look who wandered down to the docks.$0#$b#You make this whole place brighter just by being here, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.8": "Hey love. Ocean's beautiful today, but you're still the best view around here. Mind if I steal a kiss before I get back to work?$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.9": "Perfect. I was just thinking about you.$0#$b#Funny how you always seem to show up right when I'm missing you most.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.10": "There's that face I love waking up to. Come here and let me show you what I've been working on today.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.11": "My gorgeous spouse, gracing the docks with their presence. You know, Willy's gonna be jealous I get to go home to you every night.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.12": "Look what wandered into my workplace.$0#$b#The most beautiful person in the valley, coming to check on their hardworking husband.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.13": "Hey, love. Sun’s got a bite today.#$b#Don’t forget to hydrate.$0",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.14": "You make this job feel less like work. Even if all you do is wave from the pier.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.15": "Hey, sweetheart. I know I joke a lot, but seeing you right now just made my day a whole lot better.$4",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.16": "If I catch a big one today, it’s yours. Unless it's horrifying.#$b#Then it’s going right back.$0",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.17": "There's my favorite reason to look forward to going home. Though seeing you here makes work feel a lot more enjoyable.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.18": "Hey beautiful. Just the person I wanted to see. Ocean's nice, but having you here makes it perfect, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.19": "Look who decided to visit me at work. Willy's gonna wonder why I'm grinning like an idiot now, @.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.20": "My spouse, making the whole beach jealous. Come here and let me show you off to the seagulls.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.21": "Look what the ocean brought me today. My favorite treasure washed up right here on the docks.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.22": "There's my better half, brightening up the whole coastline. Want to stick around while I finish up? I work better with an audience this gorgeous.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.23": "Got roped into untangling nets again. If I don’t come home, assume I’ve been eaten by seaweed.",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.24": "If this dock collapses, just know I love you and it’s absolutely my fault.$1",
  "Daulton.BeachSpouse.25": "Don’t worry, I’ll finish up soon. Just needed one more look at you before I get back to it.$1",

  // MOUNTAIN LINES//
  
  "Daulton.Mountain.1": "Perfect spot for some mountain lake fishing. Water's always clearer up here than down at the beach.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.2": "I've been running with the Guild lately. Gil’s...a character. But he knows his stuff.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.3": "Mountain air hits different. Crisp and clean, nothing like the city smog I used to breathe.$1",
  "Daulton.Mountain.4": "Those mine shafts look interesting. Wonder what kind of monsters are lurking down there.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.5": "Mountain's got that rugged feel to it. Makes you want to test yourself against something wild.$1",
  "Daulton.Mountain.6": "Lake fishing's different from ocean fishing. Both have their charm, but this is more meditative.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.7": "I still catch myself staring at the Guild some mornings. Feels good to be part of something that matters.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.8": "Mountain lake's perfect for catching some of the more unusual fish. Always full of surprises.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.9": "This lake’s colder than it looks. Found that out the hard way once. Ask me how.$1",
  "Daulton.Mountain.10": "Sometimes I bring Maple up here to the mines.$0#$b#She gets spooked by the echo, but she still follows me in.$1",
  "Daulton.Mountain.11":  "Mountain lake's perfect for some serious fishing. Way more peaceful than the ocean.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.12":  "Mountain lake's crystal clear. Perfect for seeing what's swimming around down there.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.13": "Mountain's got that rugged appeal. Makes you want to explore every trail and cave.$1",
  "Daulton.Mountain.14": "Mountain lake's got some serious depth to it. Who knows what's swimming around down there.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.15": "Lake's got good fishing today. Sometimes you need a break from the ocean routine.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.16": "Been thinking about exploring deeper into the mines. Could be some interesting finds down there.$0",
  "Daulton.Mountain.17": "I found a broken helmet near the mine shaft once. Makes you wonder how deep that place really goes.$3",
  "Daulton.Mountain.18": "Linus offered me some kind of root tea this morning. Tasted like moss and regret.#$b#But I feel great.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.1": "Perfect. I was hoping you'd show up. Mountain lake's romantic enough, but it's perfect with you here, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.2": "If I don’t come home tonight, it means the mines won...or I got distracted by a really shiny rock.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.3": "Look what the mountain brought me today. My gorgeous spouse, right when I needed some good company up here.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.4": "If you're heading down to the mines, take it slow. I like you in one piece.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.5": "Brought Maple up here to let her hop around. She made friends with a pinecone. I didn’t ask questions.$5",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.6": "You working today? Try not to outshine the mountains too much.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.7": "The lake’s calm today. Almost makes you forget there are things underground that want to bite you.$2",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.8": "Maple kept pulling my sleeve until I followed her to this little patch of wildflowers. Smart rabbit.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.9": "Hey...check in later, yeah? Just so I know the mountain didn’t swallow you whole.$2",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.10": "I’d come with you, but I promised Maple we’d sit here and do absolutely nothing.$0",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.11": "Maple tried to chase a dragonfly straight into the lake. Now we’re both damp and pretending it didn’t happen.$5",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.12": "You heading up to the mines, or just wandering like me? Either way, good luck. And don’t trip on anything ancient.$0",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.13": "If Maple starts following you instead of me, I won’t be offended. Just slightly betrayed.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.14": "Hello, sweetheart.$0#$b#If you're out here chasing monsters in the mines, I hope they know they're outclassed today.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.15": "Maple brought me a pine needle and looked proud about it.$0#$b#I acted impressed. She earned it.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.16": "If you find anything shiny in the caves, I’m not saying you have to give it to me. But I am winking suggestively.$0",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.17": "Sometimes I wonder what would’ve happened if I never left Zuzu.$0#$b#Then you walk by, and I stop wondering.$4",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.18": "Well hello there, beautiful. Come to keep me company? The mountain is peaceful.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.19": "Look who decided to join me for some mountain air. Perfect timing. I was just thinking about how much I missed you, @.$1",
  "Daulton.MountainSpouse.20": "If you need help hauling anything later, say the word. I’m not just here for my winning personality.$1",  

  // WEATHER //
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.1": "Love days like this, @. Rain gives us an excuse to just stay inside and enjoy each other's company.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.2": "Rainy days are the best.$0#$b#No pressure to go anywhere, just us and whatever we want to do, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.3": "Days like this remind me why I love having you around, @. Cozy weather, cozy company.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.4": "Rain's perfect for tinkering in my workshop.$0#$b#Want to keep me company while I work on something?$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.5": "Perfect day to stay in and maybe play some games. Rain makes everything feel more relaxed.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.6": "Maple's extra cuddly on rainy days. Smart little girl knows when to take it easy.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.7": "Perfect atmosphere for some quiet time together.$0#$b#Rain's nature's way of telling us to slow down.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.8": "Love how the rain sounds on the roof. Makes everything feel intimate and peaceful, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.9": "I had plans today, believe it or not. Now I'm negotiating with a bunny and a blanket instead.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.10": "I lit a candle. Maple tried to eat it. It’s going well.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.11": "Rain makes me want to just curl up with you and listen to the storm.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.12": "Love how the rain makes everything smell fresh and clean. Like the world's getting a reset.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.13": "Rain's got that hypnotic quality to it.$0#$b#Makes you want to just relax and enjoy the moment.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.14": "Thinking about setting up by the window and just watching the rain with you. Sounds perfect.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.15": "I was going to make pancakes. Then I remembered I’m me, and I didn’t want to poison us both.$3",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyDay.16": "Might take Maple outside in a shoebox just to see how long she lasts. She’s brave until the wind touches her.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.1": "Love how quiet everything gets when it snows. Perfect day for staying inside with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.2": "Snow's beautiful, but it's got nothing on my gorgeous spouse. Come here and keep me warm, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.3": "Maple's loving this snow. She keeps hopping around by the window, watching the flakes fall.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.4": "Perfect day for hot drinks and cold kisses from my beautiful spouse.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.5": "Weather like this makes me want to build a fire and just hold you all day, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.6": "Maple saw the snow and immediately retreated under the bed. Smart bunny.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.7": "I should’ve built a snow fort. You and me on snack patrol, Maple as lookout. Maybe next storm.$3",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.8": "I love watching the snow fall. Even if it means shoveling later with a grumpy bunny sidekick.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.9": "Thinking about making some hot chocolate later. Snow days deserve special treats, especially when shared with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.10": "Snow makes me want to work on something creative. Maybe I'll build you something special while we're snowed in.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.11": "Weather like this makes me appreciate the simple things. Warm house, gorgeous spouse, what else do you need?$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.12": "I left some cocoa on the counter for you.$0#$b#It may or may not be mostly marshmallows.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.13": "We could go out and make snow angels...or stay in and pretend we’re responsible adults. Tough call.$3",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyDay.14": "Maple tried to dig a tunnel through the blanket pile. She might be halfway to the desert by now.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.1": "Snow’s coming down steady out there. I’ll keep the bed warm if you’re out late.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.2": "Maple’s asleep, the snow’s quiet, and I’ve got nowhere else I’d rather be than right here with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.3": "Love how snow at night makes our home feel like the only place in the world. Just us against the winter.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.4": "You should’ve seen Maple’s face when the wind hit the window. Pure drama. I taught her well.$3",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.5": "The wind’s howling tonight. Don’t worry.#$b#I checked the windows twice. We’re sealed up tight.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.6": "The snow’s piled high. Don’t worry.#$b#I already did the 'is the roof gonna cave in?' check.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.7": "You in that old hoodie, shuffling through the kitchen in socks? Cutest thing I’ve seen all day.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.8": "You’ve got that sleepy look again.$0#$b#You always get it right before you curl into me like a cat.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.9": "Snow at night makes everything feel intimate and cozy. Perfect time to show my beautiful spouse some attention.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.10": "Love how the snow muffles everything outside. Makes it feel like we're the only two people in the world, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.11": "Love how snow makes the night feel timeless. Like we could stay like this forever, love.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.12": "Come warm your hands. I’m not a heater, but I’m trying real hard to fake it tonight.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.13": "I set out a towel for your boots.$0#$b#Not because I’m neat. I just don’t want to slip and break something trying to kiss you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.SnowyNight.14": "Maple knocked over my toolbox chasing a dust mote. I think she’s just showing off at this point.$3",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.1": "Maple hates the thunder. She’s currently under three blankets and holding a grudge against the sky.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.2": "You’ve got that calm look you get when it rains. I like seeing you like this.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.3": "The goats were restless earlier, but they settled once the rain came down harder. It’s quiet now.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.4": "You looked beautiful coming in from the fields. Damp sleeves, muddy boots... still beautiful.$4",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.5": "I made sure the barn doors were latched before the worst of it came down. Everyone's dry out there.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.6": "You should’ve seen the ducks today. They love this weather.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.7": "It’s been a long day. Feels good to just sit and listen to the rain with you.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.8": "It’s quiet out here in a way Zuzu never was. I don’t miss the noise.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.9": "Maple finally curled up by the stove. Took her a while to calm down.#$b#She’s not a fan of thunder.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.10": "You ever feel like the rain washes the day off your skin? Makes things simpler. Cleaner, maybe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.11": "The way the rain hits the porch roof... I could fall asleep to it every night.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.12": "The fire’s got a good burn going. Maple’s already snoring. I’d say the evening’s going well.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.13": "I’d stay up late with you if you wanted, but if you crawl into bed now, I’m not far behind.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.RainyNight.14": "I’m glad we built this life out here. Nights like this make it feel like the right call.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.Rainy": "You don’t have to rush out there today.$0#$b#The rain’s already taking care of most things. Stay in a little longer with me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.Snowy": "Everything’s blanketed out there. Even the fence posts look soft.$0#$b#You warm enough? I can toss on another log if you want to stay in.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.Rainy": "I like sitting out here when the rain’s light like this.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.Snowy": "The snow’s piled up on the railing again. I should sweep it off, but... kinda don’t want to disturb it yet.$0",

  // SPOUSE ROOM //
  
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.1": "Maple's been hopping around all morning looking for you.$0#$b#Can't blame her...I do the same thing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.2": "Used to sleep wherever I landed. A couch, a cot, the back of a van once. Feels good to have a room that means something.",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.3": "Maple's getting spoiled with all the fresh vegetables from our farm.$0#$b#Lucky bunny gets to live in paradise with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.5": "This room's starting to feel like home.$0#$b#Guess that happens when you're with the right person.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.6": "The guys at the dock keep asking about married life.$0#$b#I just tell them I hit the jackpot.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.7": "Maple's gotten so comfortable here.$0#$b#I know exactly how she feels...this is home with you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.8": "The dock work keeps my hands busy.$0#$b#Leaves my mind free to think about you all day.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.9": "Found some interesting driftwood that might make a good project.$0#$b#Everything reminds me of you lately.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.10": "Been working on this fishing lure design all afternoon.$0#$b#The way you concentrate on your farm work is pretty mesmerizing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.11": "Sandy sent another letter from the desert.$0#$b#She keeps asking when you're both coming to visit again.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.12": "Spent the evening by the river just thinking.$0#$b#Mostly about how lucky I got when you chose me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.13": "Got some Saloon pizza for dinner again.$0#$b#One day I'll learn to cook something decent for you.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.14": "Grabbed some crab cakes from Gus again.$0#$b#Your cooking attempts are still way more impressive than anything I manage.[732]$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.15": "Beat that horror game finally.$0#$b#Now I need to find something else to keep me up too late.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.16":  "Willy's got me fixing nets again.$0#$b#At least the work's honest and the pay's decent.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.17":  "Maple got into my toolbox again.$0#$b#Little troublemaker's got more personality than half the people in town.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.18": "Sam keeps bugging me about jamming together.$0#$b#Might be fun to dust off the drums properly.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.19":  "Caught some decent fish down by the docks today.$0#$b#Thinking about grilling them up...if I can figure out how.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.20": "Arcade was packed with kids today.$0#$b#Made me feel ancient trying to play anything.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.21": "Sandy sent another postcard from the desert.$0#$b#She's living it up out there in all that sand.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.22": "Found this old metal album at the back of my stuff.$0#$b#Takes me back to my Zuzu City days.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.23": "Maple's been extra hyper today.$0#$b#Think she needs more space to run around.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.spouseRoom.24": "This old radio's acting up again.$0#$b#Might be time to actually buy a new one.$1",
  
  
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.1": "Love stepping out here and taking in the view.$1#$b#Though the scenery's even better when you join me.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.2": "Perfect spot for some fresh air and quiet thinking.$0#$b#Want to sit with me for a bit? Could use the company, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.3": "Perfect spot for some stargazing later tonight.$1#$b#Want to join me? We could make it romantic, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.4": "Been enjoying the peace out here.$0#$b#Want to steal a kiss under the open sky? Seems like perfect timing.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.5": "Do you ever get tired of looking at the sky out here? Me neither.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.6": "Maple’s been hopping around the planter boxes. I think she’s claimed this porch as her own.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.7": "The sound of the animals starting up for the day...I never thought I’d like that as much as I do.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.8": "Maple’s been lounging under the tomato plants again. I think she’s pretending to be a wild rabbit.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.9": "I used to be up late every night in Zuzu.$0#$b#Now I’m up early and talking to chickens. Wild, huh?$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.10": "Don’t worry, I already chased off a raccoon. He looked guilty before I even got out here.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.11": "Hey. Don’t let the chores eat up the whole day. You deserve a little sun on your face too.$2",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.12": "I started fixing the fence, but then Maple jumped in my toolbox and fell asleep. Guess it's a tomorrow problem now.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.13": "Maple’s been watching the chickens like she’s guarding them. Not very effective, but I appreciate the effort.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.14": "I tightened the gate hinge this morning. It squeaked one too many times during breakfast.$1",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.15": "Saw a couple deer on the edge of the woods this morning. They looked right at home.$0",
  "Daulton.Marriage.patio.16": "You look good in this light. Just thought you should know that.$4",
  
  // NIGHTMARKET // 

  "Daulton.NightMarket.1": "Love how lively everything gets here at night. Good change of pace for the docks.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.2": "Been checking out the merchants. Some of this stuff is pretty impressive.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.3": "I Love how everything feels more mysterious at night.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.4": "I bought something from that shadowy guy in the corner. No idea what it does, but it looked cool.$2",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.5": "Some of these items are so strange. And I say that as someone who once played drums at a haunted arcade.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.6": "Bought us a snack. No idea what it is. Could be seaweed, could be a dessert. Guess we’ll find out.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.7": "That guy with the beard’s been staring into the water for hours. I’d ask why, but I kinda don’t want to know.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.8": "Been enjoying the music drifting from different stalls.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.9": "I saw someone buy a jar of fog. Not sure if it’s art or a scam. Maybe both.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.10": "Bought something that smells like the ocean and coffee.$0#$b#Might be incense, might be cursed. We’ll find out tonight.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.11": "There’s a musician playing on the far end of the dock. Not bad. Might go listen a while.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.12": "Found a seashell shaped like a rabbit’s ear. Brought it for Maple. She’s gonna be smug about it.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.13": "Submarine makes me appreciate dock work even more. At least there I can jump to dry land if needed.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.14": "Don’t worry, I checked.#$b#Nothing’s cursed. Well, except maybe those little glowing fish pies.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.15": "That seaweed vendor said his wares were harvested with the permission of the waves. You can’t make this stuff up.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.16": "Submarine's amazing tech, don't get me wrong.$0#$b#Just the thought of being that deep underwater makes me nervous.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.17": "There's a vendor offering moon-touched stones.#$b#But I’m pretty sure they're just shiny gravel. Still kinda want one.$0",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.18": "That fortune teller pulled my card and just laughed. Not sure if that’s good or bad.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.19": "That submarine's incredible engineering, but...yeah, no thanks. I'll stick to surface fishing.$2",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.20": "Glad you're here with me tonight. This place is strange in the kind of way I want to share with you.$3",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.21": "You want anything? Weird potion? Singing shell? I’ve got enough gold for something ridiculous.$1",
  "Daulton.NightMarket.22": "You hungry? Some of these booths are serving things I can’t pronounce, but I’ll eat it if you do.$1",
 

  // KID LINES // 
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.1": "%kid1 fell asleep in the middle of building a tower out of turnips. I didn’t move 'em. Seemed like a solid dream.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.2": "Love watching our little one explore everything. Same curiosity I had as a kid, always taking things apart.$1#$b#Hope %kid1 inherits that sense of wonder.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.3": "Been thinking about building %kid1 a little workshop when they're older.$0#$b#Never too early to start learning how to make things with your hands, babe.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.4": "%kid2 and %kid1 are lucky to have each other.$1#$b#And I'm lucky to have this whole beautiful family, including you, love.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.5": "Never thought I'd be this happy just watching kids play.$1#$b#You've given me everything I didn't know I wanted.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.6": "I caught %kid2 trying to teach Maple tricks with a carrot on a string. It...went about how you'd expect.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.7": "Sometimes I think %kid2 might be more stubborn than both of us combined. Which is saying something.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.8": "%kid1 drew a picture of me with a fish for a head. I’d be insulted if it wasn’t kinda accurate.$2",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.9": "%kid1 and %kid2 were arguing over whether Maple should get a birthday party. I said yes. Maple seemed indifferent.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.10": "%kid1 made me a bracelet out of string and old buttons. I’m never taking it off. Not even to fish.$4",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.11": "It's wild how fast they grow. I blink, and %kid1’s already bossing Maple around like they own the place.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.12": "They’ve got your eyes, you know. Every time they smile like that, it hits me all over again.$4",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.13": "Teaching %kid1 about music already. Little hands on the drums, just like their old man.$1#$b#You should see their face light up when they make a good beat, @.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.14": "Maple's been so patient with the kids. Smart bunny knows they're part of the family now.$1#$b#%kid1 loves feeding her hay. Good to see them learning compassion early.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.15": "%kid2 fell asleep to my drumming last night. Guess they've got good taste in music already.$1#$b#Takes after their parents, obviously, love.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.16":  "Never knew how much I'd love being a dad until it happened.$1#$b#You and the kids...you've made my life complete, @.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.17": "Teaching %kid1 to be gentle with animals. Important lesson for life, not just with Maple.$1#$b#Want them to grow up respectful of all living things.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.18": "%kid2 tried to 'help' me fix something yesterday. Made twice the mess but had twice the fun.$1#$b#That's what childhood should be about.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.19": "Maple’s weirdly patient with %kid1.$0#$b#I think the bunny sees ‘em as some kind of apprentice.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.20":" Kids make you see everything through fresh eyes.$1#$b#Even the simplest things become adventures when you're sharing them with %kid1 and %kid2.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.21": "%kid2 wanted to come to the docks with me. Told ‘em the sea’s too rough today. They gave me the same look you do when I say no to pie.$3",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.22": "Maple's appointed herself as the kids' protector. Follows them everywhere.$1#$b#Good to know our bunny's got their backs when we're not around.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.23": "You were right—%kid1 totally inherited your stubborn streak. I tried to get them to nap. I failed.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.24": "Never thought I'd be the type to get sentimental, but watching %kid1 grow up...$1#$b#Changes a man's perspective on everything.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.25": "Kids are natural explorers. %kid1 and %kid2 find magic in things I'd walk right past.$1#$b#They keep me young, that's for sure.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.26": "We built a little fort in the living room. %kid1 called it the Bunny Bunker. I think Maple’s claimed it as hers now.$2",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.27": "Sometimes I catch 'em staring out at the fields like they're thinking deep thoughts. Then they ask if cows can be pirates.$1",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.28": "Taught %kid2 how to bait a hook today. They said it felt ‘mean to the worm.’ Hard to argue with that.$0",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.29": "%kid1 wanted to start a ‘rock band’ with spoons and empty jars. Maple was their only fan. Still, not a bad start.$2",
  "Daulton.MarriageDialogueKids.30": "%kid1 tried to ‘help’ water the crops. The crops got wet. So did I. So did Maple.$5",
  
  //EVENT//

   // Daulton 2-heart dialogue
  "daulton2hearts.01": "Oi! Get that rabbit away from me fish!$2",
  "daulton2hearts.02": "Maple! No! Bad bunny! Those aren't for you!$6",
  "daulton2hearts.03": "Sorry about that, Willy. She's just...endlessly curious.#$b#She thinks everything is either food or a toy. Sometimes both.$5",
  "daulton2hearts.04": "I understand, laddy. She's got a good eye for fish.$1",
  "daulton2hearts.question1": "She's adorable! What's her story?",
  "daulton2hearts.question2": "You should keep her under control.",
  "daulton2hearts.05": "Yeah, well, tell that to my drumsticks. Or what's left of them.$h#$b#She's got a thing for chewing on wooden things. Discovered that the hard way.$5",
  "daulton2hearts.rabbit.01": "Brought her with me from Zuzu. Only roommate who could stand my late-night drum practice.$h#$b#Though 'stand' might be generous. She mostly just thumped back.",
  "daulton2hearts.06": "Maple’s basically my apprentice.#$b#Though she’s better at making a mess than anything else.$h#$b#I’ve been working the docks for a while now.#$b#It’s honest work, and I get to stay near the ocean without setting foot in it$1",
  "daulton2hearts.07": "Lad's the best dock worker I've had.$1",
  "daulton2hearts.08": "Someone's gotta stay on solid ground to catch all the fish you throw up here, right?$h",
  "daulton2hearts.question3": "So you don't fish at all?",
  "daulton2hearts.question4": "Isn't that the whole point of working by the sea?",
  "daulton2hearts.09": "I'll leave the boat stuff to folks braver.#$b#Or dumber.#$b#Than me.$h#$b#Let’s just say I prefer the kind of fishing where I can still see land.",
  "daulton2hearts.nofish.01": "Fishing? From the shore, maybe. But boats and me...$s#$b#Let's just say we don't get along.$2",
  "daulton2hearts.nofish.02": "Don't look at me like that. We all have our things, right?#$b#Mine just happens to involve staying where I can't drown.",
  "daulton2hearts.10": "Well, come on, troublemaker. Let’s get you away from Willy’s stock before he decides we’re both more trouble than we’re worth.$1",
  "daulton2hearts.11": "Nice chatting with you, @.#$b#If you ever need help lifting something heavy or finding a rabbit, I’m your guy.$h",
  "daulton2hearts.12": "And if Maple goes hopping through town again, just steer her back this way.#$b#She’s got a sixth sense for snacks and absolutely zero sense of direction.$1",
  "daulton2hearts.end": "Maybe I should build Maple a leash...or a tiny boat anchor. Or just accept that I’ve been domesticated by a rabbit.$0",

  
 // Daulton 3-heart dialogue

  "daulton3hearts.01": "Come on, Maple. Let's check out the town square.#$b#No, wait! Not there!",
  "daulton3hearts.02": "Oh my! Is that a rabbit in my petunias?!$2",
  "daulton3hearts.03": "Maple! Bad bunny! Those aren't for you!$6#$b#I am so sorry, Evelyn. She usually stays right by my side, but she saw your flowers and ...$2",
  "daulton3hearts.04": "Young man, do you know how long it took me to grow those?#$b#I just planted those petunias last week!$2",
  "daulton3hearts.05": "I know, I know. She's got expensive taste, apparently.$5#$b#Look, I'll pay for new flowers. And I'll help you replant them myself.$0",
  "daulton3hearts.question1": "She's just being a bunny, Evelyn.",
  "daulton3hearts.question2": "Maybe use a fence next time?",
  "daulton3hearts.06": "Yeah, well, this 'just a bunny' has a real talent for finding the most expensive things to nibble on.$2#$b#Last week it was Gus's herb garden. Cost me a week's wages.$2",
  "daulton3hearts.apologize.01": "Thanks for understanding, @. But Evelyn's right to be upset.$s#$b#Part of being a responsible pet owner is... well, being responsible.",
  "daulton3hearts.07": "Well... at least she has good taste. Those were my prized petunias.$2",
  "daulton3hearts.08": "See? Even Evelyn admits you've got style, buddy.$1#$b#...Though maybe we stick to the clover patches from now on?",
  "daulton3hearts.09": "Oh, don't worry about paying, dear. But I will take you up on that replanting offer.#$b##My old knees aren't what they used to be.$0",
  "daulton3hearts.10": "Absolutely! This weekend work for you?#$b#I'll bring my good trowel. And maybe some chicken wire...$1",
  "daulton3hearts.11": "You know, George had a rabbit when he was young. 'Pepper,' I think.#$b#Ate through my mother-in-law's entire vegetable garden one summer!$1",
  "daulton3hearts.12": "Ha! See, Maple? You come from a long line of troublemakers.$1#$b#Though between you and me, I think she just knows quality when she sees it.$1",
  "daulton3hearts.question3": "She IS pretty cute...",
  "daulton3hearts.question4": "Why do you walk her around town?",
  "daulton3hearts.13": "Bunnies need exercise and mental stimulation, just like dogs.#$b#Plus, she gets depressed if she's cooped up all day. We've been doing these walks since I moved here from Zuzu.",
  "daulton3hearts.cute.01": "Right? How can you stay mad at this face?$1#$b#...Don't answer that. I've asked myself the same question every time I find a new hole in my socks.$1",
  "daulton3hearts.14": "Well, just try to keep her out of the flowers from now on, dear.#$b#Though I must admit, she is rather adorable.$1",
  "daulton3hearts.15": "Will do. Come on, troublemaker. Let's get you home before you find Pierre's rare seed display.$0",
  "daulton3hearts.16": "Bad bunny. You're getting plain pellets for dinner. No banana chips.$6#$b#...Okay, maybe just one banana chip.$1",
  "daulton3hearts.17": "Thanks for backing me up, @. Most people think I'm weird for walking around with a bunny.$1#$b#But hey, at least I never have a dull moment with this fluffball around.$1",
  "daulton3hearts.end": "Note to self: Evelyn's petunias are Maple's new favorite snack. Must plan routes accordingly.$0",
  
  // Daulton 4-heart dialogue

  "daulton4hearts.01": "Oh, hey @. Good timing.#$b#Come on in.#$b#Just be quiet, Maple's in the middle of her nap. Never misses it.$1",
  "daulton4hearts.02": "I was just... well, trying to figure out what to do with this.$s",
  "daulton4hearts.03": "It's my dad's old compass. Found it in a box of his things last week.#$b#The brass is all tarnished, and the needle's stuck. Probably hasn't worked right in years.$2",
  "daulton4hearts.04": "I keep thinking I should fix it, but...$s",
  "daulton4hearts.05": "This compass guided him for over thirty years. And here I am... What would he think of his son now?$2",
  "daulton4hearts.question1": "You should honor his memory. Get it restored.",
  "daulton4hearts.question2": "Maybe you're not meant to follow his path.",
  "daulton4hearts.06": "Honor his memory...$0#$b#Yeah. Yeah, maybe you're right. He loved this old thing.$1",
  "daulton4hearts.07": "Maybe Gus knows someone who could fix it up. Or Clint might have some ideas.#$b#I could keep it on my desk. I don't know. Keep his spirit alive somehow.$1",
  "daulton4hearts.ownpath.01": "My own path...$0#$b#You know, I've been so focused on what I couldn't do, I forgot about what I have done.$0",
  "daulton4hearts.ownpath.02": "I mean, I'm in the Adventurer's Guild. I've got Maple. Good friends like you.#$b#Maybe it's okay that my life looks different than Dad's.$0",
  "daulton4hearts.08": "And look who's awake! Hey girl, did we disturb your beauty sleep?$h",
  "daulton4hearts.09": "Sometimes I think this little bunny understands me better than most people.#$b#She doesn't care about any of that. She just wants her hay and head scratches.$1",
  "daulton4hearts.10": "Thanks for listening, @. It helps, talking about this stuff.#$b#Want to stay for a bit? I was about to make some coffee, and Maple always enjoys the company.$1",
  "daulton4hearts.end": "That compass is heavier than it looks.$s#$b#I'm not sure if that's a good or bad thing.",


  // Daulton 6-heart dialogue

  "daulton6hearts.01": "Thanks for coming out to the pier tonight, @. I’ve been meaning to talk to someone about...why I left Zuzu.",
  "daulton6hearts.03": "It was my dad’s old shipping route. He worked on the steam freighters out of Zuzu City.$0#$b#After he... he passed last year, I figured I’d take over his route to keep feeling close to him.$2",
  "daulton6hearts.05": "I thought I’d follow in his footsteps, but I got seasick just watching the waves.$0#$b#I made it about an hour into training before I puked on the captain’s clipboard. Didn’t even get offshore.$1",
  "daulton6hearts.07": "Funny, right? I’d sit on the boat’s edge casting my line, but the moment I drifted past waist-deep water, I’d panic and haul back to shallow sands.$2",
  "daulton6hearts.09": "So I walked off the dock and never looked back.$0#$b#Maple hated that boat smell too. She was wriggling so much I thought she’d escape my bag.$2",
  "daulton6hearts.11": "I realized I wanted to be near water without actually being in it...$0#$b#And then Willy gave me a gig here. Turns out, building a quieter life takes more courage than I expected.$0",
  "daulton6hearts.13": "Sometimes I wonder if I’m letting Dad down. He’d hate the idea of me living in fear of waves.$2#$b#I guess working at the dock was my way of honoring Dad without ending up overboard.$2",
  "daulton6hearts.15": "But then I think...he wouldn’t want me green in the face and terrified on deck. He’d want me to find a way to stay close without a panic attack.$0",
  "daulton6hearts.16": "That’s why I’m here. Tide comes in, tide goes out, but I’m not bouncing around like a speck in the sea.$2",
  "daulton6hearts.17": "Thanks for listening, by the way. Saying it out loud helps. A little.$4",
  "daulton6hearts.18": "But, enough about the past! Tonight’s calm. And I’ve got good company.$1",
  "daulton6hearts.19": "Listen, I brought two rods. Fish with me for a bit?$0",
  "daulton6hearts.21": "Maple’s already hunting crabs somewhere on shore.$1#$b#She’s my little lookout. If I start looking pale, she nips my shoe and drags me back.$1",
  "daulton6hearts.29": "Let’s set up here, under the lamp. The tide’s calm, and we can just watch the horizon shift.$0",
  "daulton6hearts.31": "Let's see if you can outfish me.$1",

  // Farmer choice prompts
  "daulton6hearts.choice1a": "I’m listening.",
  "daulton6hearts.choice1b": "Go ahead, I’m here.",
  "daulton6hearts.choice2a": "That’s smart of Maple.",
  "daulton6hearts.choice2b": "She sounds like a good buddy.",
  "daulton6hearts.resp1": "I don't know where I would be without Maple.$1",


  "daulton8hearts.01": "Daulton! The crab pots need checkin' on the far side. Take the boat, lad.",
  "daulton8hearts.02": "Willy, you know I don't... I can't do the boat thing.$6",
  "daulton8hearts.03": "Ah, @! Maybe ye can talk some sense into him. Boy works at a dock but won't get in a boat!",
  "daulton8hearts.04": "Hey @... Willy's trying to get me killed again.$s#$b#And you know it's not that simple, Willy.$s#$b#@, you remember what I told you about my dad?$2",
  "daulton8hearts.05": "Aye, his father was a good man. Worked the freighters for thirty years.",
  "daulton8hearts.06": "And I couldn't even make it past the harbor. Some legacy, huh?$0#$b#I mean, I want to get over it. I really do.$s#$b#How am I supposed to explore underwater caves for the Guild if I can't even get in a boat?$s",
  "daulton8hearts.07": "You know what?$s#$b#Maybe... maybe it's time.$s#$b#Dad's been gone over a year now. I can't keep running from this...$0",
  "daulton8hearts.question1": "You don't have to prove anything.",
  "daulton8hearts.question2": "Your dad would understand.",
  "daulton8hearts.08": "Maybe not to anyone else, but... to myself? Yeah, I do.",
  "daulton8hearts.understanding.01": "Thanks. That... that means a lot.$l#$b#But I think he'd also want me to at least try to face this.$1",
  "daulton8hearts.09": "Every time I see a boat, I think about that day. The captain's face when I couldn't stop shaking.$s#$b#'Maybe the sea life isn't for everyone, kid.' That's what he said.$2",
  "daulton8hearts.10": "But Dad loved the water. Said it was in our blood.#$b#Maybe if I just... if I could just get out there once without panicking...$0",
  "daulton8hearts.11": "@, would you come with me? Just... just to the first buoy and back?#$b#I know it's stupid, but I feel like with you there, maybe I could do it.$0",
  "daulton8hearts.question3": "Let's do this together.",
  "daulton8hearts.question4": "I don't think you're ready.",
  "daulton8hearts.12": "Together. Yeah. Okay.$0#$b#Just... if I turn green, don't laugh too hard?$1",
  "daulton8hearts.13": "Oh Yoba. The dock's getting smaller. That means we're moving. We're actually moving.$2",
  "daulton8hearts.14": "Don't think about the depth. Don't think about the waves.$2#$b#I'm stronger than this. I fight slimes! I've been blown up by my own inventions at least twelve times!$s#$b#No. No, I'm gonna think about Dad instead.",
  "daulton8hearts.15": "He used to tell me stories about the sunrise over the water. How peaceful it was before the day's work started.$0#$b#I... I think I'm starting to see what he meant.$0",
  "daulton8hearts.16": "The way the light hits the waves... He said it looked like scattered diamonds.$l#$b#I always thought he was being poetic, but... he was right.$1",
  "daulton8hearts.17": "You know what? I'm doing it. I'm actually on the water.$1#$b#Dad, if you're watching... I finally made it out here.$1",
  "daulton8hearts.18": "I might not be able to work the freighters like you did. I might always get seasick past the shallows.$s#$b#But I'm here. And that's... that's something, right?$0",
  "daulton8hearts.19": "Thank you, @. For being here. For not letting me do this alone.$l#$b#I couldn't have faced this without you.$1",
  "daulton8hearts.20": "We did it. We actually did it! I rode in a boat without completely falling apart!$1",
  "daulton8hearts.21": "I mean, I'm definitely having a drink when we get back, and Maple's getting extra treats for being patient...$h#$b#But I did it. Dad would be... I think he'd be proud.$1",
  "daulton8hearts.end": "I finally got in a boat today. It wasn't pretty, but I did it. Maybe Dad's watching and smiling.$l",
  "daulton8hearts.noboat.01": "Yeah... yeah, you're probably right.$s",
  "daulton8hearts.noboat.02": "Sorry for putting you on the spot like that. It's just...$s#$b#Sometimes I think if I had someone with me, it'd be different.$0",
  "daulton8hearts.noboat.03": "Maybe I'll try again someday. When it doesn't feel like I'm drowning just thinking about it.$s#$b#I should get back to work. Those crates won't move themselves.$s",
  "daulton8hearts.noboat.end": "Dad, I'm sorry. I'm still not ready. Maybe someday.$s",

  "daulton10hearts.01": "Hey, you actually came!$h#$b#I, uh... I tied the note to Maple and just kinda hoped she'd find you. Probably not my most reliable delivery method.",
  "daulton10hearts.02": "I've been out here for a while getting everything ready.#$b#Had to bribe Maple with an entire bag of banana chips to stay home. We'll see how long that lasts.$h",
  "daulton10hearts.03": "Lately, I’ve been thinking about how different things feel with you around.$l#$b#It’s not about where we are or what we’re doing.#$b#Just the fact that you’re part of it.$4",
  "daulton10hearts.04": "I've been sneaking out here at night. Sitting by the water, trying to make peace with it.#$b#Turns out it's not so bad when you're not actively panicking.$1",
  "daulton10hearts.05": "Back in Zuzu, everything was just... noise. Concrete and strangers and going through the motions.#$b#I had my drums and Maple, but that was it. No one really saw me, you know?",
  "daulton10hearts.06": "Then I come here, meet you, and suddenly someone's actually paying attention.$0#$b#There’s this calm I get when you’re near. Like I don’t have to keep bracing for something to go wrong.$l#$b#I didn’t realize how much I needed that until you.$4",
  "daulton10hearts.07": "And you're still here. You never made me feel stupid for any of it. You just... stayed.$4",
  "daulton10hearts.08": "Look, I'm gonna be straight with you. I'm not good at the whole romantic speech thing...#$b#But I'm pretty sure I'm falling for you. Like, really falling. And I need to know if I'm alone in this.$4",
  "daulton10hearts.question1": "(Kiss him)",
  "daulton10hearts.question2": "I think we should stay friends.",
  "daulton10hearts.09": "Oh... oh man. That was...$4#$b#Why did I wait so long to tell you?",
  "daulton10hearts.10": "I built up this whole speech in my head, but now? All I can think about is how much I want to kiss you again.$4",
  "daulton10hearts.11": "And of course she shows up now! Maple, you little spy!$h#$b#I specifically gave you the good hay so you'd stay home!$5",
  "daulton10hearts.12": "Though I guess if the little troublemaker approves, we're doing something right.$h#$b#Come here. I brought drinks and blankets. Let's just... be together for a while. Watch the stars. No more speeches, I promise.$l",
  "daulton10hearts.end": "Still can't believe tonight happened. Even Maple's approval feels like a good sign.$l",
  "daulton10hearts.nokiss.01": "Oh. Right. Yeah, no, totally. Friends is... friends is good.$s",
  "daulton10hearts.nokiss.02": "Sorry, I... I thought maybe... Doesn't matter.$s#$b#Forget I said anything.",
  "daulton10hearts.nokiss.03": "It's getting pretty late anyway. Should probably check on Maple before she eats through my sock drawer again.$s",
  "daulton10hearts.nokiss.end": "Friends it is. I'm cool with that. Totally cool.$s",

  
  "daulton14hearts.01": "Hey, you made it! I was starting to think Maple ate my note again.$h#$b#Look at her pretending to be innocent. I saw you eyeing that paper, missy.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.02": "Been out here since sunrise just... taking it all in. The water's so clear you can see straight to the bottom.$l#$b#Dad would've loved this place.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.03": "You know what's funny? I think I love this place too.",
  "daulton14hearts.04": "Oh, that reminds me. Got a letter from Marlon yesterday.#$b#Look's like my membership in the Guild is going permanent. Turns out that glowing moss I found in the volcano really impressed him.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.question1": "I'm so proud of you.",
  "daulton14hearts.question2": "What about the underwater caves?",
  "daulton14hearts.05": "Ha, yeah... those are still on my 'eventually' list.$h#$b#Baby steps, right? I can handle a boat now. Diving's the next mountain to climb.",
  "daulton14hearts.proud.01": "Thanks you. Means everything coming from you.$l#$b#You're the one who helped me get here. Who saw more in me than just the dock worker with the pet rabbit.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.06": "Full member of the Adventurer's Guild. Daulton the monster hunter.#$b#Dad might not have gotten his sailor, but I think... I think he'd be proud anyway.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.07": "Hey, come here. I have something for you.",
  "daulton14hearts.08": "I found these growing wild near the resort. Thought they looked perfect for this moment.#$b#Land flowers on a sea island. Kinda like us, right?$l",
  "daulton14hearts.09": "You helped me find the courage to face my fears. To build a life that honors where I came from while being true to who I am.#$b#I love you. So much.$4",
  "daulton14hearts.10": "And there goes our romantic moment! Maple, girl, you've got terrible timing. Again.$h",
  "daulton14hearts.11": "You know what? Let's follow her. Tide's perfect for clamming right now.#$b#We can dig up dinner, maybe find some sea glass. Make a whole morning of it.",
  "daulton14hearts.12": "Besides, I want to show you this tide pool I found yesterday. There's an octopus living in it.$h#$b#Come on. Adventure awaits, beauitful.$1",
  "daulton14hearts.end": "Sun, sea, you, and one sandy rabbit. This is the life.$1",


  // Maple Move-in Event
  "event.maple-move-in.daulton1": "Maple, look at this place! Isn't it amazing?$1",
  "event.maple-move-in.daulton2": "Look how excited she is! She's going to love living here with us!$1",
  "event.maple-move-in.daulton3": "Oh, I almost forgot! I got Maple a special treat to celebrate.$0",
  "event.maple-move-in.daulton5": "Aww, look at her! She's so happy!$4#$b#Welcome to your new home, Maple.$1",
  "event.maple-move-in.daulton6": "I'll set out her bowls and leave a note with her feeding schedule and favorite snacks.$1",
  "event.maple-move-in.message": "Maple has moved into the farmhouse!",

  // Mini Foraging Event // 

  "daulton.foraging.01": "Hmm... roots are deeper than usual this year.",
  "daulton.foraging.02": "Oh. @.$u#$b#Didn't hear you coming. Maple usually warns me.",
  "daulton.foraging.03": "She's... occupied.$5",
  "daulton.foraging.04": "Found something worth celebrating, apparently.",
  "daulton.foraging.05": "Wild horseradish. Spring root.$u#$b#Ever tried one? They're pretty good!$1",
  "daulton.foraging.06": "Here. I've got more than I need.",
  "daulton.foraging.07": "Spring's decent for foraging. Less work than actual farming.$h",
  "daulton.foraging.08": "She's getting restless. Probably smells something else worth...uh, investigating.",
  "daulton.foraging.09": "You can tag along sometime.$h#$b#If you don't mind getting your hands dirty.",
  "daulton.foraging.10": "Just don't tell Maple. She thinks this is our thing.",
  "daulton.foraging.11": "Yeah, yeah. You heard that.$5",
  "daulton.foraging.12": "See you around, @.$1",
  "daulton.foraging.message": "You feel like you've learned something about foraging... and about Daulton.",

  // Mini Saloon Event // 
  "daulton.saloon.sam1": "Ugh... I lost that level...",
  "daulton.saloon.gus1": "Evening, Daulton. The usual?$h",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton1": "Yeah. And maybe some water for Maple.$u",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton14": "Hey, Marlon. Check this out.",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton2": "Pulled this out of Skull Cavern on my day off. Prime bait stock.$h",
  "daulton.saloon.gus2": "Is that... is that BUG MEAT? On my BAR?!$a",
  "daulton.saloon.marlon1": "Cave beetle. Big one, by the look of it.$0",
  "daulton.saloon.clint1": "Gross...",
  "daulton.saloon.shane2": "Whoa...",
  "daulton.saloon.leah2": "Is that...?",
  "daulton.saloon.clint2": "You actually fight those things?$s",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton3": "Dock work keeps the lights on, Clint. Guild runs keep me from getting rusty.$h",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton4": "Besides, they drop decent loot sometimes.$h",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton5": "Maple, no.$a",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton6": "Not a snack, girl.",
  "daulton.saloon.marlon2": "Sorry, Gus. He should’ve taken that to Gil, not your bar. He’s not flashy, but he gets it done.$0",
  "daulton.saloon.marlon3": "Takes steady nerves to hunt beetles in the deep caves.$0",
  "daulton.saloon.gus3": "Could you please... remove that from my workspace?$s",
  "daulton.saloon.gus4": "My poor bar...",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton7": "Right. Sorry, Gus.",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton8": "Forgot not everyone appreciates the finer points of monster hunting.$h",
  "daulton.saloon.clint3": "How much do those things sell for anyway?",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton9": "Enough to make the risk worth it! And I like the quiet down there. Just me and whatever's trying to bite me.$u",
  "daulton.saloon.gus5": "Here. On the house.$s",
  "daulton.saloon.gus6": "For... services to the community.$s",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton10": "Appreciate it, Gus.$u",
  "daulton.saloon.maple1": "*sniff sniff*",
  "daulton.saloon.marlon4": "Keep up the good work, adventurer.$0",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton11": "You know I will.$h",
  "daulton.saloon.shane1": "Better than working retail, I guess.",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton12": "It works for me. Bit of both keeps it from getting dull.",
  "daulton.saloon.daulton13": "Come on, Maple. Let's find you something that won't give Gus nightmares.",
  "daulton.saloon.gus7": "Monster parts...",
  "daulton.saloon.sam2": "I lost again!",
  "daulton.saloon.marlon5": "Keep the Guild posted. And maybe give folks a heads-up before slapping bug guts on the bar.$0",
  "daulton.saloon.leah1": "Did Maple just try to eat bug meat?$s",
  "daulton.saloon.elliott1": "A most peculiar dietary preference indeed.$h",

  // Mini Beach Event //
  "daulton.fall.abovehead": "Elliott...",
  "daulton.fall.hammer": "That's not how a hammer works, man.",
  "daulton.fall.01": "Ah! The cruel irony of inanimate objects conspiring against artistic endeavor!$s",
  "daulton.fall.02": "Huh.",
  "daulton.fall.03": "@. Perfect timing.",
  "daulton.fall.04": "Dear farmer! You're just in time to witness my ongoing battle with these so-called tools...",
  "daulton.fall.05": "...which have clearly chosen betrayal over function.$s",
  "daulton.fall.06": "Elliott's been 'helping' for an hour. Haven't made much progress.$s",
  "daulton.fall.07": "Elliott. Hand me that.$5",
  "daulton.fall.08": "Go sit. You're better with words than wrenches.",
  "daulton.fall.09": "I only dropped the hammer twice. That’s progress, right?",
  "daulton.fall.10": "Behold! The rhythmic percussion of industry! Like waves against the shore, but with purpose!",
  "daulton.fall.11": "It's just a loose board, Elliott.$5",
  "daulton.fall.12": "You’d be surprised how much difference one board can make. Feels steadier already!$h",
  "daulton.fall.13": "Right.",
  "daulton.fall.14": "There. Fixed.",
  "daulton.fall.15": "Much better. It even feels sturdier underfoot.$h",
  "daulton.fall.16": "That's why I stick to fish. They don't need fixing.",
  "daulton.fall.17": "The sea herself must be weeping with joy. Or perhaps that’s just a leak I caused earlier...",
  "daulton.fall.ode": "Perhaps I shall immortalize this moment in verse! 'Ode to the Dock'.",
  "daulton.fall.18": "Don't.",
  "daulton.fall.19": "'When autumn's breeze kissed weathered wood, and steady hands made all things good—'",
  "daulton.fall.20": "Elliott.$5",
  "daulton.fall.21": "Yes, my friend?$h",
  "daulton.fall.22": "Stick to your cabin, bud. We've got this.",
  "daulton.fall.23": "Ah, but of course! I must withdraw before inspiration overtakes me. I’ve already rhymed ‘splinter’ with ‘winter’s glimmer’.",
  "daulton.fall.24": "Good lad. I was running out of ways to keep him from hurting himself.",
  "daulton.fall.25": "Guy means well. Just wasn't built for this kind of work.",
  "daulton.fall.question1": "He's trying his best. At least he wants to help.",
  "daulton.fall.question2": "He's pretty ridiculous. Does he always talk like that?",
  "daulton.fall.response1": "Yeah, you're right. He does try.$1",
  "daulton.fall.response2": "Just... maybe he shouldn't. Not with hammers. Or really any tools. Ever.$5",
  "daulton.fall.response3": "Ha. Yeah, he's something else.",
  "daulton.fall.response4": "He’s got his quirks, but his heart’s in the right place. Can’t knock that.$1",

  // Mini Lantern Event //
  "daulton.lantern.space": "Hold back a sec. He needs a bit o’ room.$3",
  "daulton.lantern.question1": "What's he doing?",
  "daulton.lantern.question2": "What's his problem?",
  "daulton.lantern.01": "He does this every year. Give em' some time.",
  "daulton.lantern.02": "Some things don't need explaining, friend.$s",
  "daulton.lantern.respect": "Y'don't always need to understand to show respect.",
  "daulton.lantern.hidden": " ",

  // Mini Mountain Event //
  "daulton.stormevent.01": "You hear something rustling near the trees ahead.",
  "daulton.stormevent.02": "It's Maple. She must've gotten caught in the storm.",
  "daulton.stormevent.03": "Her fur's soaked, and she looks scared. Should you take her somewhere safe?",
  "daulton.stormevent.question1": "Pick her up and go to the Saloon",
  "daulton.stormevent.question2": "Try to wait out the storm with her here",
  "daulton.stormevent.wait": "You need to get her out of here, even if it means carrying her through the rain.",
  "daulton.stormevent.04": "You poor thing! C'mere and dry off.",
  "daulton.stormevent.harvey": "Oh my! Is she alright?",
  "daulton.stormevent.05": "She's starting to calm down. Her ears have stopped twitching.",
  "daulton.stormevent.06": "She's here—? Thank Yoba...$7",
  "daulton.stormevent.07": "I've been looking everywhere. She wasn't in her usual forage spots.$7",
  "daulton.stormevent.08": "I’ve been scared outta my mind... and now she’s safe because of you. That’s not something I’ll forget.$7",
  "daulton.stormevent.09": "The storm rages on, but in here, things feel a little warmer.",
  "daulton.stormevent.end": "I should probably check that spot more often during storms. Just in case.",

  //MINI MARRIED EVENTS//
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.1": "Perfect timing, beautiful. I was just thinking this place could use some better company.",
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.2": "Water's incredible tonight. Almost as stunning as you walking in here.$4",
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.3": "Come here. These dock muscles aren't just for show.#$b#Perfect for holding you in the warm water.$4", 
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.4": "You know what I love about this place? It's just us. No Maple trying to steal your attention...$1",
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.5": "Mmm. Your skin tastes like minerals and starlight.$4",
  "Daulton.Bathhouse.6": "Think we could make this a regular thing? Private spa nights with my gorgeous spouse?$1",


  //GIFTS//

  "Daulton.Gift224": "Spaghetti? You're a lifesaver.$1#$b#Beats another night of Saloon snacks. Thanks.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift162":  "A lava eel? That's a serious catch.$1#$b#Willy's gonna be impressed when I tell him about this one.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift148": "An eel? Nice catch. This'll make a good meal after a long day.$1#$b#Willy always says fresh fish beats anything from a can.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift109": "An ancient sword? This thing's got some serious history.$1#$b#Maple would probably try to eat the handle if I'm not careful.$5",
  "Daulton.Gift691": "Barbed hook? Perfect. My old one's been slipping lately.$1#$b#Willy's gonna be jealous when he sees this setup.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift732": "Crab cakes? Fancy. You must think pretty highly of me.$1#$b#I'll try not to wolf these down too fast.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift215": "Pepper poppers? Now we're talking.$1#$b#Finally, something with some kick to it.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift151": "Squid? Now that's something you don't see every day.$1#$b#I wonder if Gus knows how to cook this properly.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift166":  "A treasure chest? Now we're talking.$1#$b#This is gonna buy Maple the good lettuce.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift260": "Hot peppers. Finally, something to make Gus's food more interesting.$0#$b#Guy keeps telling me I need to expand my palate.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift410": "Fresh blackberries? Sweet. I’ll snack on these while I work.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift206": "Pizza? You just became my favorite person today.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift534": "A ruby? You’re trying to impress me, aren't you?$1",
  "Daulton.Gift228": "Maki roll? That’s a nice change from my usual. Thanks.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift107": "A dinosaur egg... That’s one of the weirdest things I’ve ever been handed. I kinda love it.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift686": "A spinner? I’ve been meaning to replace mine. Good timing.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift692": "Lead bobber? That’ll save my line from snapping again. Thanks.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift233": "Ice cream? Sure. Who’s turning that down.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift400": "Strawberries? These smell amazing.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift444": "Duck feather? Looks like Maple would steal this before I even blink.$5",
  "Daulton.Gift351": "Muscle remedy? You trying to say I look sore?$1",
  "Daulton.Gift202": "Fried calamari? Reminds me of Zuzu street food. Nice surprise.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift167": "Joja Cola? Alright, guilty.#$b#It's bad for me but I still like it.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift531": "Aquamarine ring? That’s... unexpected. Looks good, though.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift635": "Orange? I’ll take something fresh over bar food any day.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift336": "Gold bar? Pretty generous. You sure about this?$0",
  "Daulton.Gift143": "Catfish? Good eating. Thanks for thinking of me.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift350": "Juice? Fresh fruit juice beats the processed stuff any day.$0#$b#Thanks for thinking of me.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift335": "Iron bar? Always good to keep around. Thanks.",
  "Daulton.Gift611": "Blackberry cobbler? You're making me look bad with cooking like this.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift408": "Hazelnut? Good for snacking while I work. Appreciate it.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift724": "Maple syrup? Okay, I’ll admit it.#$b#This one's going on everything I eat for a week.",
  "Daulton.Gift774": "Wild bait? This stuff works better than the regular kind.$1#$b#Good thinking.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift773": "Life elixir? Is this your way of saying I look tired?",
  "Daulton.Gift618": "Bruschetta? Classy. You've got good taste.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift64": "A ruby? That's... generous. You sure about this?$1#$b#I mean, I'll take it, but wow.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift211": "Pancakes? Now you're speaking my language. Breakfast wins again.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift395": "Coffee? You angel. That smell alone just saved my whole morning.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift610": "Fruit salad? Tastes like summer, minus the sunburn. Good stuff.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift716": "Crayfish? Not bad. I grew up on stuff like this. Just needs a little butter and patience.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift337": "Iridium bar? You must be doing well. I’ll put this to good use.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift728": "Fish stew? Perfect. This actually reminds me of something from back home.$1",
  "Daulton.Gift516": "A glow ring? Might come in handy when I trip over tools in the dark.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift530": "Topaz ring? Little flashy, but I’ll find a use for it.$0",
  

  "Daulton.Gift92": "Sap. Smells awful. Don’t take it personal.",
  "Daulton.Gift250": "Kale? Not a fan. Feels like I’m chewing weeds.",
  "Daulton.Gift478": "Rhubarb seeds? You’re assuming I know how to grow rhubarb. Bold of you.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift393": "Coral’s nice, but I trip over this stuff down by the dock all the time.",
  "Daulton.Gift772": "Oil of garlic? That stinks. Why would you even carry this around?$2",
  "Daulton.Gift118": "Glass shards? You okay, @?$2",
  "Daulton.Gift110": "A rusty spoon? Are you just cleaning out your pockets at this point?$2",
  "Daulton.Gift231": "Eggplant parmesan? You’d think cheese would save it, but it doesn’t.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift236": "Pumpkin soup? I never understood why people like this stuff.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift284": "Beets. Not even gonna pretend with this one. Hard no.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift307": "Duck mayo... Alright, now you're messing with me.",
  "Daulton.Gift103": "An ancient doll? Why does this feel cursed?",
  "Daulton.Gift684": "Bug meat? I... yeah. No thanks.",
  "Daulton.Gift346": "Beer? Too bitter. Never been into it.",
  "Daulton.Gift262": "Wheat? Unless you’re baking something with it, it’s just... wheat.",
  "Daulton.Gift423": "Plain rice. You really know how to spice up a guy’s day... with nothing at all.",
  "Daulton.Gift614": "Green tea? I’ve tried to like it. I really have.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift222": "Rhubarb pie? I know people love it, but I just don’t get the appeal.",
  "Daulton.Gift399": "Spring onions? These things go bad in like five seconds, don’t they?$0",
  "Daulton.Gift305": "Void egg? It's warm and unsettling. I’m not sure how I feel about it.$0",
  "Daulton.Gift439": "Purple slime egg? Nope. Not raising anything with teeth and a mood problem.$2", 
  "Daulton.Gift84": "Frozen tear? This thing makes me cold just looking at it. Hard pass.$2",
  "Daulton.Gift259": "Fiddlehead fern? I don't eat random plants from the forest.$4",
  "Daulton.Gift208": "Glazed yams? Yams are bad enough without making them sticky.$4",


  "gifts.Daulton.love": "This is absolutely incredible. Thank you!$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.like": "You're giving this to me? This is great! Thank you, @.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike": "Oh... For me? This is...nice.",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate": "Uhh... I don't like this at all, @.$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral": "Thank you for the gift, @. I appreciate the gesture!$0",

  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.1": "This is absolutely incredible. Thank you!$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.2": "Seriously? For me? You're the best.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.3": "No way! I've been hoping for one of these.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.4": "Thanks, @. You always know just what I like.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.5": "How’d you know I needed this today?$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.6": "You're spoiling me, @. Not that I’m complaining.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.7": "I love it. Like, genuinely love it. Thanks.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.8": "This is... wow. I don’t even know what to say. Thank you.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.love.1.9":  "I wasn’t expecting this.#$b#But I’m really glad you thought of me.$1",

  "gifts.Daulton.like.1.1": "You're giving this to me? This is great! Thank you, @.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.like.1.2": "Not bad at all. I’ll make use of it.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.like.1.3": "Appreciate it. This’ll come in handy.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.like.1.4": "Appreciate it. You didn’t have to, but I’m glad you did.$1",
  "gifts.Daulton.like.1.5": "Hey, thanks. I’ll definitely get some use out of this.$1",

  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.1": "Oh... For me? This is...nice.",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.2": "Guess it’s the thought that counts, right?$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.3": "I don’t hate it, I just have no idea what I’d do with it.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.4": "You didn’t have to bring me something, you know...$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.5": "Eh... I probably won’t use this, but thanks anyway.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.6": "Well... it’s not the worst thing I’ve ever been handed.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.7": "You didn’t find this in your storage chest, did you?$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.dislike.1.8": "I’ll just... set this somewhere and think about it later.$2",

  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.1": "Uhh... I don't like this at all, @.$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.2": "Why would you think I’d want this?$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.3": "No offense, but I can’t stand this.$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.4": "I’d honestly rather you hadn’t given me anything at all.$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.5":  "Yikes. You sure this wasn’t meant for someone else?$2",
  "gifts.Daulton.hate.1.6": "Please don’t give me this again. Seriously.$6",

  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.1": "Thank you for the gift, @. I appreciate the gesture!$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.2": "Huh. Sure, I’ll hang on to it.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.3": "Appreciate it. I guess it’s alright.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.4": "Can’t say I’m excited about it, but hey.#$b#Thanks.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.5": "Thanks. I’ll toss it in a drawer or something.$0",
  "gifts.Daulton.neutral.1.6": "Could be useful... maybe. I’ll figure it out.$0",


  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.1": "Whoa... is this what I think it is?$0#$b#This thing’s seen centuries. And you're just handing it to me?$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.2": "I can’t decide if I should display it or figure out how it sounds.$0#$b#Honestly? Might do both.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.3": "Part of me wants to restore it. Part of me wants to leave it untouched.$0#$b#Either way, it’s safe with me.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum4": "I’ve been around a lot of cheap knockoff drums...$0#$b#You spoil me.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.5": "This is the kind of gift that makes a guy fall in love all over again.$0#$b#Not that I ever stopped.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.6": "I could write a whole track around the way this drum resonates.$0#$b#Might even name the song after you.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.7": "I'll be gentle with it. Promise.$0#$b#Well, as gentle as you can be when you hit something for sound.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.8": "Thank you. I love this. Every time I look at it, I’ll remember today.$0#$b#And you. Mostly you.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.9": "I don’t know what you went through to get this, but...$0#$b#You’re unbelievable.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.10": "Thank you. This is the kind of gift you don’t forget.$0#$b#Not in a year, not in a decade.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.11": "An Ancient Drum? @, this is incredible... Look at the craftsmanship on this thing.$l#$b#I can already hear the rhythms this beauty could make. You really know how to make a guy feel appreciated.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.12": "An Ancient Drum? @, you're spoiling me here.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.13": "Holy... is this an actual Ancient Drum?$0#$b#The resonance chamber on this thing must be incredible. I can already imagine the deep, earthy tones it'll produce.Thanks for keeping my obsession well-fed, @.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.AncientDrum.14": "You found an Ancient Drum... I'm genuinely impressed, @.$1#$b#These don't just turn up anywhere. The craftsmanship is amazing. Look at these hand-carved details.$1.",

  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.1": "A rabbit's foot? Seriously, @?$5#$b#You know I have Maple, right? This is... this is messed up. I can't even look at this thing.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.2": "A rabbit's foot?$5#$b#Do you have any idea how wrong this feels? I've got a bunny at home who means the world to me. This isn't lucky...it's just sad.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.3": "I... wow. A rabbit's foot.$2#$b#@, you know how much Maple means to me. Seeing this just makes me think of... no. Just no. Please get this away from me.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.4": "A rabbit's foot... @, what were you thinking?$2#$b#This isn't just some random trinket to me. I look at this and all I can think about is my little guy at home.$5 I can't keep this.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.5": "A rabbit's foot... I can't believe you thought I'd want this.$5#$b#Every time I'd look at it, I'd think of Maple and what could happen to him. That's not luck...that's a nightmare.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.6": "You brought me a rabbit's foot? After everything I've told you about Maple?$2#$b#@, this feels like you don't know me at all. I can't accept something like this.$6",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.7": "I don't know what to say, @. A rabbit's foot?$2#$b#You've met Maple. You've seen how much I love that little bunny. This is just... wrong on every level. Please don't do this again.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.8": "A rabbit's foot for luck? The irony is killing me.$2#$b#The unluckiest thing that could happen to me is something happening to Maple.$5",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.9": "I honestly don't know what you were thinking, @.$5#$b#A rabbit's foot? When Maple is probably the most important thing in my life besides you? This hurts.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.10": "A rabbit's foot... I feel sick just looking at it.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.11": "A rabbit's foot... I need you to take this back.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.12": "No. Just... no, @.$5#$b#A rabbit's foot is the last thing I'd ever want.$2",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.13": "This is disturbing, @.$2#$b#I can't even pretend to be okay with this.$5",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.14": "I'm genuinely shocked right now.$2#$b#A rabbit's foot? What were you thinking?$5",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.rabbitsfoot.15": "A rabbit's foot... I'm speechless.$2#$b#And not in a good way, @.$5",  
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.1": "You pulled this thing out of *lava*?$0#$b#That's either love or a very weird afternoon.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.2": "Do you know how rare these are? This is incredible.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.3": "You caught a Lava Eel for me?$1#$b#@, this is the kind of fish fishermen dream about. Thank you.$1",

  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.4": "You brought me a Lava Eel?$1#$b#This thing's practically glowing. What an amazing catch, @.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.5": "A Lava Eel! This is like the holy grail of fishing.$1#$b#@, you know exactly how to make me happy.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.6": "You caught a Lava Eel... for me?$1#$b#@, this is beyond thoughtful. What a magnificent fish.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.7": "Is that heat coming from the fish?$1#$b#A Lava Eel... @, this is absolutely incredible.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.8": "Caught one of these once. Burned my glove and nearly my pride.$0#$b#Glad to see you had better luck.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.9": "Willy always said Lava Eels are the true test of a fisher’s nerve.$0#$b#Guess we’ve got our champion.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.10": "Should I be concerned this thing is still warm?$0#$b#...Nah. Let’s keep it.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.11": "You risked lava to bring me something wild and spiny.$0#$b#If that’s not romance, I don’t know what is.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.12": "Do I know how to cook it? Absolutely not.$0#$b#But I’ll stare at it proudly while we eat toast instead.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.13": "You bring home molten-lake monsters like it's no big deal.$0#$b#Pretty sure I’m the lucky one in this marriage.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.14": "A lava eel. For me.$0#$b#You know how to keep life interesting, sweetheart.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.LavaEel.15": "I'm torn between naming it something fierce or something ridiculous.$0#$b#Maybe 'Spicy Greg'.$1",

  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.1": "You brought me cake?$0#$b#You really do want me to fall for you all over again, huh?$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.2": "Chocolate cake? @, you're a lifesaver.$1#$b#You know I can barely boil water, let alone bake something this good.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.3": "A chocolate cake! This looks incredible.$1#$b#Way better than anything I could pull together, @.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.4": "Is this what being spoiled feels like?$0#$b#Because I’m not complaining.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.5": "Remind me again how I ended up married to someone this thoughtful?$0#$b#Not that I’m giving it back.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.6": "You made me chocolate cake?$1#$b#@, this is exactly what I needed. My sweet tooth thanks you.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.7": "A homemade chocolate cake?$1#$b#@, this beats Saloon food any day. You're amazing.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.8": "You're lucky I'm not a poet, or you'd be getting sonnets about frosting right now.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.9": "I’d offer to share... but I’d be lying.$0#$b#This one’s staying with me.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.10": "You brought me chocolate cake?$1#$b#@, this is perfect. I was just thinking about dessert.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.11": "A chocolate cake... this looks professional.$1#$b#@, you've got skills I definitely don't have.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.12": "Chocolate cake! This is a nice surprise.$1#$b#@, you know I can't resist anything chocolate.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.13": "You made this for me?$1#$b#A chocolate cake... @, this is so thoughtful. Thank you.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.14": "Chocolate cake... this looks amazing.$1#$b#@, you spoil me. This beats anything I could scrounge up.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.ChocolateCake.15": "A homemade chocolate cake?$1#$b#@, you know exactly what I like. This is wonderful.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.1": "Spaghetti! @, this smells just like my dad's.$4#$b#You have no idea how much this means to me. Thank you.$1",

  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.2": "Spaghetti! This is my weakness.$1#$b#@, you nailed it. Thank you.$4",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.3": "You made spaghetti for me?$4#$b#@, this is perfect.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.4": "Spaghetti... this is exactly what I needed.$1#$b#@, you got the sauce just right.$4",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.5": "Spaghetti! My absolute favorite.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.6": "Spaghetti... you know the way to my heart, @.Thank you.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.7": "You just keep finding ways to outdo yourself, huh?$0#$b#This smells like a perfect night in.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.8": "There’s something about a big plate of carbs that makes a guy feel deeply loved.$0#$b#Especially when he didn’t have to make it.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.9": "If you ever leave me, I’ll be the guy crying into cold noodles behind the Saloon.$0#$b#Just saying.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.10": "Willy saw me reheating a Saloon hot dog yesterday. Said it was ‘a cry for help.’$0#$b#Good timing on the spaghetti.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.11": "You could hand me this on a silver plate or a paper towel and I’d still be impressed.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.12": "I’ve eaten a lot of weird things off the docks.$0#$b#This is a very welcome upgrade.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.13": "I made spaghetti once. The smoke alarm still brings it up.$0#$b#I’ll leave it to the expert from now on.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.14": "I don’t know how you always know what I need, but you do.$0#$b#This? Exactly what today called for.$1",
  "Daulton.marriedgift.Spaghetti.15": "Every noodle’s a little reminder that I married up.$0#$b#Way, way up.$1",

  //MOVIES//

  "MovieInviteDaulton.1.1": "Yeah, I'd like that. It's been a while since I've been to the theater.$h",
  "MovieInviteDaulton.1.2": "Why not? Could be fun to get away from the docks for an evening.$h",
  "MovieInviteDaulton.1.3": "That's nice of you to ask. I'll come along.$h",
  "MovieInviteDaulton.1.4": "Yeah, alright. What time?$h",
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_Daulton.1": "Sounds perfect. I'll tell Maple not to wait up for us.$h",
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_Daulton.2": "You know I'd rather spend time with you than anyone else in this valley.$h",
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_Daulton.3": "Absolutely. Though knowing this town's selection, we might be in for an... experience.$h",
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_Daulton.5": "You know I can't say no to you... especially when you ask this nicely.$h",
  "MovieInvite_Spouse_Daulton.6": "You know the answer's always yes when it comes to spending time with you.$h",

